{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba '/Users/lchingen/.codex/skills/codex-claude-council/SKILL.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba '/Users/lchingen/.codex/skills/codex-claude-council/SKILL.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: codex-claude-council\n     3\tdescription: Run a multi-round research and challenge council between Codex and Claude Code on a specified objective, seeking evidence-backed agreement while preserving genuine disagreements. Use when the user requests a joint council, debate, or iterative co-review with Claude Code.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# Codex and Claude Code council\n     7\t\n     8\tClarify the objective, scope, constraints, evidence and decision needed from the request and workspace. Apply the repository's instructions and existing authorization; a council does not authorize unrelated changes or override a user's decisions. State what each reviewer must leave out of scope.\n     9\t\n    10\t## Independent investigation\n    11\t\n    12\t- Codex investigates the primary sources, code and relevant prior decisions itself. Give Claude Code the same objective, scope and primary materials, but avoid supplying a preferred conclusion in its initial assignment where independence matters. Ask it to cite exact files and concrete evidence, distinguish facts from hypotheses, and propose the cheapest decisive checks and counterexamples.\n    13\t- Run Claude Code with the model the user chose or, if none, an available appropriate model. For read-only review restrict tools to `Read,Glob,Grep` and a read-only permission mode. Preserve the exact handoff, session ID, streaming output and terminal result in the task's work area. Never bypass permissions.\n    14\t- A typical local invocation is `claude -p --model <model> --permission-mode plan --tools Read,Glob,Grep --output-format stream-json --verbose < handoff.txt > round-1.jsonl 2> round-1.stderr`. Validate installed CLI options first. Continue the same session using `--resume <session-id>` with the next challenge. Check final result and exit status; tool activity or a partial stream is not completion. Poll the running process and surface meaningful progress; do not kill a working reviewer merely because it is taking minutes. Report actual failures or access limitations accurately.\n    15\t\n    16\t## Challenge and converge\n    17\t\n    18\tCompare independent findings against the underlying material yourself before presenting them as established. Send Claude the specific disagreements, counterexamples and your own analysis, and ask it to challenge its prior conclusions as well as yours. Repeat until each material claim and proposed next step is explicitly agreed with its supporting evidence, or the remaining uncertainty or disagreement is identified. Agreement is not proof: identify what would falsify the shared hypothesis and which claims remain untested. Do not force consensus or invent a reviewer response.\n    19\t\n    20\tKeep rounds proportionate and purposeful. A reviewer who is still investigating should be allowed to finish. If meaningful progress stops because of an actual failure or impasse, preserve the trace and tell the user what remains unresolved.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Deliver\n    23\t\n    24\tGive the user the conclusion in plain language, concrete source examples, agreed causes versus hypotheses, unresolved disagreements, priority and the next discriminating test. Preserve the exchange and a concise decision record where the task's existing documentation belongs. Update dependent human-readable views when the workspace requires it. Implement changes only within the user's authorized scope and after the applicable project diagnosis and review requirements; do not change frozen baselines or treat the council's agreement as approval for a new product decision.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
