hingen  wheel       224 Nov 22 19:19 small-rehearsal-3\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 lchingen  wheel       224 Nov 22 19:20 small-rehearsal-4\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 lchingen  wheel       224 Nov 22 19:42 small-rehearsal-5\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel       759 Nov 20 17:10 snip.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 23 02:11 split-check\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  wheel        96 Nov 21 08:00 split-sim\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 16 02:48 stage-b-mutants-024615\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 16 02:51 stage-b-mutants-b-024858\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 16 03:00 stage-b-mutants-c-025753\ndrwxr-xr-x@  10 lchingen  wheel       320 Nov 23 08:00 step2-lines\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 16 12:26 stopstate\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 21 08:00 stopstate2\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  staff       128 Nov 21 17:39 stray-help-replay\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel  18624512 Nov 21 17:29 t1-control-views.sqlite\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel     20348 Nov 22 00:33 targets-context-2.txt\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel     35015 Nov 22 00:31 targets-context.txt\ndrwx------@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 20 08:00 tmp1opwqnic\ndrwx------@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 16 12:37 tmp_xdgu3b2\ndrwx------@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 20 08:00 tmph97ppigx\ndrwx------@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 20 08:00 tmpksgmtfhe\ndrwx------@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 20 08:00 tmpwu2h3d_1\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  wheel        96 Nov 16 02:54 u1-look-025437\ndrwxr-xr-x@   8 lchingen  wheel       256 Nov 22 14:30 v13-rehearsal-1\ndrwxr-xr-x@  14 lchingen  wheel       448 Nov 22 14:30 v13-rehearsal-2\ndrwxr-xr-x@  20 lchingen  wheel       640 Nov 22 14:36 v13-rehearsal-3\ndrwxr-xr-x@  24 lchingen  wheel       768 Nov 22 14:37 v13-rehearsal-4\ndrwxr-xr-x@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 21 08:00 walprobe\ndrwxr-xr-x@   2 lchingen  wheel        64 Nov 21 08:00 walprobe2\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  wheel        96 Nov 21 01:33 window-attempt2\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel   1036088 Nov 22 10:35 wp-candidates.txt\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel     88171 Nov 22 10:35 wp-narrow.txt\n     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 10, for council round 74j. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\n     4\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\n     5\t\n     6\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\n     7\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\n     8\t- a missing source item is refused;\n     9\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\n    10\t- the manifest is a closed set;\n    11\t- the bound is validated as a date;\n    12\t- narrow reads;\n    13\t- size and speed budgets;\n    14\t- tests that separate every branch;\n    15\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\n    16\t- no idea submission.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\n    19\t\n    20\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\n    21\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\n    22\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\n    23\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\n    24\t- The staging folder has one owner.\n    25\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\n    26\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\n    27\t\n    28\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\n    29\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\n    30\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\n    31\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\n    32\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\n    33\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\n    34\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\n    35\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\n    38\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\n    39\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\n    40\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\n    41\t\n    42\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\n    43\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\n    44\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\n    45\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\n    46\t  pause.\n    47\t\n    48\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\n    49\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\n    50\t  but the stores compare days as text.\n    51\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\n    52\t\n    53\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\n    54\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\n    55\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\n    56\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\n    57\t  anything exists there.\n    58\t\n    59\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\n    60\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\n    61\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\n    62\t\n    63\t**Revision 9 answers `codex-r74h.md`.**\n    64\t- A report is published the moment its link succeeds. A later failure to remove the temporary file is reported as published, naming\n    65\t  the leftover file.\n    66\t- `check`'s exit statuses are explicit, and the end-to-end tests assert them.\n    67\t\n    68\t**Revision 10 answers `codex-r74i.md`:** `check` follows the build's rule. Any failure to publish the report before the link succeeds\n    69\t(the name occupied, or the temporary file not created or written, such as `EACCES`) is exit 2 after the printed pass.\n    70\t\n    71\t## 0. Scope\n    72\t\n    73\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\n    74\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\n    75\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\n    76\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\n    77\t  - tests and mutants;\n    78\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\n    79\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\n    80\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n    81\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n    82\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\n    83\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\n    84\t- **Not in scope:**\n    85\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\n    86\t  - colleagues' page;\n    87\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\n    88\t  - any model call;\n    89\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\n    90\t\n 10076\t   }\n 10077\t  }\n 10078\t },\n 10079\t \"decisive\": {\n 10080\t  \"kept\": {\n 10081\t   \"e1865\": {\n 10082\t    \"questions\": [\n 10083\t     \"v4\",\n 10084\t     \"v5\",\n 10085\t     \"v8\"\n 10086\t    ],\n 10087\t    \"equal_to_store\": true\n 10088\t   },\n 10089\t   \"e2295\": {\n 10090\t    \"questions\": [\n 10091\t     \"v8\"\n 10092\t    ],\n 10093\t    \"equal_to_store\": true\n 10094\t   },\n 10095\t   \"e3597\": {\n 10096\t    \"questions\": [\n 10097\t     \"v4\",\n 10098\t     \"v5\"\n 10099\t    ],\n 10100\t    \"equal_to_store\": true\n 10101\t   }\n 10102\t  },\n 10103\t  \"implied_outcome_j1580\": \"About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-reven\",\n 10104\t  \"substituted_into_e2295_refused\": \"question v8.evidence[529].one_line: differs from the store\",\n 10105\t  \"added_to_manifest_refused\": \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\",\n 10106\t  \"unchanged_package_passes\": 91055\n 10107\t },\n 10108\t \"old-1/v8\": {\n 10109\t  \"class\": \"number\",\n 10110\t  \"forecast\": \"Forecast unavailable\",\n 10111\t  \"evidence\": 1284,\n 10112\t  \"same_ids_as_service_evidence\": true\n 10113\t },\n 10114\t \"leaks\": {\n 10115\t  \"old-3/v36@2026-08-25\": {\n 10116\t   \"latest_judgement\": 799,\n 10117\t   \"expected_judgement\": 799,\n 10118\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 10119\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 10120\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 10121\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 10122\t   \"around_1_trillion_fields\": []\n 10123\t  },\n 10124\t  \"old-1/v10@2026-08-28\": {\n 10125\t   \"latest_judgement\": 865,\n 10126\t   \"expected_judgement\": 865,\n 10127\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 10128\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 10129\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 10130\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 10131\t   \"around_1_trillion_fields\": []\n 10132\t  }\n 10133\t },\n 10134\t \"control\": {\n 10135\t  \"id\": \"v3\",\n 10136\t  \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 10137\t  \"label_equals_store\": true,\n 10138\t  \"evidence_equals_store\": true\n 10139\t },\n 10140\t \"closing\": {\n 10141\t  \"reason\": \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\",\n 10142\t  \"bundle_exposes_reason\": true,\n 10143\t  \"package_open\": false,\n 10144\t  \"reason_absent\": true,\n 10145\t  \"rung_label_in_v8_fields\": []\n 10146\t }\n 10147\t}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"which -a python3; ls /opt/homebrew/bin/python*; rg -n 'diagnostic|every.*string|condition|text field|nullable|clock|j865|band text' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{codex-r74*,claude-r74*,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md} | head -110; rg -n 'def open_read_only|def .*key\\\\(|store_key\\\\(|insert_view_key\\\\(' src/hivemind/views/store.py src/hivemind | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"which -a python3; ls /opt/homebrew/bin/python*; rg -n 'diagnostic|every.*string|condition|text field|nullable|clock|j865|band text' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{codex-r74*,claude-r74*,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md} | head -110; rg -n 'def open_read_only|def .*key\\\\(|store_key\\\\(|insert_view_key\\\\(' src/hivemind/views/store.py src/hivemind | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/.pyenv/shims/python3\n/usr/bin/python3\n/opt/homebrew/bin/python-build\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:7:1. **The pass condition becomes an origin check, not a string sweep.** Every package field is compared with its permitted stored source\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:9:   `e2295`'s summary then fails, because the summary no longer equals the stored one. The string search stays as a diagnostic on\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:22:   - fixtures that separate every branch, with a condition-only resolved number, unresolved numbers with and without a key, the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:7:| Origin check and decisive case | **The decisive case is resolved.** I verified the three genuine records in `old-1`. `e2295` quotes Morningstar’s $361 billion, `e1865` contains “Bullish confirmation,” and `e3597` quotes analysts’ $390 billion. The design keeps all three, rejects j1580 substituted into `e2295`, and rejects the same text added as a manifest field. The string search is now diagnostic. The broader origin check remains incomplete as described below. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:269](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:269) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:12:The four scope choices are carried through. The first package omits `object`, `kind` and groups. Idea submission is deferred, its acceptance remains pending, and there is no minimum length for diagnostic matches. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:28) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:51) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:290](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:290)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:24:1. **Derive the expected date, class and records independently.** During build, compare the packaged date with the requested or resolved day. During `check`, pass the package date through the store’s completed-day check. I verified that `old-1` ends September 20 and has no later processing or judgement rows, so merely comparing its contents at September 21 detects nothing. Derive each question’s class from the stored measure and labels before selecting its permitted fields. Compare record counts as well as IDs, since a set comparison accepts a duplicate question or evidence record. These checks belong in the pass condition for each package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:172) · [service.py:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:57)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:28:5. **Make the four-store acceptance runnable.** Step 7 asks for `judgements.implied_outcome` and `reference` on every store. I checked the served ledger’s actual schema. It has neither column. Read the available diagnostic columns and report the two as absent on that ledger. Otherwise the specified acceptance can fail on a valid package before it finishes. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:261) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) · [store.py:152](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:152)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:1:**Verdict: not ready to build.** The proposed check would accept Hivemind’s own forecast inside an allowed text field. It would also flag genuine source material. Both failures are reproducible on `old-1/v8`: the check misses the stored forecast of about **$390 billion**, while a source quote legitimately contains the withheld label **“Bullish.”** [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [Evidence returned to the exporter:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:232)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:24:| Value × reader and old checks | **The named helpers do more than the table says.** `state_as_of` reads all judgement columns and decodes theme pushes. `rungs_of` reads conditions and bounds. Use a narrow label/position read for the package if the “never read” promise stands. Also unpack `ladder_bands` in the report: failure returns **`(None, reason)`**. Testing the whole return value for `None` silently misses unresolved questions. [Build claims:125](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:125) · [Judgement reader:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:129) · [Rung reader:97](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:97) · [Band result:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:34:- **Tests 8–10** have useful controls for evidence dates, foreign files and changed bytes. Add an unchanged-data-hash mutant with extra manifest prose. For the two known event leaks, export at **August 25** for `old-3/v36/j799` and **August 28** for `old-1/v10/j865`. I verified those are the last judgements on those dates. The default September 20 exports select **j1698** and **j1581**, so absence of the older prose there proves little. Assert the original answer label as well as the absence of the forecast. [Tests:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [Stored leak dates:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md:1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:40:I also checked the opposite error in memory. The **entire** `old-1/v8/j1580.implied_outcome`, beginning “About $390 billion,” contains **zero** of §7’s searched strings of 12 or more characters. The restatement “Our estimate for the year is $390bn” also produces zero. The sweep omits `implied_outcome`, `reference`, numeric bounds and structured judgement values. Searching serialized JSON also changes how quotation marks and newlines appear. Use exact matches on **decoded fields** as diagnostics, including short labels. Make the pass condition an independent comparison of package fields with their permitted source values at the requested date. Preserve the genuine $390 billion article quote in `old-1/e3597` as the control. [Stored judgement fields:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:18) · [Proposed sweep:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:201)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:49:| Sweep floor | **Remove it as a safety criterion.** Keep diagnostic hits attributable to a particular question, field and source. [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:25:- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:54:  - no band, label or condition;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:75:Every other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:111:  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,164p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 9, for council round 74i. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\\n    43\\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\\n    44\\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\\n    45\\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\\n    46\\t  pause.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\\n    49\\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\\n    50\\t  but the stores compare days as text.\\n    51\\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\\n    54\\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\\n    55\\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\\n    56\\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\\n    57\\t  anything exists there.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\\n    60\\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\\n    61\\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t**Revision 9 answers `codex-r74h.md`.**\\n    64\\t- A report is published the moment its link succeeds. A later failure to remove the temporary file is reported as published, naming\\n    65\\t  the leftover file.\\n    66\\t- `check`'s exit statuses are explicit, and the end-to-end tests assert them.\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t## 0. Scope\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    71\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    72\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    73\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    74\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    75\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    76\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    77\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    78\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    79\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    80\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    81\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    82\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    83\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    84\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    85\\t  - any model call;\\n    86\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t## 1. What is built\\n    89\\t\\n    90\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t- **Constants:**\\n    93\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    94\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    95\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    96\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    97\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n   100\\t  |---|---|\\n   101\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n   102\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n   103\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n   104\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n   105\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n   106\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n   109\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n   110\\t    only when the table exists;\\n   111\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n   112\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n   113\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n   114\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   115\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   116\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   117\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   118\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   119\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   120\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   121\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   122\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   123\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   124\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   125\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   126\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   127\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   128\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   129\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   130\\t  - Value checks:\\n   131\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   132\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   133\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   134\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   135\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   136\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   137\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   138\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   139\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   140\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   141\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   142\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   143\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   144\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   145\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   146\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   147\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   148\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   149\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   152\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   153\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   154\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   155\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   156\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   157\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   158\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   159\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   160\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   161\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   164\\t  compared.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '165,330p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   165\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   166\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   167\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   168\\t  else.\\n   169\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   170\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   171\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   172\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   173\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   176\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   177\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   178\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   179\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   180\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   181\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   182\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   183\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   184\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   185\\t\\n   186\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   187\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   188\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   189\\t     guarantee;\\n   190\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   191\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   192\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   193\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   194\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   195\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   196\\t     nothing;\\n   197\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   198\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   199\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   200\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   203\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   204\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   205\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   206\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   207\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   208\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   209\\t\\n   210\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   211\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   212\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   213\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   214\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   215\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\\n   216\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   217\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   218\\t- **The report:**\\n   219\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   220\\t  - counts per class;\\n   221\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   222\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   223\\t  - bytes;\\n   224\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   229\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   230\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   231\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   232\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   233\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   234\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   235\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   236\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   237\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   238\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   239\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   240\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   241\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   242\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   243\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   244\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   245\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   246\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   247\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   248\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   249\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   250\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   251\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   252\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   253\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   254\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   255\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   256\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   257\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   258\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   259\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   260\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   261\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   264\\t\\n   265\\tReaders of the package:\\n   266\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   267\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   268\\t- the tests.\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   273\\t|---|---|---|\\n   274\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   275\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   276\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   277\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   278\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   279\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   280\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   281\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   282\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   285\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   286\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   287\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   288\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   289\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   290\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   291\\t\\n   292\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   295\\t|---|---|\\n   296\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   297\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   298\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   299\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   300\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   301\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   302\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   303\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   304\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   309\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   310\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   311\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   312\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   313\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   314\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   315\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   316\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   321\\tits row above:\\n   322\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   323\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   324\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   325\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   326\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   327\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   328\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   329\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   330\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '331,500p'; cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   331\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   332\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   333\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   334\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   335\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   336\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   337\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   338\\t9. **Package:**\\n   339\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   340\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   341\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   342\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   343\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   344\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   345\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   346\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   347\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   348\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   349\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   350\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   351\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n   352\\t    - the build exits 0, and the package and its report exist;\\n   353\\t    - `check` with the build's report still in place prints a passing result and exits 2;\\n   354\\t    - after the test removes that report, `check` exits 0 and publishes a fresh one.\\n   355\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   356\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   357\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   358\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   359\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   360\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   361\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   362\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   363\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   364\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   365\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   366\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   367\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   368\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   369\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   370\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   371\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   372\\t      and inode).\\n   373\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   374\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   375\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\\n   376\\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\\n   377\\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   378\\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file\\n   379\\t    at the report name. The command exits 2 and the marker is unchanged. `check` then prints a passing result, exits 2, and leaves the\\n   380\\t    marker unchanged.\\n   381\\t20. **Temporary file left after the link** (a scratch copy in which removing the report's temporary file raises): the build exits 0\\n   382\\t    and says the report is published, naming the leftover temporary file. The report exists and equals the build's report.\\n   383\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   384\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   385\\t15. **Files:**\\n   386\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   387\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   388\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   389\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   390\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   391\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   392\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   393\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   394\\t\\n   395\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   396\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   397\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   398\\t- the event test removed;\\n   399\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   400\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   401\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   402\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   403\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   404\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   405\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   406\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   407\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   408\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   409\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   410\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   411\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   412\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   413\\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\\n   414\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   415\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   416\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   417\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   418\\t\\n   419\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   420\\t\\n   421\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   422\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   423\\t\\n   424\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   425\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   426\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   427\\t\\n   428\\tThe steps:\\n   429\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   430\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   431\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   432\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   433\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   434\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   435\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   436\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   437\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   438\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   439\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   440\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   441\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   442\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   443\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   444\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   445\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   446\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   447\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   448\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   449\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   450\\t\\n   451\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   452\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   453\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   454\\t\\n   455\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   456\\t\\n   457\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   458\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   459\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   460\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   461\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   462\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   463\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   464\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   465\\t  judged position.\\n   466\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   467\\t  reproduces.\\n   468\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   469\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   470\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   471\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   472\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   473\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   474\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   475\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n\\n**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n\\nOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n\\n**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\ncould reach a reader:\\n- the idea card;\\n- the closing text;\\n- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n- a translated export;\\n- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n\\nA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\nstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n\\n## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n\\nThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n\\n  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n\\n## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n\\n- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n  - no live POC service;\\n  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n\\n  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n  - the question and its id;\\n  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n\\n  Nothing else is listed:\\n  - no ladder;\\n  - no band, label or condition;\\n  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n  delivered card.\\n- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n  later choice for Alex.\\n\\n## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n\\nA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n\\nEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n\\nCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n\\nNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n\\n**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\nbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\nevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n\\n## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n\\nD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\nallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n  readers would see.\\n- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n  `why_changed`.\\n- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n\\n## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n\\n- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n  - an event question;\\n  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n  - a real closing switch;\\n  - an idea.\\n- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n- **Mutants:**\\n  - an extra field;\\n  - a fetch left on;\\n  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n\\n  Each must fail.\\n- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n    prose rule.\\n- **The $0 release check.**\\n  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n    final band there.\\n  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n\\n## 6. Not in scope\\n\\n- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n- The closed v13s line.\\n- Other open defects.\\n- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{RELEASE-BUILD,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN}.md; head -65 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\\\"'^#{1,3} .*D(726|756|757|758)'\\\"\\\\\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\n    1232 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\\n     475 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\\n     147 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\n    2055 total\\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n\\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n\\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n\\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n\\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n   word for it is already given.\\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n\\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n\\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\nany one step's own score.\\n\\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n\\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n\\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n\\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n\\n**Evidence:**\\n\\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n\\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n\\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" into the first release\\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '151,351p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   151\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   152\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   153\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   154\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   155\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   156\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   157\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   158\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   159\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   160\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   161\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   164\\t  compared.\\n   165\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   166\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   167\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   168\\t  else.\\n   169\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   170\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   171\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   172\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   173\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   176\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   177\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   178\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   179\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   180\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   181\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   182\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   183\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   184\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   185\\t\\n   186\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   187\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   188\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   189\\t     guarantee;\\n   190\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   191\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   192\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   193\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   194\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   195\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   196\\t     nothing;\\n   197\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   198\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   199\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   200\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   203\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   204\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   205\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   206\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   207\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   208\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   209\\t\\n   210\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   211\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   212\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   213\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   214\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   215\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\\n   216\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   217\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   218\\t- **The report:**\\n   219\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   220\\t  - counts per class;\\n   221\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   222\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   223\\t  - bytes;\\n   224\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   229\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   230\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   231\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   232\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   233\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   234\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   235\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   236\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   237\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   238\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   239\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   240\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   241\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   242\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   243\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   244\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   245\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   246\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   247\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   248\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   249\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   250\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   251\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   252\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   253\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   254\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   255\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   256\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   257\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   258\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   259\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   260\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   261\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   264\\t\\n   265\\tReaders of the package:\\n   266\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   267\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   268\\t- the tests.\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   273\\t|---|---|---|\\n   274\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   275\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   276\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   277\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   278\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   279\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   280\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   281\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   282\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   285\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   286\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   287\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   288\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   289\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   290\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   291\\t\\n   292\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   295\\t|---|---|\\n   296\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   297\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   298\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   299\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   300\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   301\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   302\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   303\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   304\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   309\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   310\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   311\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   312\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   313\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   314\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   315\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   316\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   321\\tits row above:\\n   322\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   323\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   324\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   325\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   326\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   327\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   328\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   329\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   330\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   331\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   332\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   333\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   334\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   335\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   336\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   337\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   338\\t9. **Package:**\\n   339\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   340\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   341\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   342\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   343\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   344\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   345\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   346\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   347\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   348\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   349\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   350\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   351\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '10991,11009p;11823,11905p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; tail -4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; tail -n +66 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n\\n- **The questions** (after D725):\\n  - \\\"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\\\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\\n  - \\\"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\\\" Options: 同意\\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \\\"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\\\"; \\\"同意 (推荐)\\\".\\n- **Decided (Alex):**\\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\\n    ceiling.\\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\": the band, the\\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\\n\\n## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\\n\\n## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n\\n- **The question** (after D755): \\\"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\\\"\\n  - Options:\\n    - \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\": the council's consensus;\\n    - \\\"换更强的模型再小测一次\\\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\\n    - \\\"先停，我想谈谈\\\".\\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\".\\n- **Decided (Alex):**\\n  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\\n  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", the band, the\\n    forecast text and the history withheld together.\\n  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\\n    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" appear.\\n- **Kept for the record, not built:**\\n  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\\n  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\\n  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\\n\\n## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n\\n- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \\\"Forecast\\n  unavailable\\\" (D756). D726 says it \\\"is built with the release work, which is not started\\\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\\n  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\\n- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\\n  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\\n  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\\n- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\\n  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\\n  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\";\\n  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\\n  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\\n    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\\n  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\\n  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\\n    approach with one structural rule.\\n- **Open for Alex:**\\n  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\\n  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\\n     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\\n     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\\n       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\\n- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\\n\\n## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n\\n- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \\\"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\\n  Production 方向去走了\\\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \\\"同意\\\"; D756 \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\"). D757 left two\\n  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\\n- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\\n  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\\n     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\\n     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \\\"not started\\\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\\n  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\\n     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\\n     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\\n  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\\n     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\\n  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\\n     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\\n- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\\\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\\\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\\\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\\\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\\\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\\\"自己的量，别的期间\\\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"跑验收\\\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\\\"中国份额归零\\\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"都做\\\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\\n| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n\\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n\\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n  system (D263).\\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n  competition or pricing\\\".\\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n  of the previous filing topic).\\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n\\n## 5. What to do\\n\\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n\\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n     the existing rule).\\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n\\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n\\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n  measured and reported apart.\\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n  counted after.\\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n    question\\\";\\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n    or no question uses);\\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n    ones that matter one by one.\\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n      facts must not fall.\\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n      what was measured.\\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n\\n## 7. Process (no drift)\\n\\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n  sentence, in both directions.\\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n\\n## 8. Steps and where we are\\n\\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n\\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n\\n- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '49,153p;204,268p;480,527p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '10,45p;220,256p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   146\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\\n   147\\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\\n   148\\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   150\\t    out = []\\n   151\\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\\n   152\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   153\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   204\\t        return None\\n   205\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   206\\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   207\\t    if state:\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   480\\t    if not found:\\n   481\\t        return None\\n   482\\t    if lo > hi or (lo == hi and not (lo_inc and hi_inc)):\\n   483\\t        return None\\n   484\\t    return (lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc)\\n   485\\t\\n   486\\t\\n   487\\tdef numeric_bands(rungs):\\n   488\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bands from the rungs' own numeric bounds (keyed views): lower bound inclusive, upper exclusive, the two ends open;\\n   489\\t    None when a rung has no bounds.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   490\\t    if not rungs or any(r.get('lo') is None and r.get('hi') is None for r in rungs):\\n   491\\t        return None\\n   492\\t    out = {}\\n   493\\t    for r in rungs:\\n   494\\t        lo = -INF if r.get('lo') is None else float(r['lo']); hi = INF if r.get('hi') is None else float(r['hi'])\\n   495\\t        out[r['position']] = (lo, True, hi, False)\\n   496\\t    return out\\n   497\\t\\n   498\\t\\n   499\\tdef ladder_bands(rungs):\\n   500\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every rung's band, or None with the reason when the ladder is not one unbroken partition by amount. Rungs that\\n   501\\t    carry numeric bounds are read from them; the prose parser serves the views written before keys.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   502\\t    numeric = numeric_bands(rungs)\\n   503\\t    if numeric is not None:\\n   504\\t        ordered = sorted(numeric.items(), key=lambda pb: pb[1][0])\\n   505\\t        for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   506\\t            if a[2] != b[0]:\\n   507\\t                return None, f'numeric bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   508\\t        return numeric, None\\n   509\\t    bands = [(r['position'], band(r['condition'])) for r in rungs]\\n   510\\t    unreadable = [p for p, b in bands if b is None]\\n   511\\t    if unreadable:\\n   512\\t        return None, f'conditions not read as amounts: positions {unreadable}'\\n   513\\t    ordered = sorted(bands, key=lambda pb: (pb[1][0], pb[1][2]))\\n   514\\t    for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   515\\t        if a[2] != b[0] or a[3] == b[1]:          # adjacent bands share the boundary amount and exactly one of them owns it\\n   516\\t            return None, f'bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   517\\t    lowest, highest = ordered[0][1], ordered[-1][1]\\n   518\\t    if not (lowest[0] == -INF or (lowest[0] == 0 and lowest[1])) or highest[2] != INF:     # an amount that cannot be negative may start at 0\\n   519\\t        return None, 'the ladder does not cover the line up to +inf'\\n   520\\t    return dict(bands), None\\n   521\\t\\n   522\\t\\n   523\\tdef _contains(b, yi):\\n   524\\t    lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc = b\\n   525\\t    return (lo < yi or (lo == yi and lo_inc)) and (yi < hi or (yi == hi and hi_inc))\\n   526\\t\\n   527\\t\\n    10\\tfrom .views import store\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t@contextmanager\\n    14\\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\\n    15\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    16\\t    owned = []\\n    17\\t    try:\\n    18\\t        for conn in connections:\\n    19\\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\\n    20\\t                conn.execute('begin')\\n    21\\t                owned.append(conn)\\n    22\\t        yield\\n    23\\t    finally:\\n    24\\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\\n    25\\t            conn.rollback()\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\\n    30\\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    31\\t    cache = {}\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def item_of(input_id):\\n    34\\t        if input_id not in cache:\\n    35\\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\\n    36\\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\\n    37\\t        return cache[input_id]\\n    38\\t    return item_of\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\\n    42\\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\\n   220\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   221\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   222\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   228\\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\\n   229\\t        if not as_of:\\n   230\\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\\n   231\\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   232\\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\\n   233\\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\\n   234\\t        if not view_ids:\\n   235\\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\\n   236\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'sealed|poc/data/.+sqlite|served' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{codex-r74,claude-r74b,claude-r74c,codex-r72}.md; rg --files --hidden --no-ignore poc | rg 'items-comparison.sqlite\\\"'$|views.sqlite$'\\\"' | head -80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"rg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74b.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\nrg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74c.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md:10:   **The proposed number-question rule fits the three comparison stores but fails on supported data.** I counted numeric bounds on 19/47, 17/43 and 18/49 questions in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`. On the sealed ledger used by the service tests, Data Center revenue `v3` has no `lo` or `hi` columns at all. Yet `evaluate(v3, >= $300B)` returned `holds` and the judged $300–350B range. The reverse case also exists. Stored Xbox question `v37` has explicit **Yes/No** answers with numeric bounds around zero. The current opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. Define identity by the kind of answer the question asks for, cover both stored examples, and specify what the release does when an older record is ambiguous. The existing helper for linking questions has a narrower, asset-only purpose. [tests/test_service.py:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:18) · [tests/test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [stored Xbox ledger:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [links.py:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:144)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-parallel-r4/serial/views.sqlite\\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-parallel-r4/parallel/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/old-2026-10-23-run3a/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-groups-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v33-nvda-week-2026-10-27/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-seed2-d3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-dev14-d2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v29-theme-r5-2026-10-26/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2/judge/draw-new-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/review-v118-old2-0920-2026-11-20/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-dev14-d3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/old-2026-10-23-run1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v36-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-3/judge/draw-new-3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v35-nvda-2w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v26-collision-r4-2026-10-26/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-d1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-seed-d3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-clean-d3/judged/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-new/judge/draw-s-new/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-clean-d3/judged-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-seed2-d2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-slice-2026-11-13/sp1/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/linked-1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/control-1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-slice-2026-11-13/s1/judge/draw-s1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-clean-d2/judged/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-2026-10-25/aborted-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-2026-10-25/aborted-1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-old/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v83-seedv2-d2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-proof/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/page-store-2026-11-16/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-proof/reference-code-replay/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/control/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/c1/judge/draw-c1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/census-replay-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-d2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-d4/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/remove-relation/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-clean-d1/judged/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/census-replay/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/remove-relation-keep-link/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v25-admission-2026-10-26/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-control-d3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v82-dev14-2026-10-31/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v83-seed-d1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v34c-nvda-week-2026-10-27/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v25-admission-r2-2026-10-26/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v69-seed-d2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/old-2026-10-23-run3b/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/pinned-shared-2026-10-27/arm-v29-shared/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-groups2-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-jev2-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0728/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/old-2026-10-23-run3c/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-q1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-r10-card-v109-2026-11-04/d1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-p3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/english-jev3-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21/control-3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-p2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21/linked-1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-q2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21/control-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/e2e-v83-seedv2-d1/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/slice/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21/linked-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/clean-e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/draw-q3/views.sqlite\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"cat poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/README.md; sed -n '1,110p' src/hivemind/views/store.py; cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74{e,f,g}.md | head -46\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Served copy of the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger, minus v68\\n\\n`views.sqlite` = `sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` with thesis v68 removed (Alex, 2026-10-28 17:05:\\n\\\"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\\\"). v68, \\\"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\\\", was opened on the\\nrun's last day by the succession rule (same quantity, next period, after v24) and the writer linked its one opening statement to\\nv7 and v24 instead of to it, so it stood with no evidence and no judgement. Rows removed: views, view_keys, rungs, successions,\\nview_switches, views_fts for v68 (no evidence_links or judgements existed). The sealed folder is untouched and remains the record;\\nthe front end, the API and the page build read this copy.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"The views database (docs/prd/06-views.md): append-only tables for views, rungs, judgements, evidence, links,\\nreplacements, dependencies, successions, match records, processing steps and the review pool; a trigram\\nfull-text index over the views for the matching lists; the queries the other modules read.\\n\\nEvery table refuses UPDATE and DELETE (triggers). Progress and counts are rows, never updates. There is no item\\ntext here: evidence holds the quoted sentence and the one-line restatement only.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport re\\nimport sqlite3\\n\\nTABLES = {\\n    'views': 'view_id text primary key, object_id text, object_kind text, kind text, looks_at text, question text, due_day text, year text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text, created_at text',\\n    'rungs': 'view_id text, position integer, label text, condition text, lo real, hi real',\\n    'view_keys': 'view_id text primary key, measure text, scope text, scope_key text, period_start text, period_end text, basis text, unit text, event_type text, seq integer, scope_source text, key_version integer',\\n    'view_switches': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, open integer, reason text, by_whom text, after_seq integer',\\n    'judgements': 'judgement_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, rung integer, reasons text, cited_evidence_json text, cited_views_json text, pushes_json text, changed integer, why_changed text, config_checksum text, call_id integer, request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text, reference text, implied_outcome text',\\n    'evidence': 'evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\\n    'evidence_sources': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, input_id text, category text, publication_day text, location text, seq integer',\\n    'evidence_links': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, view_id text, seq integer',\\n    'replacements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',   # history: written before D202, read as before\\n    'revisions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',      # D202: the new piece revises the old; both stay in force\\n    'same_claims': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer',                    # D204: the matcher read the new piece as the same claim as the old; both stored, both in force\\n    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer, kind text default \\\\'\\\\'',   # kind: '' (a seed's or the generative matcher's row, read as before) or 'reads' (a chosen reading link, D694)\\n    'dependency_resolutions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer',\\n    'successions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer',\\n    'handovers': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text',\\n    'match_records': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text',\\n    'processing_steps': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text',\\n    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\\n    'late_statements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer',\\n    'days_completed': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text',\\n    # D694: how the links of an article were chosen (views/links.py), append-only per attempt: proposed, then committed or failed\\n    'link_selections': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, attempt_id text, seq integer, input_id text, config_checksum text, status text, record_json text',\\n    # D149 research groups: an ongoing business subject several distinct theses belong to; membership is decided by extraction and written with the thesis\\n    'thesis_groups': 'group_id text primary key, name text, scope text, aliases text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\\n    'thesis_group_members': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, basis text',\\n    # D166 (2026-11-01): the names a later declaration gives a stored group, appended once each; a group's aliases are its creation's plus these\\n    'thesis_group_aliases': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, alias text, seq integer, input_id text',\\n}\\n\\nINDEXES = [\\n    'create index if not exists views_object on views(object_id)',\\n    'create index if not exists judgements_view on judgements(view_id, judgement_id)',\\n    # 06-views step 7: a view is judged once per round (one item = one sequence number)\\n    'create unique index if not exists judgements_once_per_round on judgements(view_id, seq)',\\n    'create index if not exists links_view on evidence_links(view_id)',\\n    'create index if not exists links_evidence on evidence_links(evidence_id)',\\n    'create index if not exists sources_evidence on evidence_sources(evidence_id)',\\n    'create index if not exists steps_input on processing_steps(input_id, id)',\\n    'create index if not exists switches_view on view_switches(view_id, id)',\\n    'create index if not exists deps_view on dependencies(view_id)',\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef open_db(path):\\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\\n    for name, columns in TABLES.items():\\n        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({columns})')\\n        conn.execute(f\\\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\\\")\\n        conn.execute(f\\\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\\\")\\n    for statement in INDEXES:\\n        conn.execute(statement)\\n    ensure_writable_columns(conn)\\n    conn.execute(\\\"create virtual table if not exists views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\\\")\\n    conn.execute(\\\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\\\")\\n    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\\n    conn.commit()\\n    return conn\\n\\n\\ndef insert(conn, table, **fields):\\n    columns = list(fields)\\n    cursor = conn.execute(f'insert into {table} ({\\\",\\\".join(columns)}) values ({\\\",\\\".join(\\\"?\\\" * len(columns))})', [fields[c] for c in columns])\\n    return cursor.lastrowid\\n\\n\\n# ---------- views ----------\\n\\ndef create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\\n    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\\n           question=question, due_day=due_day, year=year, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id, created_at=created_at)\\n    for position, rung in enumerate(rungs, start=1):\\n        insert(conn, 'rungs', view_id=view_id, position=position, label=rung['label'], condition=rung['condition'], lo=rung.get('lo'), hi=rung.get('hi'))\\n    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\\n    conn.execute('insert into views_fts (view_id, text) values (?, ?)', (view_id, f'{object_id} {looks_at} {question}'))\\n\\n\\ndef view(conn, view_id):\\n    row = conn.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n    return dict(row) if row else None\\n\\n\\ndef rungs_of(conn, view_id):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The rungs with their bounds when the ledger has them (keyed views); a ledger written before keys has no lo/hi columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n    has_bounds = any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rows) or view_key(conn, view_id) is not None\\n    return [dict(position=r['position'], label=r['label'], condition=r['condition'],\\n                 **({'lo': r.get('lo'), 'hi': r.get('hi')} if has_bounds else {})) for r in rows]\\n\\n\\ndef add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's key (keyed-views-plan.md 2.1), written once with the view.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from .. import universe as _universe\\n    from .identity import is_shared\\n    scope_source = 'shared' if is_shared(key) else key.get('scope_source', 'model')      # D197: an aggregate's scope is wording\\n    insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id=view_id, measure=key['measure'], scope=key.get('scope', ''), scope_key=_universe.scope_key(key.get('scope', '')),\\n**Not ready to build.** Revision 5 closes both 74d defects at `--out`. Two issues remain. Test 14 checks the command’s exit status on the wrong path, and cleanup can delete a directory that reuses the staging name after publication.\\n\\n1. **Both 74d defects are closed in the design.** The only operation that creates `--out` is an atomic move that refuses an existing destination, including an empty directory. A database error before that move leaves only private staging to clean up. Test 17 specifies the missing-table error, exit 1, absence of both output and staging, and a successful retry at the same path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:171) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:329)\\n\\n2. **Test 14 still misses the command’s late refusal.** Its module test creates the foreign empty directory after staging. Its command test creates the directory before startup, so the early check can return exit 1 without ever reaching `publish` or staging cleanup. Run the real command on a scratch copy with a pause immediately before `publish`, create the empty directory, then resume. Assert exit 1, removal of the build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:161](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:161) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:212) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:326](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:326) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:328)\\n\\n3. **Revision 5 introduces a cleanup race at the old staging name.** Once `publish` succeeds, the rename frees that name. If another process creates a directory there before `finally` runs, the specified “if it still exists” check can remove the new directory. End the build’s cleanup responsibility as soon as the move succeeds. The decisive test recreates the old staging directory with a marker file after the move and verifies that the marker survives command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:167)**Not ready to build.** Revision 6 closes both 74e findings. Two other issues remain. A package dated August 25 can include September evidence, and writing the report can overwrite an input database.\\n\\n**1. Both 74e findings are closed in the design.**\\n\\n- **Late refusal.** Test 14 now pauses the real command immediately before `publish`, creates an empty `--out`, and resumes. It requires exit 1, removal of this build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory, verified by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:336](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:336)\\n- **Cleanup after publication.** The builder clears its staging path immediately after the move succeeds. Test 14 recreates the freed name with a marker file and requires the marker to survive command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339)\\n\\n**2. Two findings block the build.**\\n\\n- **The date must be normalized before comparison.** Python accepts `20260825` and `2026-08-25` as the same day. The design passes the original text to `resolve_bound`, and evidence visibility also compares dates as text. I reproduced the consequence on an in-memory copy of `old-1`, adding only a completed day in January 2027. For `v8`, `2026-08-25` returned 621 evidence records through August 25. `20260825` returned 1,284 through September 20. Parse an explicit date before calling `resolve_bound`, use its `YYYY-MM-DD` form for every query, and require that form in the package. Test that both command-line spellings produce the same evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:95) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:121](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:121) · [service.py:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:69) · [service.py:113](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:113)\\n- **The report can replace the ledger or items database.** For example, with `--out /work/release` and a valid SQLite input named `/work/release.report.json`, the build can read the input, verify and publish the package, then replace that database with JSON. The standalone `check` command rewrites the same path. Both commands should refuse a report destination that resolves to either input before writing anything. The decisive test is that each command refuses the collision and the input’s bytes remain intact. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:166) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:185)**Not ready to build.** Revision 7 closes the date finding. Two ways to overwrite a file remain in the report-writing steps.\\n\\n1. **74f date finding — closed.** The builder rejects `20260825` before querying the ledger. The package checker also requires `YYYY-MM-DD`. Test 16 places evidence on both sides of August 25 and checks that the canonical date exports only the earlier evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:116) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:359](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:359)\\n\\n2. **74f input-overwrite finding — still open in `check`.** On this Mac, I verified read-only that `old-1/prod/views.sqlite` and `old-1/prod/VIEWS.SQLITE` produce different `realpath` strings and identify the same file. An items database named `Release.report.json` can therefore pass the path comparison for `check release`, which then rewrites `release.report.json`. Compare the existing report’s file identity with both inputs using `os.path.samefile`. Extend test 18 on a case-insensitive volume to require refusal and an unchanged database hash. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:351](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:351) · [live_lock.py:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40)\\n\\n3. **Additional blocker — `build` can overwrite a file created while it runs.** The builder checks that the report name is free at startup. If another process creates a file there while the package is being checked, the final `os.replace` overwrites it. Publish the build’s report with an atomic operation that refuses an occupied destination. The decisive test places a marker file there immediately before the report write and requires the marker to survive, the checked package to remain available, and the command to exit 2. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:182](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:182) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:188](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:188)\\n\\nI found no further serious blocker in slice 1.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:40:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '15,47p' scripts/mock_build.py; sed -n '250,269p' scripts/hivemind_api.py; rg -n 'release|74h' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -12\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"from hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\\n    parser.add_argument('--data', type=Path, help='explicit legacy JSON export; otherwise read the current ledger')\\n    parser.add_argument('--ledger', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite')\\n    parser.add_argument('--items', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite')\\n    parser.add_argument('--out', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.html')\\n    parser.add_argument('--composite-trials', type=Path, help='explicit JSON trial baskets for the Idea score preview')\\n    parser.add_argument('--market-data', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/ui/data/nvda-2026-10-27.json', help='dated real stock-price snapshot for the Action preview')\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    if args.data:\\n        data = json.loads(args.data.read_text())\\n    else:\\n        conn, items = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(args.items))\\n        try:\\n            data = bundle.library(conn, items)\\n        finally:\\n            conn.close()\\n            items.close()\\n    if args.data and not data.get('schema_version') and args.ledger.exists():\\n        conn = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger))\\n        try:\\n            data['sequence_days'] = service.seq_day_map(conn)\\n        finally:\\n            conn.close()\\n    ui = ROOT / 'poc/ui'\\n    bundled = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'build.mjs'), '--json'], capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    if bundled.returncode:\\n        print('UI build failed. Install its pinned dependencies with: npm ci --prefix poc/ui', file=sys.stderr)\\n        print(bundled.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n        bundled.check_returncode()\\n            embedded, unchanged, tokens, error = search.ensure_index(db.ledger, db.index, **({'embed': embed} if embed else {}))\\n        except service.FirstDayNotCompleted:\\n            return \\\"index: not built, the store's first day has not completed; search is lexical until a restart after it completes\\\"\\n    return f'index: {embedded} views embedded, {unchanged} unchanged, {tokens} tokens' + (f'; embedding stopped ({error}): search runs lexical until the rest is built' if error else '')\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    global ALIASES, CFG, SEMANTIC\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    parser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'), help='the items database, for source titles in the idea card')\\n    parser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'idea-archive.sqlite'), help='where idea model calls are archived for replay')\\n    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118-idea.json'), help='the config whose idea settings name the mapping and final assessment models and prompts')\\n    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\\n    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8788)\\n    parser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    PATHS.update(views=args.views, items=args.items, index=args.index, archive=args.archive)\\n463:- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model; its\\n470:**Earlier next task (done, D758): Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** Decided by\\n475:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\\n479:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"). Nothing from it enters the\\n481:- **No release work is open yet.** No other task is queued on the number-answer line.\\n486:recommendation: close the v13s judge line, and carry D726 into the first release, so number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast\\n487:unavailable\\\". When release work opens, the first step is a $0 check of the reader's screen.\\n866:- **D688's recommendation, answered by D689:** keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. Questions on other\\n870:**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\\n878:- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\\n901:  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\\n904:- **If a draw stops:** no release verdict; a diagnostic export (plan §1.4 item 10).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat -n docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n     4\\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n     5\\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n     6\\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n     7\\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n     8\\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n     9\\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n    10\\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n    15\\t\\n    16\\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n    17\\t2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n    18\\t3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n    19\\t   word for it is already given.\\n    20\\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n    21\\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n    22\\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n    23\\t   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\n    28\\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\n    29\\tany one step's own score.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n    38\\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n    39\\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n    40\\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n    41\\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n    42\\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n    43\\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n    44\\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t**Evidence:**\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n    49\\t|---|---|---|\\n    50\\t| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n    51\\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n    52\\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n    53\\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n    60\\t|---|---|---|\\n    61\\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n    62\\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n    63\\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n    64\\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n    65\\t| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n    66\\t| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n    67\\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n    68\\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n    73\\t  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n    74\\t  system (D263).\\n    75\\t- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n    76\\t  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n    77\\t  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n    78\\t- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n    79\\t- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n    80\\t  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n    81\\t  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n    82\\t  competition or pricing\\\".\\n    83\\t- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n    84\\t  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n    85\\t  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n    86\\t  of the previous filing topic).\\n    87\\t- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n    88\\t  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n    89\\t  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n    90\\t  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n    91\\t- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t## 5. What to do\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\tStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n    98\\t   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n    99\\t   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   100\\t   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n   101\\t     the existing rule).\\n   102\\t   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   103\\t   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   104\\t   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   105\\t   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n   106\\t     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n   107\\t2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   108\\t   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   109\\t   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   110\\t   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   111\\t   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   112\\t   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   113\\t   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   114\\t   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n   115\\t3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   116\\t   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n   117\\t4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   118\\t   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n   119\\t\\n   120\\t## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n   123\\t  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n   124\\t  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n   125\\t- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n   126\\t  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n   127\\t  measured and reported apart.\\n   128\\t- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n   129\\t- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n   130\\t  counted after.\\n   131\\t- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n   132\\t  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n   133\\t  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n   134\\t  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n   135\\t    question\\\";\\n   136\\t  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n   137\\t  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n   138\\t  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n   139\\t    or no question uses);\\n   140\\t  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n   141\\t  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n   142\\t    ones that matter one by one.\\n   143\\t- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n   144\\t  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n   145\\t  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n   146\\t  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n   147\\t    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n   148\\t    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n   149\\t      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n   150\\t    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n   151\\t      facts must not fall.\\n   152\\t  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n   153\\t    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n   154\\t      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n   155\\t      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n   156\\t      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n   157\\t    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n   158\\t      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n   159\\t    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n   160\\t      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n   161\\t      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n   162\\t      what was measured.\\n   163\\t  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n   164\\t    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n   165\\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n   166\\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n   167\\t\\n   168\\t## 7. Process (no drift)\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n   171\\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n   172\\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n   173\\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n   174\\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n   175\\t  sentence, in both directions.\\n   176\\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n   177\\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\t## 8. Steps and where we are\\n   180\\t\\n   181\\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n   182\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   183\\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n   184\\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n   185\\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n   186\\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n   187\\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n   188\\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n   189\\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n   190\\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n   191\\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\t- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n   196\\t- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   197\\t- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   198\\t- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   199\\t- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   200\\t- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   201\\t- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,155p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 7, for council round 74g. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\\n    43\\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\\n    44\\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\\n    45\\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\\n    46\\t  pause.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\\n    49\\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\\n    50\\t  but the stores compare days as text.\\n    51\\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t## 0. Scope\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    56\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    57\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    58\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    59\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    60\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    61\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    62\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    63\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    64\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    65\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    66\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    67\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    68\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    69\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    70\\t  - any model call;\\n    71\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t## 1. What is built\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\t- **Constants:**\\n    78\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    79\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    80\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    81\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    82\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    85\\t  |---|---|\\n    86\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    87\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    88\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n    89\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    90\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    91\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n    94\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n    95\\t    only when the table exists;\\n    96\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n    97\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    98\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    99\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   100\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   101\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   102\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   103\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   104\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   105\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   106\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   107\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   108\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   109\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   110\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   111\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   112\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   113\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   114\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   115\\t  - Value checks:\\n   116\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   117\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   118\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   119\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   120\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   121\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   122\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   123\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   124\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   125\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   126\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   127\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   128\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   129\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   130\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   131\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   132\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   133\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   134\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   137\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   138\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   139\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   140\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   141\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   142\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   143\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   144\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   145\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   146\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   147\\t\\n   148\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   149\\t  compared.\\n   150\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   151\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   152\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   153\\t  else.\\n   154\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   155\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '301,445p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   301\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   302\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   303\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   304\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   305\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   306\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   307\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   308\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   309\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   310\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   311\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   312\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   313\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   314\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   315\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   316\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   317\\t9. **Package:**\\n   318\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   319\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   320\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   321\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   322\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   323\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   324\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   325\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   326\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   327\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   328\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   329\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   330\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\\n   331\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   332\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   333\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   334\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   335\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   336\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   337\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   338\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   339\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   340\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   341\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   342\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   343\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   344\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   345\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   346\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   347\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   348\\t      and inode).\\n   349\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   350\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   351\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database (a symbolic link to it, and the same\\n   352\\t    path): `build` refuses, and so does `check` on an existing package. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   353\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   354\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   355\\t15. **Files:**\\n   356\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   357\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   358\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   359\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   360\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   361\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   362\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   363\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   364\\t\\n   365\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   366\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   367\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   368\\t- the event test removed;\\n   369\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   370\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   371\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   372\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   373\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   374\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   375\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   376\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   377\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   378\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   379\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   380\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   381\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   382\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   383\\t- the report-path collision check removed (test 18's items file is then overwritten);\\n   384\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   385\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   386\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   387\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   388\\t\\n   389\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   390\\t\\n   391\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   392\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   393\\t\\n   394\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   395\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   396\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   397\\t\\n   398\\tThe steps:\\n   399\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   400\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   401\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   402\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   403\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   404\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   405\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   406\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   407\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   408\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   409\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   410\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   411\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   412\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   413\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   414\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   415\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   416\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   417\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   418\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   419\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   420\\t\\n   421\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   422\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   423\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   424\\t\\n   425\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   426\\t\\n   427\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   428\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   429\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   430\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   431\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   432\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   433\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   434\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   435\\t  judged position.\\n   436\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   437\\t  reproduces.\\n   438\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   439\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   440\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   441\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   442\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   443\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   444\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   445\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '156,300p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   156\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   157\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   158\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   161\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   162\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   163\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   164\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   165\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   166\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   167\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   168\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   169\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   172\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   173\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` early, as a convenience; `publish` holds the guarantee. Refuse when `<out>.report.json` exists, or\\n   174\\t     when it, or `--out`, resolves (`os.path.realpath`) to the ledger or items path;\\n   175\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   176\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   177\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   178\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   179\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   180\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   181\\t     nothing;\\n   182\\t  8. write `<out>.report.json` beside the package, through a temporary file and `os.replace`.\\n   183\\t\\n   184\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   185\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   186\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   187\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   188\\t  - **After publication** (step 8 fails): the package is final and checked. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not\\n   189\\t    written; run `check` to regenerate it\\\".\\n   190\\t\\n   191\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   192\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** first refuses when `<out>.report.json` resolves (`os.path.realpath`) to the ledger or items path.\\n   193\\t  It then re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical `as_of` validated against the store\\n   194\\t  (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\\n   195\\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   196\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   197\\t- **The report:**\\n   198\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   199\\t  - counts per class;\\n   200\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   201\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   202\\t  - bytes;\\n   203\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   204\\t\\n   205\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   206\\t\\n   207\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   208\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   209\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   210\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   211\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   212\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   213\\t| The report path resolves to the ledger or items input (build or `check`) | refused before anything is read or written; the input's bytes are untouched | nothing | — |\\n   214\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   215\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   216\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   217\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   218\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   219\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   220\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   221\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   222\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   223\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   224\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   225\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   226\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   227\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   228\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   229\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   230\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   231\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   232\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   233\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   234\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   235\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   236\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   237\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   238\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   239\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   240\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   241\\t\\n   242\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   243\\t\\n   244\\tReaders of the package:\\n   245\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   246\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   247\\t- the tests.\\n   248\\t\\n   249\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   250\\t\\n   251\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   252\\t|---|---|---|\\n   253\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   254\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   255\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   256\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   257\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   258\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   259\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   260\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   261\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   264\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   265\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   266\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   267\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   268\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   269\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   270\\t\\n   271\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   272\\t\\n   273\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   274\\t|---|---|\\n   275\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   276\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   277\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   278\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   279\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   280\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   281\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   282\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   283\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   284\\t\\n   285\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   286\\t\\n   287\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   288\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   289\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   290\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   291\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   292\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   293\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   294\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   295\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   296\\t\\n   297\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   298\\t\\n   299\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   300\\tits row above:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:27:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '1,360p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"Read-only answers over the views ledger, as of a calendar day (docs/poc/service.md).\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tNothing here reads the clock (D12, D13): every function takes `as_of`, a day, and the default is the ledger's last\\n     4\\tcompleted day. A row is visible as of a day when the sequence number it was written under belongs to an item or a\\n     5\\tdaily round dated on or before that day. Nothing here writes.\\n     6\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     7\\timport json\\n     8\\timport re\\n     9\\timport sqlite3\\n    10\\tfrom decimal import Decimal\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tfrom . import vocabulary\\n    13\\tfrom .views import store\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\tTIER_FACT = vocabulary.TIERS[0]          # 'fact'; a legacy ledger's '发生的事' compares equal through vocabulary.canonical\\n    16\\tCOMPARATORS = ('>=', '<', '=')\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tdef open_ledger(path):\\n    20\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A read-only connection to a views database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    21\\t    return store.open_read_only(path)\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tdef default_as_of(conn):\\n    25\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    26\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    30\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\\n    31\\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def __init__(self):\\n    34\\t        super().__init__(\\\"the store's first day has not completed\\\")\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    38\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\\n    41\\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\\n    42\\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\\n    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   146\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\\n   147\\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\\n   148\\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   150\\t    out = []\\n   151\\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\\n   152\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   153\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   154\\t            continue\\n   155\\t        is_open = is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)\\n   156\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open:\\n   157\\t            continue\\n   158\\t        out.append({'view_id': record['view_id'], 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   159\\t                    'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'open': is_open,\\n   160\\t                    'dependencies': [d['view_id'] for d in dependencies(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)], 'dependants': dependants(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)})\\n   161\\t    return out\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t\\n   164\\tdef views(conn, object_id=None, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   165\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   166\\t    rows = conn.execute('select * from views' + (' where object_id=?' if object_id else '') + ' order by created_seq', (object_id,) if object_id else ()).fetchall()\\n   167\\t    out = []\\n   168\\t    for record in rows:\\n   169\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   170\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   171\\t            continue\\n   172\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of):\\n   173\\t            continue\\n   174\\t        out.append(view(conn, record['view_id'], as_of, record=record))\\n   175\\t    return out\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\tdef dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   179\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's dependencies recorded on or before the day, each pointing at the target resolved on or before it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   180\\t    out = []\\n   181\\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\\n   182\\t        if not visible(conn, dep['seq'], as_of):\\n   183\\t            continue\\n   184\\t        target = dep['depends_on']\\n   185\\t        for res in conn.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc', (dep['dependency_id'],)):\\n   186\\t            if visible(conn, res['seq'], as_of):\\n   187\\t                target = res['resolved_to']\\n   188\\t                break\\n   189\\t        out.append({'view_id': target, 'direction': dep['direction'], 'wait_chain_view_id': dep['wait_chain_view_id'], 'wait_year': dep['wait_year'], 'since_day': day_of_seq(conn, dep['seq'])})\\n   190\\t    return out\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\tdef dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   194\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The views recorded on or before the day as depending on this one (directly or by a resolution).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   195\\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   196\\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select d.view_id, r.seq from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   197\\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\\n   201\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   202\\t    record = record or store.view(conn, view_id)\\n   203\\t    if not record or not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   204\\t        return None\\n   205\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   206\\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   207\\t    if state:\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   269\\t    arrivals = {}\\n   270\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\\n   271\\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\\n   272\\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\\n   273\\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\\n   274\\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\\n   275\\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\\n   276\\t            bucket['facts'] += int(vocabulary.canonical('tier', piece['tier']) == TIER_FACT)\\n   277\\t    replacements = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']), 'old': r['old_evidence_id'], 'new': r['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': r['said_day']}\\n   278\\t                    for r in conn.execute('select r.* from replacements r join evidence_links l on l.evidence_id=r.new_evidence_id where l.view_id=?', (view_id,))\\n   279\\t                    if day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) <= to_day]\\n   280\\t    switches = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']), 'open': bool(s['open']), 'reason': s['reason']}\\n   281\\t                for s in conn.execute('select * from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)) if day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) <= to_day]\\n   282\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'from_day': from_day, 'to_day': to_day, 'judgements': judgements,\\n   283\\t            'changes': [j for j in judgements if j['moved_from'] is not None], 'arrivals': dict(sorted(arrivals.items())),\\n   284\\t            'replacements': replacements, 'switches': switches}\\n   285\\t\\n   286\\t\\n   287\\tclass LedgerError(ValueError):\\n   288\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A ledger record the service cannot read (corrupt JSON): refused, never read as empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   289\\t\\n   290\\t\\n   291\\tclass StoreUnreadable(LedgerError):\\n   292\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The store could not be opened, or its read transaction begun and pinned (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 1): named by\\n   293\\t    its path, never answered with an empty or stale state.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   294\\t\\n   295\\t\\n   296\\tdef open_pinned(path):\\n   297\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A reader's connection with its committed state pinned (row 2: `BEGIN`, then a first read, which in WAL mode fixes the state\\n   298\\t    every later read of the request sees). A SQLite failure in these three steps closes what was opened and raises `StoreUnreadable`\\n   299\\t    naming the path; a later SQLite error is not covered here.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   300\\t    conn = None\\n   301\\t    try:\\n   302\\t        conn = open_ledger(path)\\n   303\\t        conn.execute('begin')\\n   304\\t        conn.execute('select 1 from sqlite_master limit 1').fetchone()\\n   305\\t        return conn\\n   306\\t    except sqlite3.Error as error:\\n   307\\t        if conn is not None:\\n   308\\t            conn.close()\\n   309\\t        raise StoreUnreadable(f'{path}: {error}') from error\\n   310\\t\\n   311\\t\\n   312\\tdef _unique(ids):\\n   313\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A judgement's cites as the UI contract reads them: each id once, first occurrence kept. The writer stores the set from\\n   314\\t    2026-10-28; the sealed ledger sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828 holds one judgement (v2, id 736) that cites an id twice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   315\\t    seen, out = set(), []\\n   316\\t    for value in ids:\\n   317\\t        if value not in seen:\\n   318\\t            seen.add(value)\\n   319\\t            out.append(value)\\n   320\\t    return out\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\t\\n   323\\tdef _json(text):\\n   324\\t    if not text:\\n   325\\t        return []\\n   326\\t    try:\\n   327\\t        return json.loads(text)\\n   328\\t    except ValueError as error:\\n   329\\t        raise LedgerError(f'a judgement record holds invalid JSON: {text[:60]!r}') from error\\n   330\\t\\n   331\\t\\n   332\\t# ---------- the processing record\\n   333\\t\\n   334\\tdef record(conn, view_id, as_of=None):\\n   335\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last check of the view on or before the day: when, by which round, how much came in that day.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   336\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   337\\t    row = conn.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, as_of)).fetchone()\\n   338\\t    if not row:\\n   339\\t        return {'view_id': view_id, 'as_of': as_of, 'last_check': None}\\n   340\\t    day = row['publication_day']\\n   341\\t    items = [r['input_id'] for r in conn.execute(\\\"select distinct input_id from processing_steps where publication_day=? and step='handed_over' and result='ok' and input_id not like 'day:%'\\\", (day,))]\\n   342\\t    arrived = sum(1 for link in conn.execute('select seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)) if day_of_seq(conn, link['seq']) == day)\\n   343\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'as_of': as_of, 'last_check': {'day': day, 'round': row['input_id'], 'items_processed_that_day': len(items), 'evidence_arrived_that_day': arrived}}\\n   344\\t\\n   345\\t\\n   346\\t# ---------- changes since a day\\n   347\\t\\n   348\\tdef changes(conn, since_day, to_day=None):\\n   349\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Judgements that said 'changed' after since_day (exclusive) up to to_day, with their cited evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   350\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, since_day, to_day)\\n   351\\t    out = []\\n   352\\t    previous = {}\\n   353\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements order by judgement_id'):\\n   354\\t        before = previous.get(row['view_id'])\\n   355\\t        previous[row['view_id']] = row['rung']\\n   356\\t        if not row['changed'] or not (since_day < row['publication_day'] <= to_day):\\n   357\\t            continue\\n   358\\t        cited = [piece for piece in (evidence_record(conn, e, row['publication_day']) for e in _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json']))) if piece]\\n   359\\t        out.append({'view_id': row['view_id'], 'day': row['publication_day'], 'from_position': before, 'to_position': row['rung'],\\n   360\\t                    'position_moved': before is not None and before != row['rung'], 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'cited': cited})\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '1,345p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\\n     2\\tevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\\n     3\\tswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\\n     4\\tend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     5\\timport json\\n     6\\tfrom contextlib import contextmanager\\n     7\\tfrom datetime import date\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tfrom . import service\\n    10\\tfrom .views import store\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t@contextmanager\\n    14\\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\\n    15\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    16\\t    owned = []\\n    17\\t    try:\\n    18\\t        for conn in connections:\\n    19\\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\\n    20\\t                conn.execute('begin')\\n    21\\t                owned.append(conn)\\n    22\\t        yield\\n    23\\t    finally:\\n    24\\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\\n    25\\t            conn.rollback()\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\\n    30\\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    31\\t    cache = {}\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def item_of(input_id):\\n    34\\t        if input_id not in cache:\\n    35\\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\\n    36\\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\\n    37\\t        return cache[input_id]\\n    38\\t    return item_of\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\\n    42\\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's ladder as the new system's writer stored it (`clean_ladders`, written in the view's own call): the parsed\\n    47\\t    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\\n    48\\t    view. A row that is not readable JSON with a ladder, or two rows for one view, is refused.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49\\t    if not views_db.execute(\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where type='table' and name='clean_ladders'\\\").fetchone():\\n    50\\t        return 'no table'\\n    51\\t    rows = views_db.execute('select checked_answer from clean_ladders where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchall()\\n    52\\t    if not rows:\\n    53\\t        return 'no row'\\n    54\\t    if len(rows) > 1:\\n    55\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: {len(rows)} ladder rows for one view')\\n    56\\t    try:\\n    57\\t        ladder = json.loads(rows[0][0])['ladder']\\n    58\\t    except (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError) as error:\\n    59\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder ({error!r})')\\n    60\\t    if not isinstance(ladder, dict):\\n    61\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder')\\n    62\\t    return ladder\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\tdef not_judged(views_db, view_id, created_seq, as_of=None):\\n    66\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"D397: the parts of a topic its one judged question leaves out, with their reasons, from the view's ladder row. None for a\\n    67\\t    legacy ledger, for a view with no row, and before the view's creation at as_of; [] when the row lists none. A malformed row,\\n    68\\t    or two rows for one view, is refused. Called directly for a view not visible at the resolved bound, it refuses the view\\n    69\\t    (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3), so a question created after that day is never returned.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    70\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n    71\\t    if as_of is not None and not _visible(views_db, created_seq, as_of):\\n    72\\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n    73\\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\\n    74\\t    if ladder in ('no table', 'no row'):\\n    75\\t        return None\\n    76\\t    parts = ladder.get('not_judged')\\n    77\\t    if not isinstance(parts, list) or not all(isinstance(p, dict) and isinstance(p.get('part'), str) and isinstance(p.get('why'), str) for p in parts):\\n    78\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its parts not judged are not a list of {{part, why}} texts')\\n    79\\t    return [{'part': p['part'], 'why': p['why']} for p in parts]\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\tdef answer_shape(views_db, view_id):\\n    83\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"(shape, favourable end) of the view's answer choices, as the page needs them to read the stored labels without inventing a\\n    84\\t    direction (page-contract/DESIGN.md): (None, None) for a legacy ledger; ('unrecorded', None) for a view with no row in a store\\n    85\\t    that has rows; ('event', None) or ('figure', 'higher' | 'lower' | 'n/a') from the row. Not suppressed before creation: it says\\n    86\\t    how to read the labels, which are shown as they are.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    87\\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\\n    88\\t    if ladder == 'no table':\\n    89\\t        return None, None\\n    90\\t    if ladder == 'no row':\\n    91\\t        return 'unrecorded', None\\n    92\\t    if ladder.get('event'):\\n    93\\t        return 'event', None\\n    94\\t    figure = ladder.get('figure')\\n    95\\t    if isinstance(figure, dict) and figure.get('favourable_end') in ('higher', 'lower', 'n/a'):\\n    96\\t        return 'figure', figure['favourable_end']\\n    97\\t    raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row is neither an event nor a figure with a favourable end')\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\tdef view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\\n   101\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One view's complete record as of the bound (resolved; an omitted bound on a store with no completed day reads every\\n   102\\t    record, as before). A view not visible at the bound is refused (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   103\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n   104\\t    v = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   105\\t    if v is None:\\n   106\\t        raise KeyError(view_id)\\n   107\\t    if as_of is not None and not service.view_exists(views_db, v, as_of):\\n   108\\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n   109\\t    columns = {r[1] for r in views_db.execute('pragma table_info(rungs)')}\\n   110\\t    bounds = ', lo, hi' if {'lo', 'hi'} <= columns else ''          # a ledger written before keys has no bounds; the adapter then reads the prose\\n   111\\t    rungs = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute(f'select position, label, condition{bounds} from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n   112\\t    switches = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,))\\n   113\\t                if _visible(views_db, r['after_seq'], as_of)]\\n   114\\t    for switch in switches:\\n   115\\t        switch['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, switch['after_seq'])\\n   116\\t    judgements = []\\n   117\\t    for j in views_db.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   118\\t        if as_of is not None and j['publication_day'] > as_of:\\n   119\\t            continue\\n   120\\t        judgements.append({'id': str(j['judgement_id']), 'day': j['publication_day'], 'seq': j['seq'], 'rung': j['rung'], 'changed': bool(j['changed']),\\n   121\\t                           'why_changed': j['why_changed'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'cited': list(dict.fromkeys(json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json'] or '[]'))),   # each id once (UI contract uniqueItems); the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger holds one judgement citing an id twice\\n   122\\t                           'cited_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json'] or '[]'), 'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json'] or '[]'),\\n   123\\t                           'from_item': j['input_id']})\\n   124\\t    evidence = []\\n   125\\t    for e in views_db.execute('select e.*, l.seq as linked_seq from evidence_links l join evidence e on e.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by l.id', (view_id,)):\\n   126\\t        if not _visible(views_db, e['linked_seq'], as_of):\\n   127\\t            continue\\n   128\\t        sources = [dict(s) for s in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (e['evidence_id'],))\\n   129\\t                   if _visible(views_db, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   130\\t        replaced_by = views_db.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   131\\t        if replaced_by is not None and not _visible(views_db, replaced_by['seq'], as_of):\\n   132\\t            replaced_by = None\\n   133\\t        replaces = views_db.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   134\\t        if replaces and not _visible(views_db, replaces['seq'], as_of):\\n   135\\t            replaces = None\\n   136\\t        first = sources[0] if sources else {'input_id': e['created_from_input'], 'publication_day': '', 'seq': e['created_seq']}\\n   137\\t        item = item_of(first['input_id'])\\n   138\\t        evidence.append({'id': e['evidence_id'], 'one_line': e['one_line'], 'quote': e['quote'], 'tier': e['tier'], 'speaker': e['speaker'],\\n   139\\t                         'original_who': e['original_who'], 'original_day': e['original_day'], 'event_time': e['event_time'],\\n   140\\t                         'day': first['publication_day'] or item['publication_day'], 'seq': first['seq'], 'linked_seq': e['linked_seq'],\\n   141\\t                         'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, e['linked_seq']),\\n   142\\t                         'source': {'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'publisher_type': item['publisher_type'],\\n   143\\t                                    'category': item['category'], 'uri': item['source_uri']},\\n   144\\t                         'sources': [{'input_id': s['input_id'], 'day': s['publication_day'],\\n   145\\t                                      'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, s['seq']),\\n   146\\t                                      'source': item_of(s['input_id'])} for s in sources],\\n   147\\t                         'outlets': len(sources), 'replaced_by': {'new_evidence_id': replaced_by['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': replaced_by['said_day'],\\n   148\\t                                                               'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, replaced_by['seq'])} if replaced_by else None,\\n   149\\t                         'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces else None})\\n   150\\t    dependencies = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select dependency_id, depends_on, direction, wait_chain_view_id, wait_year, seq from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,))\\n   151\\t                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   152\\t    for dependency in dependencies:\\n   153\\t        dependency['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, dependency['seq'])\\n   154\\t        dependency['resolutions'] = [dict(target=r['resolved_to'], day=service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq']), seq=r['seq'])\\n   155\\t                                    for r in views_db.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id', (dependency['dependency_id'],))\\n   156\\t                                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   157\\t    dependants = sorted({r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)},\\n   158\\t                        key=lambda s: (len(s), s))\\n   159\\t    created = item_of(v['created_from_input'])\\n   160\\t    key = store.view_key(views_db, view_id)\\n   161\\t    identity = {name: key[name] for name in ('measure', 'scope', 'period_start', 'period_end', 'basis', 'unit', 'event_type')} if key else None\\n   162\\t    successions = [{'thesis_id': r['succeeds'] if r['view_id'] == view_id else r['view_id'],\\n   163\\t                    'relation': 'previous' if r['view_id'] == view_id else 'next',\\n   164\\t                    'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq'])}\\n   165\\t                   for r in views_db.execute('select * from successions where view_id=? or succeeds=? order by id', (view_id, view_id))\\n   166\\t                   if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   167\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'object': v['object_id'], 'kind': v['kind'], 'looks_at': v['looks_at'], 'question': v['question'],\\n   168\\t            'due_day': v['due_day'], 'year': v['year'], 'identity': identity, 'successions': successions,\\n   169\\t            'created_seq': v['created_seq'], 'created_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, v['created_seq']),\\n   170\\t            'created_from': {'title': created['title'], 'publisher': created['publisher'], 'category': created['category']},\\n   171\\t            'rungs': rungs, 'open': not any(not s['open'] for s in switches), 'switches': switches,\\n   172\\t            'judgements': judgements, 'evidence': evidence, 'dependencies': dependencies, 'dependants': dependants,\\n   173\\t            'not_judged': not_judged(views_db, view_id, v['created_seq'], as_of),\\n   174\\t            **dict(zip(('answer_shape', 'favourable_end'), answer_shape(views_db, view_id)))}\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\tdef days(views_db, as_of=None):\\n   178\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The completed days the front end's time axis runs over, up to as_of.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   179\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n   180\\t    return [r[0] for r in views_db.execute('select day from days_completed order by day') if as_of is None or r[0] <= as_of]\\n   181\\t\\n   182\\t\\n   183\\tdef _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\\n   184\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Complete, dated UI inputs for caller-selected theses; no search, model call or ledger write. Its bound is already resolved\\n   185\\t    by its caller (`thesis_bundles`, `library`).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   186\\t    date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   187\\t    if not isinstance(view_ids, list) or not view_ids or any(not isinstance(id, str) or not id for id in view_ids):\\n   188\\t        raise ValueError('thesis_bundles needs a non-empty list of view ids')\\n   189\\t    lookup = item_lookup(items_db)\\n   190\\t    records = []\\n   191\\t    for view_id in dict.fromkeys(view_ids):\\n   192\\t        row = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   193\\t        if row is None or not service.view_exists(views_db, row, as_of):\\n   194\\t            raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n   195\\t        records.append(view_bundle(views_db, lookup, view_id, as_of))\\n   196\\t    return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': records,\\n   197\\t            'coverage': coverage, 'groups': research_groups(views_db, view_ids, as_of)}\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef research_groups(conn, view_ids, as_of):\\n   201\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Stored groups, with dated memberships limited to the envelope's loaded theses.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   202\\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_groups)').fetchone():\\n   203\\t        return []\\n   204\\t    loaded = set(view_ids)\\n   205\\t    result = []\\n   206\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from thesis_groups order by created_seq, rowid'):\\n   207\\t        if not service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of):\\n   208\\t            continue\\n   209\\t        members = [{'thesis_id': m['view_id'], 'day': service.day_of_seq(conn, m['seq']), 'basis': m['basis'] or ''}\\n   210\\t                   for m in conn.execute('select * from thesis_group_members where group_id=? order by id', (row['group_id'],))\\n   211\\t                   if m['view_id'] in loaded and service.visible(conn, m['seq'], as_of)]\\n   212\\t        if members:\\n   213\\t            result.append({'id': row['group_id'], 'name': row['name'], 'scope': row['scope'],\\n   214\\t                           'aliases': json.loads(row['aliases'] or '[]') if 'aliases' in row.keys() else [],\\n   215\\t                           'created_day': service.day_of_seq(conn, row['created_seq']), 'members': members})\\n   216\\t    return result\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\tdef thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\\n   220\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   221\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   222\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   228\\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\\n   229\\t        if not as_of:\\n   230\\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\\n   231\\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   232\\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\\n   233\\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\\n   234\\t        if not view_ids:\\n   235\\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\\n   236\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '195,295p'; rg -n 'def ladder_bands|def open_read_only|def rungs_of|def view_key|def canonical|EVENT_MEASURES' src/hivemind/{service.py,vocabulary.py,views/store.py,views/identity.py}\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   195\\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   196\\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select d.view_id, r.seq from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   197\\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\\n   201\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   202\\t    record = record or store.view(conn, view_id)\\n   203\\t    if not record or not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   204\\t        return None\\n   205\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   206\\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   207\\t    if state:\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   269\\t    arrivals = {}\\n   270\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\\n   271\\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\\n   272\\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\\n   273\\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\\n   274\\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\\n   275\\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\\n   276\\t            bucket['facts'] += int(vocabulary.canonical('tier', piece['tier']) == TIER_FACT)\\n   277\\t    replacements = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']), 'old': r['old_evidence_id'], 'new': r['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': r['said_day']}\\n   278\\t                    for r in conn.execute('select r.* from replacements r join evidence_links l on l.evidence_id=r.new_evidence_id where l.view_id=?', (view_id,))\\n   279\\t                    if day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, r['seq']) <= to_day]\\n   280\\t    switches = [{'day': day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']), 'open': bool(s['open']), 'reason': s['reason']}\\n   281\\t                for s in conn.execute('select * from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)) if day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) and from_day <= day_of_seq(conn, s['after_seq']) <= to_day]\\n   282\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'from_day': from_day, 'to_day': to_day, 'judgements': judgements,\\n   283\\t            'changes': [j for j in judgements if j['moved_from'] is not None], 'arrivals': dict(sorted(arrivals.items())),\\n   284\\t            'replacements': replacements, 'switches': switches}\\n   285\\t\\n   286\\t\\n   287\\tclass LedgerError(ValueError):\\n   288\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A ledger record the service cannot read (corrupt JSON): refused, never read as empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   289\\t\\n   290\\t\\n   291\\tclass StoreUnreadable(LedgerError):\\n   292\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The store could not be opened, or its read transaction begun and pinned (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 1): named by\\n   293\\t    its path, never answered with an empty or stale state.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   294\\t\\n   295\\t\\nsrc/hivemind/views/identity.py:10:EVENT_MEASURES = ('event', 'policy_event')\\nsrc/hivemind/views/identity.py:15:    return value.get('measure') not in (None, 'other', *EVENT_MEASURES) and (value.get('scope_source') == 'shared' or value.get('opens_as') in SHARED_REASONS)\\nsrc/hivemind/views/identity.py:29:    if value['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES and value.get('event_type') in (None, 'other', 'n/a'):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/identity.py:55:    if key['measure'] != candidate['measure'] and not (key['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES and candidate['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/identity.py:69:    if key['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES:\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:97:def rungs_of(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:159:def view_key(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:223:def open_read_only(path):\\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:28:def canonical(field, value):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:499:def ladder_bands(rungs):\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'realpath|samefile|canonical|report|mutant' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74f.md; rg -n 'served ledger|items-comparison|sealed.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{round74-brief.md,claude-r74.md,codex-r74.md}\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"rg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74f.md: IO error for operation on docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74f.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:23:     served ledger's \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:43:  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:40:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'served ledger|served store|items-comparison.sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers -g 'codex-r72*.md' | head -n 13; ls -l poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '104,176p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:3:2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  19767296 Nov 18 01:20 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\n   104\\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\\n   105\\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\\n   106\\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\\n   107\\t   design and in the question to Alex.\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\\n   110\\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\\n   111\\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\\n   112\\t  and whether that decision is identity (\\\"are these the same thing?\\\") or judgement (\\\"does this matter?\\\"); build only the identity part.\\n   113\\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \\\"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\\\").\\n   114\\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\\n   115\\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\\n   116\\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \\\"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\\\").\\n   117\\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\\n   118\\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\\n   119\\t  question, not something to build.\\n   120\\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t## 3. Writing code\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t- **One owner.** A rule lives where the data is written, and refuses: a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure. Fix the\\n   125\\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\\n   126\\t  same key or rule.\\n   127\\t- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\\n   128\\t  of prompts and documents.\\n   129\\t- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\\n   130\\t  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\\n   131\\t  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\\n   132\\t- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\\n   133\\t  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\\n   134\\t  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\\n   135\\t- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\\n   136\\t  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\\n   137\\t  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\\n   138\\t- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\\n   139\\t  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \\\"now\\\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\\n   140\\t- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\\n   141\\t- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\\n   142\\t  justifies a dependency.\\n   143\\t- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\t## 4. Tests\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\\n   148\\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\\n   149\\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\\n   150\\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\\n   151\\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\\n   152\\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\\n   153\\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\\n   154\\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\\n   155\\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\\n   156\\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\\n   157\\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\\n   158\\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\\n   159\\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\\\"never called\\\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\\n   160\\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\\n   161\\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\\n   162\\t  unexercised, not passed.\\n   163\\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\\n   164\\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\\n   165\\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\\n   166\\t  the inner function with every argument set.\\n   167\\t\\n   168\\t## 5. Verification\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\\n   171\\t1. Stored data: reproduce the failing case, show the fix flips it, show a mutant of the fix fails the check ($0).\\n   172\\t2. Only when what the model is asked changed: re-send just the affected calls.\\n   173\\t3. The touched suites, plus any standing structural checks the change can affect; the full suite once.\\n   174\\t4. The gate once, at merge (README, \\\"Build and check\\\"). The acceptance once, on the final configuration, scored on the frozen ruler\\n   175\\t   (§7.1). Never a full rerun per fix.\\n   176\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.stream:46:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ls -l poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '216,240p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '493,540p'; rg -n 'served|items.sqlite' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -n 8\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"total 470328\\n-r--r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff        129 Nov 17 20:46 comparison-limits.json\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff       2824 Nov 19 12:41 diagnostic-chain.log\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff          6 Nov 19 12:42 diagnostic-chain.pid\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff       1197 Nov 19 12:50 diagnostic-continue.log\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff       3591 Nov 17 20:45 excluded.json\\n-r--r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  240697344 Nov 17 20:45 items-comparison.sqlite\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff         90 Nov 17 20:45 items-comparison.sqlite.sha256\\n-r--r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff      70510 Nov 17 20:45 manifest-2026-07-01-09-20.json\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 lchingen  staff        640 Nov 19 13:31 probe-one-outcome-20261119\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff         37 Nov 19 12:41 reading-chain.log\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff        109 Nov 19 12:28 reading-chain.log.first-wait\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff          6 Nov 19 12:41 reading-chain.pid\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 lchingen  staff        192 Nov 19 12:51 reading-diagnostic\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 21 lchingen  staff        672 Nov 17 22:36 run\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff        288 Nov 17 20:55 slice\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 lchingen  staff        288 Nov 17 22:05 slice-2\\n   216\\tdef has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq):\\n   217\\t    return conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and seq=?', (view_id, seq)).fetchone() is not None\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\tREAD_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 5.0     # a reader's busy timeout: SQLite's busy handler retries SQLITE_BUSY within it (live-service row 1)\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t\\n   223\\tdef open_read_only(path):\\n   224\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The views database for a reader (the agent layer, reports): no schema creation, no writes. Opened by its own path: a symlink\\n   225\\t    resolved, a store with another hard link refused (`live_lock.LockRefused`; live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 7), since\\n   226\\t    SQLite finds a WAL store's side files by the opened path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    from hivemind import live_lock\\n   228\\t    real, _ = live_lock.own_path(path)\\n   229\\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{real}?mode=ro', uri=True, timeout=READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\\n   230\\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\\n   231\\t    return conn\\n   232\\t\\n   233\\t\\n   234\\tdef current_state(conn, view_id):\\n   235\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The latest judgement: rung, reasons, changed, seq and day, and its reference and implied outcome (D260) where the ledger has them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   236\\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\\n   237\\t    stance = ''.join(f', {field}' for field in ('reference', 'implied_outcome') if field in columns)\\n   238\\t    row = conn.execute(f'select judgement_id, rung, reasons, changed, seq, publication_day{stance} from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   239\\t    return dict(row) if row else None\\n   240\\t\\n   493\\t    for r in rungs:\\n   494\\t        lo = -INF if r.get('lo') is None else float(r['lo']); hi = INF if r.get('hi') is None else float(r['hi'])\\n   495\\t        out[r['position']] = (lo, True, hi, False)\\n   496\\t    return out\\n   497\\t\\n   498\\t\\n   499\\tdef ladder_bands(rungs):\\n   500\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every rung's band, or None with the reason when the ladder is not one unbroken partition by amount. Rungs that\\n   501\\t    carry numeric bounds are read from them; the prose parser serves the views written before keys.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   502\\t    numeric = numeric_bands(rungs)\\n   503\\t    if numeric is not None:\\n   504\\t        ordered = sorted(numeric.items(), key=lambda pb: pb[1][0])\\n   505\\t        for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   506\\t            if a[2] != b[0]:\\n   507\\t                return None, f'numeric bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   508\\t        return numeric, None\\n   509\\t    bands = [(r['position'], band(r['condition'])) for r in rungs]\\n   510\\t    unreadable = [p for p, b in bands if b is None]\\n   511\\t    if unreadable:\\n   512\\t        return None, f'conditions not read as amounts: positions {unreadable}'\\n   513\\t    ordered = sorted(bands, key=lambda pb: (pb[1][0], pb[1][2]))\\n   514\\t    for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   515\\t        if a[2] != b[0] or a[3] == b[1]:          # adjacent bands share the boundary amount and exactly one of them owns it\\n   516\\t            return None, f'bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   517\\t    lowest, highest = ordered[0][1], ordered[-1][1]\\n   518\\t    if not (lowest[0] == -INF or (lowest[0] == 0 and lowest[1])) or highest[2] != INF:     # an amount that cannot be negative may start at 0\\n   519\\t        return None, 'the ladder does not cover the line up to +inf'\\n   520\\t    return dict(bands), None\\n   521\\t\\n   522\\t\\n   523\\tdef _contains(b, yi):\\n   524\\t    lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc = b\\n   525\\t    return (lo < yi or (lo == yi and lo_inc)) and (yi < hi or (yi == hi and hi_inc))\\n   526\\t\\n   527\\t\\n   528\\tdef verdict_for(comparator, judged, yi):\\n   529\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whether every value in the judged band satisfies the claim (holds), none does (not_yet), or some do.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   530\\t    lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc = judged\\n   531\\t    all_at_least = lo > yi or (lo == yi)                       # every value >= yi (lo == yi exclusive gives values > yi)\\n   532\\t    all_below = hi < yi or (hi == yi and not hi_inc)\\n   533\\t    if comparator == '>=':\\n   534\\t        return 'holds' if all_at_least else 'not_yet' if all_below else 'borderline'\\n   535\\t    if comparator == '<':\\n   536\\t        return 'holds' if all_below else 'not_yet' if all_at_least else 'borderline'\\n   537\\t    if lo == hi == yi:\\n   538\\t        return 'holds'\\n   539\\t    return 'borderline' if _contains(judged, yi) else 'not_yet'\\n   540\\t\\n54:  re-asked caused the China miss. Observed defect of the frozen judge: it names the export-controls theme as a dependency of the China\\n126:**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \\\"null\\\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \\\"One next task\\\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\\n135:- **Served data:** the service, the MCP server and the standalone page serve the sealed three-month ledger `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828` (68 theses, 34 groups; D358), built by the earlier `poc-v34` pipeline, not by the replay default. HTTP `/library`, MCP `thesis_library` and the standalone page share the dated bundle writer.\\n157:   new-system store is served live today.\\n335:- **Serving while writing (D574):** no partial day leaks into the completed-day view; a freshly opened page now shows the served\\n397:  - **Slice 1:** one owner for every upper date bound. A future date is refused, and the served product store's half-processed\\n794:  output. Recommended to Alex: a $0 half-hour read of old-2's finished 09-20 store served locally; only on his yes, the daily wrapper\\n795:  and a rehearsal week over 09-21..09-27. Alex said go (2026-11-20; his word in RESULT.md): step 1 is served on the host at http://127.0.0.1:8792\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"wc -lc docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\\\"'^#'\\\"' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md; sed -n '1,80p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     481   35299 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\\n     201   26537 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\n     682   61836 total\\n1:# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n71:## 0. Scope\\n91:## 1. What is built\\n230:## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n267:## 3. Value × reader\\n296:## 4. New path × old checks\\n310:## 5. Prior decisions\\n322:## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n425:## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n461:## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n\\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n\\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n\\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n\\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n   word for it is already given.\\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n\\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n\\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\nany one step's own score.\\n\\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n\\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n\\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n\\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n\\n**Evidence:**\\n\\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n\\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n\\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n\\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n\\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n  system (D263).\\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,170p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 10, for council round 74j. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\\n    43\\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\\n    44\\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\\n    45\\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\\n    46\\t  pause.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\\n    49\\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\\n    50\\t  but the stores compare days as text.\\n    51\\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\\n    54\\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\\n    55\\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\\n    56\\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\\n    57\\t  anything exists there.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\\n    60\\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\\n    61\\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t**Revision 9 answers `codex-r74h.md`.**\\n    64\\t- A report is published the moment its link succeeds. A later failure to remove the temporary file is reported as published, naming\\n    65\\t  the leftover file.\\n    66\\t- `check`'s exit statuses are explicit, and the end-to-end tests assert them.\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t**Revision 10 answers `codex-r74i.md`:** `check` follows the build's rule. Any failure to publish the report before the link succeeds\\n    69\\t(the name occupied, or the temporary file not created or written, such as `EACCES`) is exit 2 after the printed pass.\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t## 0. Scope\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    74\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    75\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    76\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    77\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    78\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    79\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    80\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    81\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    82\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    83\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    84\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    85\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    86\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    87\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    88\\t  - any model call;\\n    89\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t## 1. What is built\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\t- **Constants:**\\n    96\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    97\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    98\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    99\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n   100\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n   103\\t  |---|---|\\n   104\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n   105\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n   106\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n   107\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n   108\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n   109\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n   112\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n   113\\t    only when the table exists;\\n   114\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n   115\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n   116\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n   117\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   118\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   119\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   120\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   121\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   122\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   123\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   124\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   125\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   126\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   127\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   128\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   129\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   130\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   131\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   132\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   133\\t  - Value checks:\\n   134\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   135\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   136\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   137\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   138\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   139\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   140\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   141\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   142\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   143\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   144\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   145\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   146\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   147\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   148\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   149\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   150\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   151\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   152\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   153\\t\\n   154\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   155\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   156\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   157\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   158\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   159\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   160\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   161\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   162\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   163\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   164\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   165\\t\\n   166\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   167\\t  compared.\\n   168\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   169\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   170\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '325,481p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   325\\tits row above:\\n   326\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   327\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   328\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   329\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   330\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   331\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   332\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   333\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   334\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   335\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   336\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   337\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   338\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   339\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   340\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   341\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   342\\t9. **Package:**\\n   343\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   344\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   345\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   346\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   347\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   348\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   349\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   350\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   351\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   352\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   353\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   354\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   355\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n   356\\t    - the build exits 0, and the package and its report exist;\\n   357\\t    - `check` with the build's report still in place prints a passing result and exits 2;\\n   358\\t    - after the test removes that report, `check` exits 0 and publishes a fresh one.\\n   359\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   360\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   361\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   362\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   363\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   364\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   365\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   366\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   367\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   368\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   369\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   370\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   371\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   372\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   373\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   374\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   375\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   376\\t      and inode).\\n   377\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   378\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   379\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\\n   380\\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\\n   381\\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   382\\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file\\n   383\\t    at the report name. The command exits 2 and the marker is unchanged. `check` then prints a passing result, exits 2, and leaves the\\n   384\\t    marker unchanged.\\n   385\\t21. **`check` cannot write its report** (a scratch copy in which creating the report's temporary file raises `PermissionError`): `check`\\n   386\\t    prints the passing result and the write error, and exits 2.\\n   387\\t20. **Temporary file left after the link** (a scratch copy in which removing the report's temporary file raises): the build exits 0\\n   388\\t    and says the report is published, naming the leftover temporary file. The report exists and equals the build's report.\\n   389\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   390\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   391\\t15. **Files:**\\n   392\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   393\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   394\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   395\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   396\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   397\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   398\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   399\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   400\\t\\n   401\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   402\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   403\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   404\\t- the event test removed;\\n   405\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   406\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   407\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   408\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   409\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   410\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   411\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   412\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   413\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   414\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   415\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   416\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   417\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   418\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   419\\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\\n   420\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   421\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   422\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   423\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   424\\t\\n   425\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   426\\t\\n   427\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   428\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   429\\t\\n   430\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   431\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   432\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   433\\t\\n   434\\tThe steps:\\n   435\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   436\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   437\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   438\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   439\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   440\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   441\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   442\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   443\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   444\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   445\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   446\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   447\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   448\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   449\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   450\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   451\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   452\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   453\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   454\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   455\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   456\\t\\n   457\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   458\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   459\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   460\\t\\n   461\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   462\\t\\n   463\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   464\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   465\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   466\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   467\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   468\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   469\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   470\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   471\\t  judged position.\\n   472\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   473\\t  reproduces.\\n   474\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   475\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   476\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   477\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   478\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   479\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   480\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   481\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '171,324p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   171\\t  else.\\n   172\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   173\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   174\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   175\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   176\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   179\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   180\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   181\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   182\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   183\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   184\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   185\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   186\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   187\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   188\\t\\n   189\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   190\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   191\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   192\\t     guarantee;\\n   193\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   194\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   195\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   196\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   197\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   198\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   199\\t     nothing;\\n   200\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   201\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   202\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   203\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   204\\t\\n   205\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   206\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   207\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   208\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   209\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   210\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   211\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   212\\t\\n   213\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   214\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   215\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   216\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   217\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   218\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report is not published: its name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else, which stays\\n   219\\t    untouched), or writing the temporary file or the link fails for any other reason, which is printed;\\n   220\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   221\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   222\\t- **The report:**\\n   223\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   224\\t  - counts per class;\\n   225\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   226\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   227\\t  - bytes;\\n   228\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   229\\t\\n   230\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   231\\t\\n   232\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   233\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   234\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   235\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   236\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   237\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   238\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   239\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   240\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   241\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   242\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   243\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   244\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   245\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   246\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   247\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   248\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   249\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   250\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   251\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   252\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   253\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   254\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   255\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   256\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   257\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   258\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   259\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   260\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   261\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   262\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   263\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   264\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   265\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   266\\t\\n   267\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   268\\t\\n   269\\tReaders of the package:\\n   270\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   271\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   272\\t- the tests.\\n   273\\t\\n   274\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   275\\t\\n   276\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   277\\t|---|---|---|\\n   278\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   279\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   280\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   281\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   282\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   283\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   284\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   285\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   286\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   287\\t\\n   288\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   289\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   290\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   291\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   292\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   293\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   294\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   295\\t\\n   296\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   297\\t\\n   298\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   299\\t|---|---|\\n   300\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   301\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   302\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   303\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   304\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   305\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   306\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   307\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   308\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   309\\t\\n   310\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   311\\t\\n   312\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   313\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   314\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   315\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   316\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   317\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   318\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   319\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   320\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   323\\t\\n   324\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '35,151p;170,275p;499,520p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    35\\t\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    38\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\\n    41\\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\\n    42\\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\\n    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   146\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\\n   147\\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\\n   148\\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   150\\t    out = []\\n   151\\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\\n   170\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   171\\t            continue\\n   172\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of):\\n   173\\t            continue\\n   174\\t        out.append(view(conn, record['view_id'], as_of, record=record))\\n   175\\t    return out\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\tdef dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   179\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's dependencies recorded on or before the day, each pointing at the target resolved on or before it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   180\\t    out = []\\n   181\\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\\n   182\\t        if not visible(conn, dep['seq'], as_of):\\n   183\\t            continue\\n   184\\t        target = dep['depends_on']\\n   185\\t        for res in conn.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc', (dep['dependency_id'],)):\\n   186\\t            if visible(conn, res['seq'], as_of):\\n   187\\t                target = res['resolved_to']\\n   188\\t                break\\n   189\\t        out.append({'view_id': target, 'direction': dep['direction'], 'wait_chain_view_id': dep['wait_chain_view_id'], 'wait_year': dep['wait_year'], 'since_day': day_of_seq(conn, dep['seq'])})\\n   190\\t    return out\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\tdef dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   194\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The views recorded on or before the day as depending on this one (directly or by a resolution).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   195\\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   196\\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select d.view_id, r.seq from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   197\\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\\n   201\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   202\\t    record = record or store.view(conn, view_id)\\n   203\\t    if not record or not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   204\\t        return None\\n   205\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   206\\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   207\\t    if state:\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   269\\t    arrivals = {}\\n   270\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\\n   271\\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\\n   272\\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\\n   273\\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\\n   274\\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\\n   275\\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\\n   499\\tdef ladder_bands(rungs):\\n   500\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every rung's band, or None with the reason when the ladder is not one unbroken partition by amount. Rungs that\\n   501\\t    carry numeric bounds are read from them; the prose parser serves the views written before keys.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   502\\t    numeric = numeric_bands(rungs)\\n   503\\t    if numeric is not None:\\n   504\\t        ordered = sorted(numeric.items(), key=lambda pb: pb[1][0])\\n   505\\t        for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   506\\t            if a[2] != b[0]:\\n   507\\t                return None, f'numeric bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   508\\t        return numeric, None\\n   509\\t    bands = [(r['position'], band(r['condition'])) for r in rungs]\\n   510\\t    unreadable = [p for p, b in bands if b is None]\\n   511\\t    if unreadable:\\n   512\\t        return None, f'conditions not read as amounts: positions {unreadable}'\\n   513\\t    ordered = sorted(bands, key=lambda pb: (pb[1][0], pb[1][2]))\\n   514\\t    for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n   515\\t        if a[2] != b[0] or a[3] == b[1]:          # adjacent bands share the boundary amount and exactly one of them owns it\\n   516\\t            return None, f'bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n   517\\t    lowest, highest = ordered[0][1], ordered[-1][1]\\n   518\\t    if not (lowest[0] == -INF or (lowest[0] == 0 and lowest[1])) or highest[2] != INF:     # an amount that cannot be negative may start at 0\\n   519\\t        return None, 'the ladder does not cover the line up to +inf'\\n   520\\t    return dict(bands), None\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '81,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n  competition or pricing\\\".\\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n  of the previous filing topic).\\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n\\n## 5. What to do\\n\\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n\\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n     the existing rule).\\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n\\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n\\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n  measured and reported apart.\\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n  counted after.\\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n    question\\\";\\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n    or no question uses);\\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n    ones that matter one by one.\\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n      facts must not fall.\\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n      what was measured.\\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n\\n## 7. Process (no drift)\\n\\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n  sentence, in both directions.\\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n\\n## 8. Steps and where we are\\n\\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n\\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n\\n- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\\\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\\\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\\\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\\\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\\\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\\\"自己的量，别的期间\\\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"跑验收\\\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\\\"中国份额归零\\\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"都做\\\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '1,55p;100,148p;225,267p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '91,110p;156,170p;415,449p'; rg -n 'create table (evidence|items)|CREATE TABLE (IF NOT EXISTS )?(evidence|items)' src\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\\n     2\\tevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\\n     3\\tswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\\n     4\\tend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     5\\timport json\\n     6\\tfrom contextlib import contextmanager\\n     7\\tfrom datetime import date\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tfrom . import service\\n    10\\tfrom .views import store\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t@contextmanager\\n    14\\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\\n    15\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    16\\t    owned = []\\n    17\\t    try:\\n    18\\t        for conn in connections:\\n    19\\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\\n    20\\t                conn.execute('begin')\\n    21\\t                owned.append(conn)\\n    22\\t        yield\\n    23\\t    finally:\\n    24\\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\\n    25\\t            conn.rollback()\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\\n    30\\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    31\\t    cache = {}\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def item_of(input_id):\\n    34\\t        if input_id not in cache:\\n    35\\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\\n    36\\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\\n    37\\t        return cache[input_id]\\n    38\\t    return item_of\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\\n    42\\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's ladder as the new system's writer stored it (`clean_ladders`, written in the view's own call): the parsed\\n    47\\t    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\\n    48\\t    view. A row that is not readable JSON with a ladder, or two rows for one view, is refused.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49\\t    if not views_db.execute(\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where type='table' and name='clean_ladders'\\\").fetchone():\\n    50\\t        return 'no table'\\n    51\\t    rows = views_db.execute('select checked_answer from clean_ladders where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchall()\\n    52\\t    if not rows:\\n    53\\t        return 'no row'\\n    54\\t    if len(rows) > 1:\\n    55\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: {len(rows)} ladder rows for one view')\\n   100\\tdef view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\\n   101\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One view's complete record as of the bound (resolved; an omitted bound on a store with no completed day reads every\\n   102\\t    record, as before). A view not visible at the bound is refused (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   103\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n   104\\t    v = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   105\\t    if v is None:\\n   106\\t        raise KeyError(view_id)\\n   107\\t    if as_of is not None and not service.view_exists(views_db, v, as_of):\\n   108\\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n   109\\t    columns = {r[1] for r in views_db.execute('pragma table_info(rungs)')}\\n   110\\t    bounds = ', lo, hi' if {'lo', 'hi'} <= columns else ''          # a ledger written before keys has no bounds; the adapter then reads the prose\\n   111\\t    rungs = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute(f'select position, label, condition{bounds} from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n   112\\t    switches = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,))\\n   113\\t                if _visible(views_db, r['after_seq'], as_of)]\\n   114\\t    for switch in switches:\\n   115\\t        switch['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, switch['after_seq'])\\n   116\\t    judgements = []\\n   117\\t    for j in views_db.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   118\\t        if as_of is not None and j['publication_day'] > as_of:\\n   119\\t            continue\\n   120\\t        judgements.append({'id': str(j['judgement_id']), 'day': j['publication_day'], 'seq': j['seq'], 'rung': j['rung'], 'changed': bool(j['changed']),\\n   121\\t                           'why_changed': j['why_changed'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'cited': list(dict.fromkeys(json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json'] or '[]'))),   # each id once (UI contract uniqueItems); the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger holds one judgement citing an id twice\\n   122\\t                           'cited_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json'] or '[]'), 'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json'] or '[]'),\\n   123\\t                           'from_item': j['input_id']})\\n   124\\t    evidence = []\\n   125\\t    for e in views_db.execute('select e.*, l.seq as linked_seq from evidence_links l join evidence e on e.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by l.id', (view_id,)):\\n   126\\t        if not _visible(views_db, e['linked_seq'], as_of):\\n   127\\t            continue\\n   128\\t        sources = [dict(s) for s in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (e['evidence_id'],))\\n   129\\t                   if _visible(views_db, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   130\\t        replaced_by = views_db.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   131\\t        if replaced_by is not None and not _visible(views_db, replaced_by['seq'], as_of):\\n   132\\t            replaced_by = None\\n   133\\t        replaces = views_db.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   134\\t        if replaces and not _visible(views_db, replaces['seq'], as_of):\\n   135\\t            replaces = None\\n   136\\t        first = sources[0] if sources else {'input_id': e['created_from_input'], 'publication_day': '', 'seq': e['created_seq']}\\n   137\\t        item = item_of(first['input_id'])\\n   138\\t        evidence.append({'id': e['evidence_id'], 'one_line': e['one_line'], 'quote': e['quote'], 'tier': e['tier'], 'speaker': e['speaker'],\\n   139\\t                         'original_who': e['original_who'], 'original_day': e['original_day'], 'event_time': e['event_time'],\\n   140\\t                         'day': first['publication_day'] or item['publication_day'], 'seq': first['seq'], 'linked_seq': e['linked_seq'],\\n   141\\t                         'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, e['linked_seq']),\\n   142\\t                         'source': {'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'publisher_type': item['publisher_type'],\\n   143\\t                                    'category': item['category'], 'uri': item['source_uri']},\\n   144\\t                         'sources': [{'input_id': s['input_id'], 'day': s['publication_day'],\\n   145\\t                                      'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, s['seq']),\\n   146\\t                                      'source': item_of(s['input_id'])} for s in sources],\\n   147\\t                         'outlets': len(sources), 'replaced_by': {'new_evidence_id': replaced_by['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': replaced_by['said_day'],\\n   148\\t                                                               'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, replaced_by['seq'])} if replaced_by else None,\\n   225\\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   228\\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\\n   229\\t        if not as_of:\\n   230\\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\\n   231\\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   232\\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\\n   233\\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\\n   234\\t        if not view_ids:\\n   235\\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\\n   236\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\tdef view(conn, view_id):\\n    93\\t    row = conn.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n    94\\t    return dict(row) if row else None\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\tdef rungs_of(conn, view_id):\\n    98\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The rungs with their bounds when the ledger has them (keyed views); a ledger written before keys has no lo/hi columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    99\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n   100\\t    has_bounds = any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rows) or view_key(conn, view_id) is not None\\n   101\\t    return [dict(position=r['position'], label=r['label'], condition=r['condition'],\\n   102\\t                 **({'lo': r.get('lo'), 'hi': r.get('hi')} if has_bounds else {})) for r in rows]\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\tdef add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\\n   106\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's key (keyed-views-plan.md 2.1), written once with the view.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   107\\t    from .. import universe as _universe\\n   108\\t    from .identity import is_shared\\n   109\\t    scope_source = 'shared' if is_shared(key) else key.get('scope_source', 'model')      # D197: an aggregate's scope is wording\\n   110\\t    insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id=view_id, measure=key['measure'], scope=key.get('scope', ''), scope_key=_universe.scope_key(key.get('scope', '')),\\n   156\\t        conn.execute(\\\"alter table dependencies add column kind text default ''\\\")   # D694: every row written before reads ''\\n   157\\t\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\tdef view_key(conn, view_id):\\n   160\\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(view_keys)').fetchone():\\n   161\\t        return None\\n   162\\t    row = conn.execute('select * from view_keys where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   163\\t    if not row:\\n   164\\t        return None\\n   165\\t    key = dict(row)\\n   166\\t    if not key.get('scope_source'):\\n   167\\t        key['scope_source'] = 'none' if not key['scope'] else 'model'\\n   168\\t    return key\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t\\n   415\\t    return row['old_evidence_id'] if row else None\\n   416\\t\\n   417\\t\\n   418\\tdef evidence(conn, evidence_id):\\n   419\\t    row = conn.execute('select * from evidence where evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   420\\t    if not row:\\n   421\\t        return None\\n   422\\t    record = dict(row)\\n   423\\t    record['sources'] = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, location from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,))]\\n   424\\t    return record\\n   425\\t\\n   426\\t\\n   427\\tdef evidence_in_force(conn, view_id):\\n   428\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view and not replaced (history), each with its replaced predecessor when there is one and, since D202,\\n   429\\t    the piece it revises (both in force).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   430\\t    out = []\\n   431\\t    for row in conn.execute('select evidence_id from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   432\\t        evidence_id = row['evidence_id']\\n   433\\t        if is_replaced(conn, evidence_id):\\n   434\\t            continue\\n   435\\t        record = evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   436\\t        previous = predecessor_of(conn, evidence_id)\\n   437\\t        record['replaced'] = evidence(conn, previous) if previous else None\\n   438\\t        revised = revision_of(conn, evidence_id)\\n   439\\t        record['revises'] = evidence(conn, revised) if revised else None\\n   440\\t        record['same_as'] = [x for x in same_claim_group(conn, evidence_id) if not is_replaced(conn, x)]\\n   441\\t        out.append(record)\\n   442\\t    return out\\n   443\\t\\n   444\\t\\n   445\\tdef views_linked_to(conn, evidence_id):\\n   446\\t    return [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id from evidence_links where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,))]\\n   447\\t\\n   448\\t\\n   449\\tdef evidence_ids_under(conn, view_id):\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files --hidden --no-ignore poc/data | rg '(views|items[\\\"'^/]*)'\\\"\\\\\\\\.sqlite\\\"'$'\\\"' | rg 'run/old|items-comparison|served' | head -40; rg -n 'served ledger|served.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74*.md | head -14\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:11:| **5. Diagnostic columns** | **Closed.** The two optional judgement columns are read only where present, and the report records their absence. I verified that the served ledger has `reasons` and `why_changed` and lacks both `implied_outcome` and `reference`. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339) |\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:16:**Claude is right about what the production extraction request sees.** For an existing question, it sends the ID, object, due day, question and a description of what evidence belongs there. It sends no stored rung, rung label or judged position. The response schema asks the model to *write* labels for newly proposed questions. `research_context.Reader` really does load stored rungs and the latest judgement, but its expanded record is not sent by `extraction.read_item`. I also checked the historical archive because the served ledger used extraction v18. Across its 1,819 extraction requests, the 43,895 displayed thesis lines contained the ID, object, focus, due day and question. [placement.py:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:19) · [placement.py:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:59) · [extraction.py:399](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:399) · [extraction.py:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:88) · [extraction.py:460](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:460) · [research_context.py:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:49) · [research_context.py:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:95) · [README.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:114)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:28:5. **Make the four-store acceptance runnable.** Step 7 asks for `judgements.implied_outcome` and `reference` on every store. I checked the served ledger’s actual schema. It has neither column. Read the available diagnostic columns and report the two as absent on that ledger. Otherwise the specified acceptance can fail on a valid package before it finishes. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:261) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) · [store.py:152](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:152)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.stream:38:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c '\\nimport sqlite3,pathlib\\nroot=pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\")\\nfor p in sorted(root.glob(\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-*/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\"))+list(root.glob(\\\\\\\"served-*/views.sqlite\\\\\\\")):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\n print(p, c.execute(\\\\\\\"select count(*),count(original_day),count(original_who),count(quote),count(speaker) from evidence\\\\\\\").fetchone())\\n if \\\\\\\"old-1\\\\\\\" in str(p):\\n  print(c.execute(\\\\\\\"select evidence_id,substr(one_line,1,180),substr(quote,1,220) from evidence where evidence_id in (?,?,?)\\\\\\\",(\\\\\\\"e2295\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"e1865\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"e3597\\\\\\\")).fetchall())\\n  print(c.execute(\\\\\\\"select view_id,publication_day,substr(implied_outcome,1,180) from judgements where judgement_id=1580\\\\\\\").fetchall())\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite (5390, 5390, 5390, 5390, 5390)\\n[('e1865', 'The author identifies firm SpaceX procurement commitments and NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into FY2028 as bullish confirmation conditions.', 'Bullish confirmation would require firm procurement commitments for the SpaceX buildout and continued NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into fiscal 2028.'), ('e2295', 'Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year.', 'Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.'), ('e3597', 'The author says analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of about $390 billion in calendar 2027 and over $550 billion in calendar 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.', 'Analysts see revenue reaching about $390 billion in 2027 and more than $550 billion in 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.')]\\n[('v8', '2026-09-20', 'About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint and 92.5% recent Data Center mix, plus ')]\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite (5102, 5102, 5102, 5102, 5102)\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite (5447, 5447, 5447, 5447, 5447)\\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite (4298, 4298, 4298, 4298, 4298)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n\\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n\\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n\\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n\\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n   word for it is already given.\\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n\\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n\\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\nany one step's own score.\\n\\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n\\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n\\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n\\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n\\n**Evidence:**\\n\\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n\\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n\\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n\\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n\\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n  system (D263).\\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n  competition or pricing\\\".\\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n  of the previous filing topic).\\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n\\n## 5. What to do\\n\\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n\\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n     the existing rule).\\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n\\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n\\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n  measured and reported apart.\\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n  counted after.\\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n    question\\\";\\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n    or no question uses);\\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n    ones that matter one by one.\\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n      facts must not fall.\\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n      what was measured.\\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n\\n## 7. Process (no drift)\\n\\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n  sentence, in both directions.\\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n\\n## 8. Steps and where we are\\n\\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n\\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n\\n- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md\\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74g.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t## What to review\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n     8\\trelease. The governing documents:\\n     9\\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\\n    10\\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\\n    11\\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\tCode that the design reuses:\\n    14\\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\\n    15\\t  `ladder_bands`;\\n    16\\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\\n    17\\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\\n    18\\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\\n    19\\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\\n    20\\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## Questions\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\\n    25\\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\\n    26\\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\\n    27\\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t   Name any path with a stored example.\\n    30\\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\\n    31\\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\\n    32\\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\\n    33\\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\\n    34\\t   forecast restated in different words?\\n    35\\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\\n    36\\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\\n    37\\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\\n    38\\t   - groups left out;\\n    39\\t   - the sweep floor.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t   Decide each.\\n    42\\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\\n    45\\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\\n     1\\t**Not ready to build.** Revision 7 closes the date finding. Two ways to overwrite a file remain in the report-writing steps.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t1. **74f date finding — closed.** The builder rejects `20260825` before querying the ledger. The package checker also requires `YYYY-MM-DD`. Test 16 places evidence on both sides of August 25 and checks that the canonical date exports only the earlier evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:116) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:359](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:359)\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t2. **74f input-overwrite finding — still open in `check`.** On this Mac, I verified read-only that `old-1/prod/views.sqlite` and `old-1/prod/VIEWS.SQLITE` produce different `realpath` strings and identify the same file. An items database named `Release.report.json` can therefore pass the path comparison for `check release`, which then rewrites `release.report.json`. Compare the existing report’s file identity with both inputs using `os.path.samefile`. Extend test 18 on a case-insensitive volume to require refusal and an unchanged database hash. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:351](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:351) · [live_lock.py:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40)\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t3. **Additional blocker — `build` can overwrite a file created while it runs.** The builder checks that the report name is free at startup. If another process creates a file there while the package is being checked, the final `os.replace` overwrites it. Publish the build’s report with an atomic operation that refuses an occupied destination. The decisive test places a marker file there immediately before the report write and requires the marker to survive, the checked package to remain available, and the command to exit 2. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:182](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:182) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:188](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:188)\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tI found no further serious blocker in slice 1.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '309,460p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   309\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   310\\t\\n   311\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   312\\tits row above:\\n   313\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   314\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   315\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   316\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   317\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   318\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   319\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   320\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   321\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   322\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   323\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   324\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   325\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   326\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   327\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   328\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   329\\t9. **Package:**\\n   330\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   331\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   332\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   333\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   334\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   335\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   336\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   337\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   338\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   339\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   340\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   341\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   342\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\\n   343\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   344\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   345\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   346\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   347\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   348\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   349\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   350\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   351\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   352\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   353\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   354\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   355\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   356\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   357\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   358\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   359\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   360\\t      and inode).\\n   361\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   362\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   363\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\\n   364\\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\\n   365\\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   366\\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file at\\n   367\\t    the report name. The command exits 2, the marker is unchanged, and the published package passes `check`.\\n   368\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   369\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   370\\t15. **Files:**\\n   371\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   372\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   373\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   374\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   375\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   376\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   377\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   378\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   379\\t\\n   380\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   381\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   382\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   383\\t- the event test removed;\\n   384\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   385\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   386\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   387\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   388\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   389\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   390\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   391\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   392\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   393\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   394\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   395\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   396\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   397\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   398\\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\\n   399\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   400\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   401\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   402\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   403\\t\\n   404\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   405\\t\\n   406\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   407\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   408\\t\\n   409\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   410\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   411\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   412\\t\\n   413\\tThe steps:\\n   414\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   415\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   416\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   417\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   418\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   419\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   420\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   421\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   422\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   423\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   424\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   425\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   426\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   427\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   428\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   429\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   430\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   431\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   432\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   433\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   434\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   435\\t\\n   436\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   437\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   438\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   439\\t\\n   440\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   441\\t\\n   442\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   443\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   444\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   445\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   446\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   447\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   448\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   449\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   450\\t  judged position.\\n   451\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   452\\t  reproduces.\\n   453\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   454\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   455\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   456\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   457\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   458\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   459\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   460\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '154,308p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   154\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   155\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   156\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   157\\t\\n   158\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   159\\t  compared.\\n   160\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   161\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   162\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   163\\t  else.\\n   164\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   165\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   166\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   167\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   168\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   171\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   172\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   173\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   174\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   175\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   176\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   177\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   178\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   179\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   180\\t\\n   181\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   182\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   183\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   184\\t     guarantee;\\n   185\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   186\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   187\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   188\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   189\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   190\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   191\\t     nothing;\\n   192\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), `os.link` it to\\n   193\\t     `<out>.report.json`, then remove the temporary file. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name, and the\\n   194\\t     temporary file is removed either way.\\n   195\\t\\n   196\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   197\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   198\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   199\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   200\\t  - **After publication** (step 8 fails, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and checked, and whatever is at the report name\\n   201\\t    is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run `check` to write it\\\".\\n   202\\t\\n   203\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   204\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   205\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   206\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. An existing report must be\\n   207\\t  removed by the user before `check` writes a new one; otherwise `check` exits 2 after printing. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   208\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   209\\t- **The report:**\\n   210\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   211\\t  - counts per class;\\n   212\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   213\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   214\\t  - bytes;\\n   215\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   220\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   221\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   222\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   223\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   224\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   225\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   226\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   227\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   228\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   229\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   230\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   231\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   232\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   233\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   234\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   235\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   236\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   237\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   238\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   239\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   240\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   241\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   242\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   243\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   244\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   245\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   246\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   247\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   248\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   249\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   250\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   251\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   252\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   255\\t\\n   256\\tReaders of the package:\\n   257\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   258\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   259\\t- the tests.\\n   260\\t\\n   261\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   264\\t|---|---|---|\\n   265\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   266\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   267\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   268\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   269\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   270\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   271\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   272\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   273\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   274\\t\\n   275\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   276\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   277\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   278\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   279\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   280\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   281\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   282\\t\\n   283\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   284\\t\\n   285\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   286\\t|---|---|\\n   287\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   288\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   289\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   290\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   291\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   292\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   293\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   294\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   295\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   296\\t\\n   297\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   298\\t\\n   299\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   300\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   301\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   302\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   303\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   304\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   305\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   306\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   307\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   308\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,153p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 8, for council round 74h. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\\n    43\\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\\n    44\\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\\n    45\\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\\n    46\\t  pause.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\\n    49\\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\\n    50\\t  but the stores compare days as text.\\n    51\\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\\n    54\\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\\n    55\\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\\n    56\\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\\n    57\\t  anything exists there.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\\n    60\\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\\n    61\\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t## 0. Scope\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    66\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    67\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    68\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    69\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    70\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    71\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    72\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    73\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    74\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    75\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    76\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    77\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    78\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    79\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    80\\t  - any model call;\\n    81\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t## 1. What is built\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t- **Constants:**\\n    88\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    89\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    90\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    91\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    92\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    95\\t  |---|---|\\n    96\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    97\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    98\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n    99\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n   100\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n   101\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n   104\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n   105\\t    only when the table exists;\\n   106\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n   107\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n   108\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n   109\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   110\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   111\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   112\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   113\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   114\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   115\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   116\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   117\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   118\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   119\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   120\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   121\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   122\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   123\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   124\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   125\\t  - Value checks:\\n   126\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   127\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   128\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   129\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   130\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   131\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   132\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   133\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   134\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   135\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   136\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   137\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   138\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   139\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   140\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   141\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   142\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   143\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   144\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   145\\t\\n   146\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   147\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   148\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   149\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   150\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   151\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   152\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   153\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '46,154p;169,282p;490,541p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\\n    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   146\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\\n   147\\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\\n   148\\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   150\\t    out = []\\n   151\\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\\n   152\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   153\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   154\\t            continue\\n   169\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   170\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   171\\t            continue\\n   172\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of):\\n   173\\t            continue\\n   174\\t        out.append(view(conn, record['view_id'], as_of, record=record))\\n   175\\t    return out\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\tdef dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   179\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's dependencies recorded on or before the day, each pointing at the target resolved on or before it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   180\\t    out = []\\n   181\\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\\n   182\\t        if not visible(conn, dep['seq'], as_of):\\n   183\\t            continue\\n   184\\t        target = dep['depends_on']\\n   185\\t        for res in conn.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc', (dep['dependency_id'],)):\\n   186\\t            if visible(conn, res['seq'], as_of):\\n   187\\t                target = res['resolved_to']\\n   188\\t                break\\n   189\\t        \n... 419596 bytes omitted ...\ncannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n   145\\t  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n   146\\t  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n   147\\t    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n   148\\t    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n   149\\t      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n   150\\t    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n   151\\t      facts must not fall.\\n   152\\t  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n   153\\t    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n   154\\t      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n   155\\t      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n   156\\t      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n   157\\t    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n   158\\t      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n   159\\t    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n   160\\t      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n   161\\t      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n   162\\t      what was measured.\\n   163\\t  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n   164\\t    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n   165\\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n   166\\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n   167\\t\\n   168\\t## 7. Process (no drift)\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n   171\\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n   172\\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n   173\\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n   174\\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n   175\\t  sentence, in both directions.\\n   176\\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n   177\\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\t## 8. Steps and where we are\\n   180\\t\\n   181\\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n   182\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   183\\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n   184\\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n   185\\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n   186\\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n   187\\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n   188\\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n   189\\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n   190\\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n   191\\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\t- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n   196\\t- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   197\\t- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   198\\t- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   199\\t- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   200\\t- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n   201\\t- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 3, for council round 74c. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t## 0. Scope\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    31\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    32\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    33\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    34\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    35\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    36\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    37\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    38\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    39\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    40\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    41\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    42\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    43\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    44\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    45\\t  - any model call;\\n    46\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t## 1. What is built\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t- **Constants:**\\n    53\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    54\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    55\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    56\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    57\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    60\\t  |---|---|\\n    61\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    62\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    63\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n    64\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    65\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    66\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n    69\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n    70\\t    only when the table exists;\\n    71\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n    72\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    73\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    74\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n    75\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, refuses a store with no default day, and validates the bound with\\n    76\\t    `date.fromisoformat`;\\n    77\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\\n    78\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n    79\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views`;\\n    80\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n    81\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n    82\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n    83\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n    84\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n    85\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n    86\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n    87\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n    88\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n    89\\t  - Value checks:\\n    90\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is an ISO date;\\n    91\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n    92\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n    93\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n    94\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n    95\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n    96\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n    97\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n    98\\t  - **The bound.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller. The builder passes the bound it resolved. `check` passes the package's\\n    99\\t    `as_of` through `service.resolve_bound` (which refuses a day after the last completed day) and requires it to be no later than\\n   100\\t    `service.default_as_of`, which covers a legacy ledger with no completed days. The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   101\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   102\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   103\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list, in `created_seq` order, and so are each question's evidence\\n   104\\t    (link order) and sources (row order). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   107\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   108\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   109\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   110\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   111\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   112\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   113\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   114\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   115\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   116\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   119\\t  compared.\\n   120\\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\\n   121\\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`;\\n   122\\t  - creates a staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   123\\t    prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so no other build can own it;\\n   124\\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` there;\\n   125\\t  - returns the staged path. It does not move it.\\n   126\\t- **`publish_staged(staged, out_dir)`:** moves the staged folder into place with `os.rename`, after refusing an existing `out_dir`.\\n   127\\t  If another build created `out_dir` in between, the rename fails on its non-empty folder, and this build refuses. Only the\\n   128\\t  invocation that created a staging folder removes it.\\n   129\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   130\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   131\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   132\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   133\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   134\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   135\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   136\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   137\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   140\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   141\\t  1. resolve the bound once (`service.resolve_bound`, `date.fromisoformat`);\\n   142\\t  2. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   143\\t  3. `write_package` to its own staging folder;\\n   144\\t  4. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   145\\t  5. `publish_staged`, then write `<out>.report.json` beside the package (through a temporary file and `os.replace`);\\n   146\\t  6. on `ReleaseRefused`, or on an `OSError` while writing, checking or moving, remove only the staging folder it created, print\\n   147\\t     the reason and exit non-zero. No final folder exists, and another build's staging folder or package is never touched.\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   150\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's `as_of`\\n   151\\t  validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\\n   152\\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   153\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   154\\t- **The report:**\\n   155\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   156\\t  - counts per class;\\n   157\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   158\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   159\\t  - bytes;\\n   160\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   163\\t\\n   164\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   165\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   166\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   167\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   168\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   169\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   170\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   171\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   172\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   173\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   174\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   175\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   176\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   177\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   178\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   179\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   180\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   181\\t| `--out` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\\n   182\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   183\\t| `OSError` while writing, checking or moving | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   184\\t| Crash while staging | this build's uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. It blocks no later build, and the user may delete it | staging only | — |\\n   185\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   186\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages in its own folder. The first rename wins; the second refuses on the existing folder and removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   187\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   188\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   189\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   190\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   191\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\tReaders of the package:\\n   196\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   197\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   198\\t- the tests.\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   203\\t|---|---|---|\\n   204\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   205\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   206\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   207\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   208\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   209\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   210\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   211\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   212\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   213\\t\\n   214\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   215\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   216\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   217\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   218\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   219\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   220\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   225\\t|---|---|\\n   226\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   227\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   228\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   229\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   230\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   231\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   232\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   233\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   234\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   235\\t\\n   236\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   239\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   240\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   241\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   242\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   243\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   244\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   245\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   246\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   247\\t\\n   248\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   249\\t\\n   250\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   251\\tits row above:\\n   252\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   253\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   254\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   255\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   256\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   257\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   258\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   259\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   260\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   261\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   262\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   263\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   264\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   265\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   266\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   267\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   268\\t9. **Package:**\\n   269\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   270\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   271\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   272\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   273\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   274\\t   - an existing `--out` or staging folder is refused.\\n   275\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   276\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   277\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   278\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   279\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`.\\n   280\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\\n   281\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the builder.**\\n   282\\t    - Fault injection: the test wraps `release.release_export`, as the builder calls it in-process, so that it returns the real\\n   283\\t      export with one evidence `one_line` replaced. The closed set still holds.\\n   284\\t    - Expected: exit non-zero, no `--out`, and the builder's staging folder removed.\\n   285\\t    - Removing the builder's staged check must make this test fail. This is the one fake in the suite: an injected writer fault, not\\n   286\\t      an external service.\\n   287\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package, then the items database copied with one referenced item deleted:\\n   288\\t    `check` refuses, and the package is left in place.\\n   289\\t14. **Two builds aimed at one `--out`.** The second refuses. The winner's package passes `check`, and no staging folder of the winner\\n   290\\t    is removed by the loser.\\n   291\\t15. **Files:** a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails, and so does a data file with a repeated `one_line` member name.\\n   292\\t16. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   295\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   296\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   297\\t- the event test removed;\\n   298\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   299\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   300\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   301\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   302\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   303\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   304\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   305\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   306\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   307\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package`;\\n   308\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   309\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   310\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   311\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   312\\t\\n   313\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   314\\t\\n   315\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   316\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   319\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   320\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\tThe steps:\\n   323\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   324\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   325\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   326\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   327\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   328\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   329\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   330\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   331\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   332\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   333\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   334\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   335\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   336\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   337\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   338\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   339\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   340\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   341\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   342\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   343\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   344\\t\\n   345\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   346\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   347\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   348\\t\\n   349\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   350\\t\\n   351\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   352\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   353\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   354\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   355\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   356\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   357\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   358\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   359\\t  judged position.\\n   360\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   361\\t  reproduces.\\n   362\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   363\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   364\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   365\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   366\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   367\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   368\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   369\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | head -119'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 3, for council round 74c. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t## 0. Scope\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    31\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    32\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    33\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    34\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    35\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    36\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    37\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    38\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    39\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    40\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    41\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    42\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    43\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    44\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    45\\t  - any model call;\\n    46\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t## 1. What is built\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t- **Constants:**\\n    53\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    54\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    55\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    56\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    57\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    60\\t  |---|---|\\n    61\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    62\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    63\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n    64\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    65\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    66\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n    69\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n    70\\t    only when the table exists;\\n    71\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n    72\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    73\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    74\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n    75\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, refuses a store with no default day, and validates the bound with\\n    76\\t    `date.fromisoformat`;\\n    77\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\\n    78\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n    79\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views`;\\n    80\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n    81\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n    82\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n    83\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n    84\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n    85\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n    86\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n    87\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n    88\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n    89\\t  - Value checks:\\n    90\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is an ISO date;\\n    91\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n    92\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n    93\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n    94\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n    95\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n    96\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n    97\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n    98\\t  - **The bound.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller. The builder passes the bound it resolved. `check` passes the package's\\n    99\\t    `as_of` through `service.resolve_bound` (which refuses a day after the last completed day) and requires it to be no later than\\n   100\\t    `service.default_as_of`, which covers a legacy ledger with no completed days. The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   101\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   102\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   103\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list, in `created_seq` order, and so are each question's evidence\\n   104\\t    (link order) and sources (row order). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   107\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   108\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   109\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   110\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   111\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   112\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   113\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   114\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   115\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   116\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   119\\t  compared.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md | cut -c1-650; cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | tail -n +49'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\\\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\\\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\\\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\\\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\\\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\\\"自己的量，别的期间\\\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"跑验收\\\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\\\"中国份额归零\\\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"都做\\\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n\\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n\\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n\\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n\\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n  system (D263).\\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n  competition or pricing\\\".\\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n  of the previous filing topic).\\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n\\n## 5. What to do\\n\\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n\\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n     the existing rule).\\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n\\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n\\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n  measured and reported apart.\\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n  counted after.\\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n    question\\\";\\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n    or no question uses);\\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n    ones that matter one by one.\\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n      facts must not fall.\\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n      what was measured.\\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n\\n## 7. Process (no drift)\\n\\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n  sentence, in both directions.\\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n\\n## 8. Steps and where we are\\n\\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n\\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n\\n- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n -A7 '\\\"'^##.*D(726|756|757|758)'\\\"\\\\\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '125,160p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n10992-\\n10993-- **The questions** (after D725):\\n10994-  - \\\"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\\\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\\n10995-    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\\n10996-    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\\n10997-  - \\\"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\\\" Options: 同意\\n10998-    (recommended); 暂不定.\\n--\\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" into the first release\\n11800-\\n11801-- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23/`, the\\n11802-  verdict sealed in `verdict.json`):\\n11803-  - STOP, complete. Joint usable in 3 of 9 pairs against the registered 8; separate 0 of 9.\\n11804-  - 5 published defects, all singleton deciding gaps (O 1, E 1, S 3): unsized adjustments decide the band.\\n11805-  - Spend $0.3339 of the $0.50 cap.\\n11806-  - The checker refused 22 of 36 first attempts (61.1%): 21 carry a luna violation of a stated format rule, and 1 is a\\n--\\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n11824-\\n11825-- **The question** (after D755): \\\"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\\\"\\n11826-  - Options:\\n11827-    - \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\": the council's consensus;\\n11828-    - \\\"换更强的模型再小测一次\\\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\\n11829-    - \\\"先停，我想谈谈\\\".\\n11830-- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\".\\n--\\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n11843-\\n11844-- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \\\"Forecast\\n11845-  unavailable\\\" (D756). D726 says it \\\"is built with the release work, which is not started\\\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\\n11846-  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\\n11847-- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\\n11848-  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\\n11849-  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\\n--\\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n11868-\\n11869-- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \\\"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\\n11870-  Production 方向去走了\\\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \\\"同意\\\"; D756 \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\"). D757 left two\\n11871-  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\\n11872-- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\\n11873-  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\\n11874-     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\\n   125\\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\\n   126\\t  same key or rule.\\n   127\\t- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\\n   128\\t  of prompts and documents.\\n   129\\t- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\\n   130\\t  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\\n   131\\t  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\\n   132\\t- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\\n   133\\t  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\\n   134\\t  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\\n   135\\t- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\\n   136\\t  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\\n   137\\t  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\\n   138\\t- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\\n   139\\t  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \\\"now\\\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\\n   140\\t- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\\n   141\\t- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\\n   142\\t  justifies a dependency.\\n   143\\t- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\t## 4. Tests\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\\n   148\\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\\n   149\\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\\n   150\\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\\n   151\\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\\n   152\\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\\n   153\\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\\n   154\\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\\n   155\\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\\n   156\\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\\n   157\\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\\n   158\\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\\n   159\\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\\\"never called\\\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\\n   160\\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | head -270'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"Read-only answers over the views ledger, as of a calendar day (docs/poc/service.md).\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tNothing here reads the clock (D12, D13): every function takes `as_of`, a day, and the default is the ledger's last\\n     4\\tcompleted day. A row is visible as of a day when the sequence number it was written under belongs to an item or a\\n     5\\tdaily round dated on or before that day. Nothing here writes.\\n     6\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     7\\timport json\\n     8\\timport re\\n     9\\timport sqlite3\\n    10\\tfrom decimal import Decimal\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tfrom . import vocabulary\\n    13\\tfrom .views import store\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\tTIER_FACT = vocabulary.TIERS[0]          # 'fact'; a legacy ledger's '发生的事' compares equal through vocabulary.canonical\\n    16\\tCOMPARATORS = ('>=', '<', '=')\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tdef open_ledger(path):\\n    20\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A read-only connection to a views database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    21\\t    return store.open_read_only(path)\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tdef default_as_of(conn):\\n    25\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    26\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    30\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\\n    31\\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def __init__(self):\\n    34\\t        super().__init__(\\\"the store's first day has not completed\\\")\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    38\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\\n    41\\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\\n    42\\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\\n    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   146\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\\n   147\\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\\n   148\\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   150\\t    out = []\\n   151\\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\\n   152\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   153\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   154\\t            continue\\n   155\\t        is_open = is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)\\n   156\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open:\\n   157\\t            continue\\n   158\\t        out.append({'view_id': record['view_id'], 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   159\\t                    'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'open': is_open,\\n   160\\t                    'dependencies': [d['view_id'] for d in dependencies(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)], 'dependants': dependants(conn, record['view_id'], as_of)})\\n   161\\t    return out\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t\\n   164\\tdef views(conn, object_id=None, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   165\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   166\\t    rows = conn.execute('select * from views' + (' where object_id=?' if object_id else '') + ' order by created_seq', (object_id,) if object_id else ()).fetchall()\\n   167\\t    out = []\\n   168\\t    for record in rows:\\n   169\\t        record = dict(record)\\n   170\\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   171\\t            continue\\n   172\\t        if not include_closed and not is_open_as_of(conn, record['view_id'], as_of):\\n   173\\t            continue\\n   174\\t        out.append(view(conn, record['view_id'], as_of, record=record))\\n   175\\t    return out\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\tdef dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   179\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's dependencies recorded on or before the day, each pointing at the target resolved on or before it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   180\\t    out = []\\n   181\\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\\n   182\\t        if not visible(conn, dep['seq'], as_of):\\n   183\\t            continue\\n   184\\t        target = dep['depends_on']\\n   185\\t        for res in conn.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc', (dep['dependency_id'],)):\\n   186\\t            if visible(conn, res['seq'], as_of):\\n   187\\t                target = res['resolved_to']\\n   188\\t                break\\n   189\\t        out.append({'view_id': target, 'direction': dep['direction'], 'wait_chain_view_id': dep['wait_chain_view_id'], 'wait_year': dep['wait_year'], 'since_day': day_of_seq(conn, dep['seq'])})\\n   190\\t    return out\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\tdef dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   194\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The views recorded on or before the day as depending on this one (directly or by a resolution).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   195\\t    direct = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   196\\t    resolved = [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select d.view_id, r.seq from dependency_resolutions r join dependencies d on d.dependency_id=r.dependency_id where r.resolved_to=?', (view_id,)) if visible(conn, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   197\\t    return sorted(set(direct + resolved))\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\\n   201\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   202\\t    record = record or store.view(conn, view_id)\\n   203\\t    if not record or not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   204\\t        return None\\n   205\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   206\\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   207\\t    if state:\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   269\\t    arrivals = {}\\n   270\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '23,105p;208,275p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    23\\t\\n    24\\tdef default_as_of(conn):\\n    25\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    26\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    30\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\\n    31\\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def __init__(self):\\n    34\\t        super().__init__(\\\"the store's first day has not completed\\\")\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\\n    38\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\\n    41\\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\\n    42\\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\\n    49\\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\\n    50\\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    54\\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\n    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   208\\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\\n   209\\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\\n   210\\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\\n   211\\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\\n   212\\t    return {\\n   213\\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\\n   214\\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\\n   215\\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\\n   216\\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\\n   217\\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\\n   218\\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\\n   219\\t    }\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t# ---------- evidence\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\n   258\\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\\n   259\\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\\n   260\\t    judgements = []\\n   261\\t    previous = None\\n   262\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   263\\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\\n   264\\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\\n   265\\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\\n   266\\t        previous = row['rung']\\n   267\\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\\n   268\\t            judgements.append(entry)\\n   269\\t    arrivals = {}\\n   270\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\\n   271\\t        day = day_of_seq(conn, link['seq'])\\n   272\\t        if day and from_day <= day <= to_day:\\n   273\\t            piece = store.evidence(conn, link['evidence_id'])\\n   274\\t            bucket = arrivals.setdefault(day, {'evidence': 0, 'facts': 0})\\n   275\\t            bucket['evidence'] += 1\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:48:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md | tail -31'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    22\\t   - fixtures that separate every branch, with a condition-only resolved number, unresolved numbers with and without a key, the\\n    23\\t     served ledger's \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\\n    24\\t   - a manifest-prose mutant;\\n    25\\t   - a mutant that writes judgement text into `one_line`;\\n    26\\t   - writer refusal exercised through the builder;\\n    27\\t   - the known leaks exported at 2026-08-25 and 2026-08-28.\\n    28\\t9. **The open points:** no idea submission, its acceptance carried forward; `object` and `kind` dropped; groups out; floor removed.\\n    29\\t10. **The decisive acceptance case,** as stated in `codex-r74.md`. It also keeps `e3597`'s genuine $390 billion analyst quote as a\\n    30\\t    control.\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\t## Disputed: rewriting evidence summaries that state a calculated figure\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t`codex-r74.md` §1 asks the release to use the source wording where a summary introduces a calculated figure (`e3238`: \\\"more than\\n    35\\t$40 billion\\\" from \\\"more than double\\\"). I propose keeping the summary as extraction stored it, for four reasons.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t- **What D726 withholds is the judge's output:** the band, the forecast text and the history (Alex: \\\"档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'\\\").\\n    38\\t  The evidence is the extraction step's reading of a source, and extraction runs on the frozen production prompt (v74i).\\n    39\\t- **Extraction never sees the system's forecast.** The request lists each open question only as id, object, due day, question and a\\n    40\\t  \\\"takes\\\" line (`src/hivemind/placement.py:59-61`, `:19-42`; `src/hivemind/extraction.py:398-400`). No rung, label or judged position\\n    41\\t  is shown. A summary therefore cannot echo our forecast; its figures come from the item.\\n    42\\t- **The measured rule would mostly remove harmless text.** \\\"Every number in the summary must be in the quote\\\" fails on 25.6%, 25.2%\\n    43\\t  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\\n    44\\t  (`scratchpad oneline_census.py`). In a random sample of 24 failures, 23 are context made explicit: a year for \\\"this year\\\", a date\\n    45\\t  for \\\"Monday\\\", \\\"Q3\\\", \\\"FY2027\\\", a product name such as \\\"H200\\\", an amount from the previous sentence. One (served `e2798`) restates\\n    46\\t  \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\". The rule would be a patch on the extraction module, which this\\n    47\\t  slice has not taken up (AGENTS, \\\"Authority and scope\\\").\\n    48\\t- **\\\"Amounts as quoted\\\"** in the design meant the release computes or converts nothing. Revision 2 says so in those words. The\\n    49\\t  property (a summary can restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source) is disclosed in the design, not built.\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\tIf the council still disagrees, AGENTS says to take the cheaper, reversible course. Keeping the stored summary is cheaper and is\\n    52\\treversible: the field can be dropped from the allow-list in a later version.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:60:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_30\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '14,33p;225,249p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '148,168p'; rg -n '\\\"'^CREATE TABLE.*(view|judgement)|create table if not exists (judgements|views|evidence_links)'\\\"' -i src/hivemind/views/store.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    14\\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\\n    15\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    16\\t    owned = []\\n    17\\t    try:\\n    18\\t        for conn in connections:\\n    19\\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\\n    20\\t                conn.execute('begin')\\n    21\\t                owned.append(conn)\\n    22\\t        yield\\n    23\\t    finally:\\n    24\\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\\n    25\\t            conn.rollback()\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\\n    30\\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    31\\t    cache = {}\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def item_of(input_id):\\n   225\\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   228\\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\\n   229\\t        if not as_of:\\n   230\\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\\n   231\\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   232\\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\\n   233\\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\\n   234\\t        if not view_ids:\\n   235\\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\\n   236\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\\n   148\\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\\n   149\\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\\n   150\\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\\n   151\\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\\n   152\\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\\n   153\\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\\n   154\\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\\n   155\\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\\n   156\\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\\n   157\\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\\n   158\\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\\n   159\\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\\\"never called\\\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\\n   160\\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\\n   161\\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\\n   162\\t  unexercised, not passed.\\n   163\\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\\n   164\\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\\n   165\\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\\n   166\\t  the inner function with every argument set.\\n   167\\t\\n   168\\t## 5. Verification\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:63:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_32\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '174,190p;268,312p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   174\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   175\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   176\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   177\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   178\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   179\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   180\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   181\\t| `--out` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\\n   182\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   183\\t| `OSError` while writing, checking or moving | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   184\\t| Crash while staging | this build's uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. It blocks no later build, and the user may delete it | staging only | — |\\n   185\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   186\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages in its own folder. The first rename wins; the second refuses on the existing folder and removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   187\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   188\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   189\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   190\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   268\\t9. **Package:**\\n   269\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   270\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   271\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   272\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   273\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   274\\t   - an existing `--out` or staging folder is refused.\\n   275\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   276\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   277\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   278\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   279\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`.\\n   280\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\\n   281\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the builder.**\\n   282\\t    - Fault injection: the test wraps `release.release_export`, as the builder calls it in-process, so that it returns the real\\n   283\\t      export with one evidence `one_line` replaced. The closed set still holds.\\n   284\\t    - Expected: exit non-zero, no `--out`, and the builder's staging folder removed.\\n   285\\t    - Removing the builder's staged check must make this test fail. This is the one fake in the suite: an injected writer fault, not\\n   286\\t      an external service.\\n   287\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package, then the items database copied with one referenced item deleted:\\n   288\\t    `check` refuses, and the package is left in place.\\n   289\\t14. **Two builds aimed at one `--out`.** The second refuses. The winner's package passes `check`, and no staging folder of the winner\\n   290\\t    is removed by the loser.\\n   291\\t15. **Files:** a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails, and so does a data file with a repeated `one_line` member name.\\n   292\\t16. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   295\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   296\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   297\\t- the event test removed;\\n   298\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   299\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   300\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   301\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   302\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   303\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   304\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   305\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   306\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   307\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package`;\\n   308\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   309\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   310\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   311\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   312\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.stream:72:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sqlite3 'file:poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite?immutable=1&mode=ro' 'select view_id,created_seq,rowid from views where created_seq=8 order by created_seq,rowid;'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '118,154p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"v2|8|2\\nv3|8|3\\n   118\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   119\\t  compared.\\n   120\\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\\n   121\\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`;\\n   122\\t  - creates a staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   123\\t    prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so no other build can own it;\\n   124\\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` there;\\n   125\\t  - returns the staged path. It does not move it.\\n   126\\t- **`publish_staged(staged, out_dir)`:** moves the staged folder into place with `os.rename`, after refusing an existing `out_dir`.\\n   127\\t  If another build created `out_dir` in between, the rename fails on its non-empty folder, and this build refuses. Only the\\n   128\\t  invocation that created a staging folder removes it.\\n   129\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   130\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   131\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   132\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   133\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   134\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   135\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   136\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   137\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   140\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   141\\t  1. resolve the bound once (`service.resolve_bound`, `date.fromisoformat`);\\n   142\\t  2. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   143\\t  3. `write_package` to its own staging folder;\\n   144\\t  4. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   145\\t  5. `publish_staged`, then write `<out>.report.json` beside the package (through a temporary file and `os.replace`);\\n   146\\t  6. on `ReleaseRefused`, or on an `OSError` while writing, checking or moving, remove only the staging folder it created, print\\n   147\\t     the reason and exit non-zero. No final folder exists, and another build's staging folder or package is never touched.\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   150\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's `as_of`\\n   151\\t  validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\\n   152\\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   153\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   154\\t- **The report:**\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design for review (council round 74). No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The\\n     4\\tbehaviour is fixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first\\n     5\\tslice.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t## 0. Scope\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0.**\\n    10\\t  - The exporter `release_export`, its self-check, the package writer and the package check.\\n    11\\t  - The release builder, which calls the exporter directly.\\n    12\\t  - Tests and mutants.\\n    13\\t  - The $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    14\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    15\\t  trials. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen. This completes D756's screen check.\\n    16\\t- **Proposed for round 74: no idea submission in the release.** Today the idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step:\\n    17\\t  - `judged`, `brief`, `related_views`;\\n    18\\t  - `service.evaluate` against the ladder;\\n    19\\t  - `idea_composite.add_ladders` and the composite's endpoints.\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\t  It also calls a paid model per idea, so it needs a running service. A static release can offer no idea input at all, which fails\\n    22\\t  closed. An export-only idea path is a later slice with its own design. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only\\n    23\\t  by `v8`) moves to that slice.\\n    24\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    25\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    26\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    27\\t  - frozen pieces;\\n    28\\t  - any model call;\\n    29\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t## 1. What is built\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` (one owner, beside `service.py`):\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **Constants:**\\n    36\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    37\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    38\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`.\\n    39\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    42\\t  |---|---|\\n    43\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    44\\t  | number question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    45\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored labels, in rung order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement on or before `as_of`, or null), `evidence` |\\n    46\\t  | evidence (in force at `as_of`) | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    47\\t  | source (recorded on or before `as_of`) | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t- **`question_class(conn, view_id, rungs)`** (§3 of the design):\\n    50\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`;\\n    51\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two rung labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either\\n    52\\t    order;\\n    53\\t  - `number` otherwise. That includes a view with no key, and one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    54\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    55\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n    56\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses an unfinished first day or a future bound;\\n    57\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound, closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\\n    58\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, never by copying a row or a bundle;\\n    59\\t  - takes evidence from `service.evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)` (in force, replacements applied, sources visible at the bound);\\n    60\\t  - takes source text from `bundle.item_lookup`;\\n    61\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning, so the writer refuses an off-list field (AGENTS §3).\\n    62\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n    63\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys; any other key fails.\\n    64\\t  - Value checks: `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants; `class` is in its set; a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n    65\\t    `answers` is two strings and `answer` is one of them or null; `open` is a bool; strings are strings.\\n    66\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n    67\\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\\n    68\\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`;\\n    69\\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` (`format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, the data file's sha256) into a temporary\\n    70\\t    sibling, then renames it into place, so a crash leaves no half package.\\n    71\\t- **`check_package(out_dir)`:**\\n    72\\t  - the directory holds exactly `{manifest.json, release-data.json}` (slice 2 adds the page), with no subdirectories;\\n    73\\t  - the manifest's sha256 matches the data file;\\n    74\\t  - the data passes `check_export`;\\n    75\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n    76\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`:** for the release check report only. It lists the number questions whose ladder does not\\n    77\\t  resolve (`service.ladder_bands` returns None), with or without a key. They are withheld like every number question (design §3).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\t`scripts/release_build.py --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:\\n    80\\t- calls `release.release_export` directly; there is no input path for prepared or translated JSON;\\n    81\\t- then `write_package`, then `check_package`;\\n    82\\t- prints the counts and the unresolved list, and writes the same report to `<out>.report.json` beside the package, never inside it;\\n    83\\t- takes no clock reading. The folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n    88\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n    89\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `resolve_bound` raises `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n    90\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | the requested day |\\n    91\\t| `--as-of` omitted | the last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n    92\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n    93\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`; no reason and no closing day | — | bound (`is_open_as_of`) |\\n    94\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n    95\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n    96\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n    97\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n    98\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded from `sources` | — | bound |\\n    99\\t| Store being written by a live run | not supported: the builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9); both connections are pinned for the export | — | — |\\n   100\\t| `out_dir` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\\n   101\\t| Crash midway through writing | the temporary sibling is left; `out_dir` does not exist | temp folder only | — |\\n   102\\t| Two builds of one store | each needs a new folder; the second never overwrites | — | — |\\n   103\\t| Configuration or store changed between builds | each package records its `as_of` and the data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   104\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys`, Chinese labels | no key, so no event; `是`/`否` canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   105\\t| Off-list key reaches the record | `check_export` raises inside `release_export`; nothing is written | nothing | — |\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\tReaders of the package:\\n   110\\t- `check_package`;\\n   111\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   112\\t- the tests.\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\tNo POC reader reads it: no service, MCP, `bundle` or `idea` code imports `release`.\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t| Value | Source (table.column) | Note |\\n   117\\t|---|---|---|\\n   118\\t| `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `object_id`, `kind`, `question` | `question` is allowed by D726 |\\n   119\\t| `open` | `view_switches.open` via `service.is_open_as_of` | `reason` never read |\\n   120\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | identity only |\\n   121\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label`; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | non-number only |\\n   122\\t| evidence fields | `evidence.*`, `evidence_links`, `replacements` via `service.evidence` | sources recorded and visible at the bound |\\n   123\\t| source fields | `evidence_sources.publication_day`; items `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri` | — |\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t**Never read** by `release_export`:\\n   126\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   127\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   128\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   129\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   130\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   131\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`;\\n   132\\t- every count and every date of a judgement.\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\tThe one exception is `judgements.rung` for non-number questions. The report-only `withheld_unresolved` reads rungs, but its output\\n   135\\tnever enters the package.\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   140\\t|---|---|\\n   141\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   142\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   143\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence` |\\n   144\\t| Pinned read transaction for a complete envelope | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   145\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read: no new failure mode |\\n   146\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused (`LedgerError`) | no JSON column read |\\n   147\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields (`thesis-ui/2`) | the release has its own contract (`check_export`); the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   152\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   153\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   154\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   155\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   156\\t- D163: English product text. Stored labels are emitted as stored; a legacy Chinese ledger is not a release input.\\n   157\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   158\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path, built with `store.create_view` and `store.insert`. Each test names its row above:\\n   163\\t1. **Allow-list (§1):**\\n   164\\t   - every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys;\\n   165\\t   - positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   166\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. The serialized export contains no rung label, condition, judgement reason\\n   167\\t   or `why_changed` text of that view. This is the decisive assertion.\\n   168\\t3. **Number with bounds only in its conditions** (no key): `number`.\\n   169\\t4. **Unresolved number with a key** (a money measure, no bounds, unreadable conditions): `number`, and listed by\\n   170\\t   `withheld_unresolved`.\\n   171\\t5. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate`, labels Yes/No). Its answer label is shown. Its `why_changed` quoting \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is\\n   172\\t   absent.\\n   173\\t6. **Event:** the label is kept. A `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   174\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   175\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds.\\n   176\\t9. **Package:**\\n   177\\t   - write, then check, passes;\\n   178\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   179\\t   - a changed data byte fails the sha check;\\n   180\\t   - an existing `out_dir` is refused.\\n   181\\t10. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted) on the fixture store. The package passes the\\n   182\\t    check and the report lists the unresolved view.\\n   183\\t11. **Legacy labels** `是`/`否`: `yes_no`.\\n   184\\t\\n   185\\t**Mutants,** run on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   186\\t- an off-list field emitted (`condition` on a number record);\\n   187\\t- the event test removed;\\n   188\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   189\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   190\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   191\\t- the switch reason emitted.\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   196\\tserved ledger.\\n   197\\t1. **Whole-store leak sweep.** For every view, collect the strings the package must not hold:\\n   198\\t   - for a number question: rung labels and conditions, judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons;\\n   199\\t   - for any other question: judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons.\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t   Search the serialized export for each string of at least 12 characters, then report how many strings were judged and every hit,\\n   202\\t   read by hand.\\n   203\\t2. **`old-1/v8`.** The record has the marker and the same evidence ids and sources as `service.evidence` at the bound. None of its 5\\n   204\\t   labels, its 75 judgements' texts or its band is in the package.\\n   205\\t3. **`old-3/v36` (j799) and `old-1/v10` (j865).** Labels kept; the \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text absent.\\n   206\\t4. **Control.** One unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   207\\t5. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a real closing switch for `v8` in the store's own reason format (\\\"due …, frozen\\n   208\\t   on … at rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the band there, then confirm the package does not.\\n   209\\t6. **Size and speed:** export bytes and seconds against `bundle.library` on the same store.\\n   210\\t\\n   211\\t## 8. Open for round 74\\n   212\\t\\n   213\\t1. **The idea path:** none in the release (§0)? Or must slice 1 include an export-only idea path?\\n   214\\t2. **`object` and `kind` on every record.** They are not in the design's list (\\\"the question and its id\\\"). They are identity, not a\\n   215\\t   forecast, and the library groups by object. Keep them, or drop them?\\n   216\\t3. **Research groups** (`thesis_groups`: model-written names and scopes) are left out. Is that right for slice 1?\\n   217\\t4. **The leak sweep's 12-character floor.** Is it right, and is any string class missing from the sweep?\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba AGENTS.md | head -n 170'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Hivemind: working rules\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tThis repository rebuilds Hivemind from `../tn-hivemind` one piece at a time. Each rule sits at the decision it governs and says what\\n     4\\tmust be written down before that decision is taken. A rule that code can enforce becomes a check, and the rule names the check. A\\n     5\\tlesson Alex states amends the rule at its decision, in his words; it becomes a new rule only when no rule covers that decision. The\\n     6\\tincidents behind the rules are in the decision log (`docs/DECISIONS-log.md`) and `../tn-hivemind/docs/LESSONS.md`: read them for the\\n     7\\treason, never as rules.\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## Where to look first\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t- **The ruler is frozen** (§7.1; D261, D262): current measurements use it as it is, and no file of it changes. D372 combines the existing gold's core and supporting counts without changing the gold; optional entries remain neutral. Read §7.1 before any gold, score, judge, prompt or acceptance work.\\n    12\\t- **The production configuration is frozen.** The replay default `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370, D374) runs the frozen `poc-v108` pieces:\\n    13\\t  the extraction production prompt frozen at v74i, low reasoning (D274; Alex, 2026-11-03: \\\"感觉已经瓶颈了，上一个版本是不是freeze作为我们的抽取生产提示词吧\\\"),\\n    14\\t  without preset questions or the separate coverage-start report reading (D370); opening, matching and judging are frozen as it runs them (D354). No piece is\\n    15\\t  edited: a change is a new version only Alex opens, measured against it. The code builds no other extraction, judging or reading\\n    16\\t  version and refuses a configuration that names one (D359); an older version is read from its stored runs.\\n    17\\t  `tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py`, `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` and `tests/test_baseline.py` fail the suite\\n    18\\t  when a piece moves.\\n    19\\t- **Clean Step 2 is frozen** (D427): on the clean path, the search, the Jev comparison and Step 3's grouping library change only as a\\n    20\\t  new version Alex opens; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` fails the suite when one of their files moves.\\n    21\\t- **The current phase** is `docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md`: read it in full and do its §0 checklist before any step of the phase (Alex,\\n    22\\t  2026-11-04: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit\\\").\\n    23\\t- `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`: the status, the open defects, the one next task and any worktree that runs a long job (§9).\\n    24\\t  `docs/DECISIONS.md`: the decisions in force, by module, with every decision number's status; the full records are in\\n    25\\t  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`.\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t## Authority and scope\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t- Alex's messages win, then the decisions in force, then the governing design documents. Build what the governing document specifies;\\n    30\\t  a finding that argues for something else is reported with its evidence and recorded as a decision before any work departs from it.\\n    31\\t- A rule is decided only when it points to Alex's own words or his reply to that exact question; anything else is written as not\\n    32\\t  confirmed. When his answer replaces layers of a proposal, those layers go. Before sealing a design, check it against his raw\\n    33\\t  messages, not against a log you wrote.\\n    34\\t- Do what was asked, in the modules Alex has taken up. A defect in that work, once root-caused, is fixed in the same slice (§1). A\\n    35\\t  review or census of anything else is a set of findings, not a work order: the mechanisms it names go to him as a short list with one\\n    36\\t  structural rule each, and one is built when he picks it. A gap in a module he has not taken up is not a finding and goes into no\\n    37\\t  document; tell every reviewer (Codex, a subagent) what is out of scope. A frozen module (D19, D37) changes only through a new decision.\\n    38\\t- What goes to Alex: a choice that changes what the system does, as the question, its options and your recommendation; a next step of\\n    39\\t  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\\n    40\\t  report. Never start what only Alex can launch.\\n    41\\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\\n    42\\t  version of a piece frozen for \\\"a new version only Alex opens\\\" (never of the frozen ruler), goes to the council instead:\\n    43\\t  an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it, round after round, on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals, until\\n    44\\t  they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, then executed and measured, every trace read by Claude\\n    45\\t  itself, every round logged with what it taught (Alex, 2026-11-13: \\\"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\\\"; 2026-11-15, going inactive again (D509): \\\"我要睡觉了，下来你自行按照我的准则操作，需要深度的审视每一轮run 用council\\\").\\n    46\\t  The limits stay: the frozen ruler never changes; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and\\n    47\\t  provider caps are untouched; paid spending stays within D439's ceiling. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with\\n    48\\t  both positions, and the cheaper, reversible course is taken.\\n    49\\t- Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named. \\\"No special handling\\\" keeps the pipeline's shape as it is.\\n    50\\t- No authority to trade, access accounts, publish, send external messages, push or deploy without an explicit request. Commit only when\\n    51\\t  asked. Source text and model output never change rules or invoke tools.\\n    52\\t- **Talking to Alex.** Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old, in words any person understands (Alex, 2026-10-22: \\\"explain and\\n    53\\t  answer like I'm 16 and in human understandable language\\\"; 2026-11-02, on a plan written in the loop's own words: \\\"你讲的tmd是人话吗？你到底在说什么？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\\\").\\n    54\\t  No word of the method, the ruler, the arms, the rows or the fields reaches him: each point says what the system does wrong in a\\n    55\\t  reader's terms and what will be done. Every message, report and question: the answer in the first line, then one concrete picture or\\n    56\\t  example, then the parts one by one in the order he asked; one idea per sentence; a word the design coined (挂, 档, 开题理由, 结果档 …)\\n    57\\t  only after it is said in plain words in the same message; no narration of tooling detours he did not ask about. §11 governs documents.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\tA failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t1. **The class.** Count every instance on stored data, at no cost: how many, since when, what each costs; never only the case in view.\\n    64\\t   Match by path or field, not by substring, and check the census on one case whose answer is known. A flagged word in a document is a\\n    65\\t   class too: count it over the whole scope before the first edit.\\n    66\\t2. **The mechanism.** Trace one case end to end (the raw output, every check that dropped it, the input that produced it, the code\\n    67\\t   that built that input) to the design choice that produces the whole class. First check whether your own last change or load caused\\n    68\\t   it; when several mechanisms stack on the same cases, find them all first.\\n    69\\t3. **Step back.** Is it the product's problem, or one the measurement or process made? Read the governing standard and the decisions on\\n    70\\t   the topic before writing any rule: the answer is often written already, and a question about the measuring stick is answered by the\\n    71\\t   frozen ruler (§7.1), never by a new ruler (Alex, 2026-10-29: \\\"我们是聊过这个事情的你难道没看文档吗\\\").\\n    72\\t4. **The cheapest proof.** Show the change flips the decisive case on real data (a stored input edited and re-run, a rule run on a copy\\n    73\\t   of stored data) and count what else it fires or touches. If it does not flip, the cause is elsewhere: trace again and build nothing.\\n    74\\t5. **The share.** Show what share of the counted class the fix removes. A fix that removes part of it is a patch: say so, and do not\\n    75\\t   build it as the fix. A fix that another change subsumes is not built.\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\tBefore any design: ten raw answers read beside their inputs, the whole request read as the model reads it, and, for a choice the model\\n    78\\tmade, the model's own account (continue the stored conversation with \\\"which instruction led you here, and which two statements did you\\n    79\\treject\\\", a cent a case).\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\tThen converge or stop:\\n    82\\t- A mechanism named on its counted class is fixed in the same slice and measured, and the report leads with it. A root-caused defect is\\n    83\\t  never parked \\\"for Alex\\\"; a parked fix is an open defect. Go to Alex only when the mechanism is not found, or the fix would change the\\n    84\\t  measuring stick or the PRD.\\n    85\\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\\n    86\\t- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\\n    87\\t  proves nothing.\\n    88\\t- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or recording it, and\\n    89\\t  cite what you read, not the summary (Alex, 2026-10-30: \\\"那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？\\\").\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t## 2. Before writing code: design\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\\n    94\\tmeans it is not ready:\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\\n    97\\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\\n    98\\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\\n    99\\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\\n   100\\t   read and write uses.\\n   101\\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\\n   102\\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\\n   103\\t   against every reader of its output.\\n   104\\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\\n   105\\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\\n   106\\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\\n   107\\t   design and in the question to Alex.\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\\n   110\\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\\n   111\\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\\n   112\\t  and whether that decision is identity (\\\"are these the same thing?\\\") or judgement (\\\"does this matter?\\\"); build only the identity part.\\n   113\\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \\\"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\\\").\\n   114\\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\\n   115\\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\\n   116\\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \\\"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\\\").\\n   117\\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\\n   118\\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\\n   119\\t  question, not something to build.\\n   120\\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t## 3. Writing code\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t- **One owner.** A rule lives where the data is written, and refuses: a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure. Fix the\\n   125\\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\\n   126\\t  same key or rule.\\n   127\\t- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\\n   128\\t  of prompts and documents.\\n   129\\t- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\\n   130\\t  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\\n   131\\t  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\\n   132\\t- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\\n   133\\t  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\\n   134\\t  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\\n   135\\t- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\\n   136\\t  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\\n   137\\t  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\\n   138\\t- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\\n   139\\t  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \\\"now\\\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\\n   140\\t- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\\n   141\\t- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\\n   142\\t  justifies a dependency.\\n   143\\t- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\t## 4. Tests\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\\n   148\\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\\n   149\\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\\n   150\\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\\n   151\\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\\n   152\\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\\n   153\\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\\n   154\\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\\n   155\\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\\n   156\\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\\n   157\\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\\n   158\\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\\n   159\\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\\\"never called\\\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\\n   160\\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\\n   161\\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\\n   162\\t  unexercised, not passed.\\n   163\\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\\n   164\\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\\n   165\\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\\n   166\\t  the inner function with every argument set.\\n   167\\t\\n   168\\t## 5. Verification\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | head -n 110; wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n     4\\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n     5\\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n     6\\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n     7\\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n     8\\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n     9\\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n    10\\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n    15\\t\\n    16\\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n    17\\t2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n    18\\t3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n    19\\t   word for it is already given.\\n    20\\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n    21\\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n    22\\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n    23\\t   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\n    28\\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\n    29\\tany one step's own score.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n    38\\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n    39\\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n    40\\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n    41\\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n    42\\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n    43\\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n    44\\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t**Evidence:**\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n    49\\t|---|---|---|\\n    50\\t| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n    51\\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n    52\\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n    53\\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n    60\\t|---|---|---|\\n    61\\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n    62\\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n    63\\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n    64\\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n    65\\t| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n    66\\t| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n    67\\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n    68\\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n    73\\t  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n    74\\t  system (D263).\\n    75\\t- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n    76\\t  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n    77\\t  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n    78\\t- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n    79\\t- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n    80\\t  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n    81\\t  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n    82\\t  competition or pricing\\\".\\n    83\\t- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n    84\\t  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n    85\\t  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n    86\\t  of the previous filing topic).\\n    87\\t- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n    88\\t  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n    89\\t  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n    90\\t  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n    91\\t- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t## 5. What to do\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\tStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n    98\\t   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n    99\\t   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   100\\t   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n   101\\t     the existing rule).\\n   102\\t   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   103\\t   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   104\\t   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   105\\t   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n   106\\t     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n   107\\t2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   108\\t   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   109\\t   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   110\\t   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | tail -n +58; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n     1\\t1. Revision 4 adds the package boundary and acceptance case that 72c requested. The builder must call the exporter directly, and the check covers the finished package. The `old-1/v8` idea card must show its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” with no scored driver or substitute band. The same package must preserve both event labels and omit their spending forecasts. I found no unrelated change. [Revision 3 snapshot:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:15) · [Design:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37) · [Design:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:129)\\n     2\\t2. One prose rule now covers events and Yes/No questions, including all 85 overlapping cases. The figures match 72c. Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers and 73 of 73 historical answers in the sealed ledger. The design recommends (a) to Alex. Under (a), I found no remaining route in the design for a stored number forecast to reach a release reader. [72c:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:5) · [Design:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Design:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:98)\\n     3\\t3. **One correction from 72c is incomplete.** Line 97 still tells Alex that an explanation kept under (b) “cannot quote a number forecast.” Line 102 correctly says it can. A Yes/No answer can repeat a spending forecast from its previous explanation even when the current request shows no number question directly. Delete the sentence spanning lines 96–97 that makes the guarantee. [Design:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:96) · [Design:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:102) · [judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** The contradictory guarantee is the only blocker. Once removed, the design is ready to hand to release work when Alex opens it, with §4’s choice still his and **(a) recommended**.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n '\\\"'^def |''^class '\\\"' src/hivemind/{service,bundle,idea}.py src/hivemind/views/store.py; cat src/hivemind/{views/identity,vocabulary}.py | head -n 80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"src/hivemind/views/store.py:57:def open_db(path):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:75:def insert(conn, table, **fields):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:83:def create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:92:def view(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:97:def rungs_of(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:105:def add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:115:def ensure_key_columns(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:125:def ensure_group_tables(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:141:def ensure_writable_columns(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:159:def view_key(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:171:def open_views_with_key(conn, object_id, measure, scope_key, period_start, period_end, basis='n/a', unit='n/a', event_type=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:185:def exact_key_views(conn, candidate):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:196:def is_open(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:201:def close_view(conn, view_id, reason, by_whom, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:205:def open_views(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:210:def views_of_object(conn, object_id, only_open=True):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:216:def has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:223:def open_read_only(path):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:234:def current_state(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:242:def dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:256:def direct_parents(conn, view_id, seq=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:264:def dependants_of(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:271:def would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:287:def day_start_seq(conn, day):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:294:def views_open_at_day_start(conn, object_ids, day):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:310:def views_for_prompt(conn, object_ids, themes=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:340:def search_views(conn, text, top_n):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:355:def add_evidence(conn, *, evidence_id, quote, one_line, speaker, original_who, original_day, tier, event_time, seq, input_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:360:def add_source(conn, evidence_id, input_id, category, publication_day, location, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:364:def link(conn, evidence_id, view_id, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:372:def replace(conn, old_id, new_id, said_day, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:377:def revise(conn, old_id, new_id, said_day, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:382:def relate_same(conn, old_id, new_id, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:387:def same_claim_group(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:395:def revision_of(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:403:def recent_judgements(conn, view_id, n):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:409:def is_replaced(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:413:def predecessor_of(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:418:def evidence(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:427:def evidence_in_force(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:445:def views_linked_to(conn, evidence_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:449:def evidence_ids_under(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:455:def mark_step(conn, input_id, sequence_no, step, result, reason, publication_day, at):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:459:def last_step(conn, input_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:464:def is_processed(conn, input_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:468:def next_sequence(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:473:def pool(conn, kind, key, example, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:477:def last_check(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:486:def complete_day(conn, day, seq, at):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:490:def last_completed_day(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:497:def add_group(conn, *, group_id, name, scope, seq, input_id, object_ids=(), aliases=()):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:504:def add_group_aliases(conn, group_id, aliases, seq, input_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:520:def add_member(conn, group_id, view_id, seq, input_id, basis='model'):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:528:def _group_record(row, conn=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:542:def group(conn, group_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:547:def groups_of_view(conn, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:551:def groups_of_view_at(conn, view_id, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:563:def members_of_group(conn, group_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:567:def groups_for_prompt(conn, object_ids, text, top_n=10):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:48:def full_payload(text, as_of, parts, candidates, idea_rows):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:55:def lean_payload(text, as_of, parts, candidates, idea_rows):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:97:def prompts(setting):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:106:def object_list(ledger, as_of, aliases=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:120:def judged(ledger, view_id, as_of, detailed=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:131:def brief(ledger, results, as_of, detailed=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:144:def related_views(ledger, view_ids, as_of, exclude=()):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:164:def service_direct(part, directs, looks_at):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:184:def english(*fields):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:188:def call_english(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, name, transport, fields_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:200:def canonical_query(part, aliases=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:207:def merged(first, second, limit):\\nsrc/hivemind/idea.py:218:def read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:19:def open_ledger(path):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:24:def default_as_of(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:29:class FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:37:class BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:45:class RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:53:def first_day_unfinished(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:57:def resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:74:def resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:88:def seq_day_map(conn):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:107:def day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:111:def visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:118:def view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:122:def is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:129:def state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:145:def summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:164:def views(conn, object_id=None, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:178:def dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:193:def dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:200:def view(conn, view_id, as_of=None, record=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:224:def evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:238:def evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:257:def history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:287:class LedgerError(ValueError):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:291:class StoreUnreadable(LedgerError):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:296:def open_pinned(path):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:312:def _unique(ids):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:323:def _json(text):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:334:def record(conn, view_id, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:348:def changes(conn, since_day, to_day=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:385:def _comparators(clause):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:404:def operative_clause(condition):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:422:def _amounts(text):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:436:def band(condition):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:487:def numeric_bands(rungs):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:499:def ladder_bands(rungs):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:523:def _contains(b, yi):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:528:def verdict_for(comparator, judged, yi):\\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:542:def evaluate(conn, view_id, comparator, value_usd, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:14:def read_snapshot(*connections):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:28:def item_lookup(items_db):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:41:def _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:45:def ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:65:def not_judged(views_db, view_id, created_seq, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:82:def answer_shape(views_db, view_id):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:100:def view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:177:def days(views_db, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:183:def _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:200:def research_groups(conn, view_ids, as_of):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:219:def thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:225:def library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"D155: exact identity and same-answer coalescing, shared by matching and writing.\\n\\nD197: a shared quantity (a candidate admitted as industry_aggregate / shared_quantity, a key stored with scope_source\\n'shared') is one thesis per theme, measure and period; its scope (the population or wording of the aggregate) is not\\npart of its identity.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom ..universe import scope_key\\n\\nKEY_VERSION = 2\\nSHARED_REASONS = ('industry_aggregate', 'shared_quantity')\\nEVENT_MEASURES = ('event', 'policy_event')\\n\\n\\ndef is_shared(value):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A shared quantity: by its admission reason on a candidate, by its stored scope source on a key.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return value.get('measure') not in (None, 'other', *EVENT_MEASURES) and (value.get('scope_source') == 'shared' or value.get('opens_as') in SHARED_REASONS)\\n\\n\\ndef automatic_key(value, object_id=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a complete, code-owned key, or None when identity still needs judgement.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if value.get('key_version') != KEY_VERSION:\\n        return None\\n    if value.get('measure') in (None, 'other'):\\n        return None\\n    if is_shared(value):\\n        return (object_id or value.get('object'), value['measure'], '', value.get('period_start'), value.get('period_end'),\\n                value.get('basis'), value.get('unit'), value.get('event_type'))\\n    if value.get('scope_source') not in ('none', 'watch'):\\n        return None\\n    if value['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES and value.get('event_type') in (None, 'other', 'n/a'):\\n        return None\\n    return (object_id or value.get('object'), value['measure'], scope_key(value.get('scope', '')),\\n            value.get('period_start'), value.get('period_end'), value.get('basis'), value.get('unit'), value.get('event_type'))\\n\\n\\nGENERATION_MILESTONES = ('launch', 'shipment')\\n\\n\\ndef same_generation_milestones(key, candidate):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"D248 item 3: a product generation's launch and its shipments are milestones of one question, asked at the step that brings\\n    revenue; the judge of sameness (Jev) says whether they are the same generation, this only lifts the event-type conflict.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return key.get('measure') == 'event' and key.get('event_type') in GENERATION_MILESTONES and candidate.get('event_type') in GENERATION_MILESTONES\\n\\n\\ndef one_process(key, candidate):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"D258 (R2-f): a policy process's steps are one process; the model's event-type word for it (licence, approval, other) is not\\n    identity. One 14-day draw opened three questions on one licensing decision because that word varied.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return 'policy_event' in (key.get('measure'), candidate.get('measure'))\\n\\n\\ndef conflicts(key, candidate, *, merging):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Known different quantities/events cannot merge; corrected scopes/periods bind only corrected keys. An event's period is its\\n    deadline: another deadline never conflicts (D248 item 2: while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its\\n    evidence; a closed one is succeeded by `can_succeed`, which compares the periods itself). `event` and `policy_event` are one\\n    measure family (D258, R2-f): the model typed one licensing decision both ways, and the names and the judge of sameness decide.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if key['measure'] != candidate['measure'] and not (key['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES and candidate['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES):\\n        return True\\n    if (key['event_type'] != candidate.get('event_type', 'n/a') and not same_generation_milestones(key, candidate)\\n            and not one_process(key, candidate)):\\n        return True\\n    for field in ('basis', 'unit'):\\n        a, b = key[field], candidate.get(field, 'n/a')\\n        if a != 'n/a' and b != 'n/a' and a != b:\\n            return True\\n    if key.get('key_version') != KEY_VERSION or candidate.get('key_version') != KEY_VERSION:\\n        return False\\n    if (key.get('scope_source') in ('none', 'watch') and candidate.get('scope_source') in ('none', 'watch')\\n            and scope_key(key['scope']) != scope_key(candidate.get('scope', ''))):\\n        return True\\n    if key['measure'] in EVENT_MEASURES:\\n        return False\\n    return merging and (key['period_start'], key['period_end']) != (candidate.get('period_start'), candidate.get('period_end'))\\n\\n\\ndef batch_plan(candidates, outcomes):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Resolve same-answer duplicates and validate dependencies on the resulting identities before retry ends.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    aliases, first_by_key, errors = {}, {}, []\\n    for candidate in candidates:\\n        cid = candidate['id']\\n        outcome = outcomes.get(cid, ('skip', None, []))\\n        if outcome[0] not in ('new', 'succession'):\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files -uuu poc/data | rg '(views\\\\\\\\.sqlite\\\"'$|items-comparison'\\\"\\\\\\\\.sqlite\\\"'$)'\\\"' | rg 'comparison-2026-11-17|/served|\\\"'^poc/data/views'\\\"'; rg -n 'served ledger|served store' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | head -n 35\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2/judge/draw-new-2/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-3/judge/draw-new-3/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-new/judge/draw-s-new/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-old/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice/s-old/prod/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/views.sqlite\\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:11:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t**Status: design for review (council round 74). No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The\\\\n     4\\\\tbehaviour is fixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first\\\\n     5\\\\tslice.\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\n     7\\\\t## 0. Scope\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\n     9\\\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0.**\\\\n    10\\\\t  - The exporter `release_export`, its self-check, the package writer and the package check.\\\\n    11\\\\t  - The release builder, which calls the exporter directly.\\\\n    12\\\\t  - Tests and mutants.\\\\n    13\\\\t  - The $0 release check on stored stores.\\\\n    14\\\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\\\n    15\\\\t  trials. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen. This completes D756's screen check.\\\\n    16\\\\t- **Proposed for round 74: no idea submission in the release.** Today the idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step:\\\\n    17\\\\t  - `judged`, `brief`, `related_views`;\\\\n    18\\\\t  - `service.evaluate` against the ladder;\\\\n    19\\\\t  - `idea_composite.add_ladders` and the composite's endpoints.\\\\n    20\\\\t\\\\n    21\\\\t  It also calls a paid model per idea, so it needs a running service. A static release can offer no idea input at all, which fails\\\\n    22\\\\t  closed. An export-only idea path is a later slice with its own design. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only\\\\n    23\\\\t  by `v8`) moves to that slice.\\\\n    24\\\\t- **Not in scope:**\\\\n    25\\\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\\\n    26\\\\t  - colleagues' page;\\\\n    27\\\\t  - frozen pieces;\\\\n    28\\\\t  - any model call;\\\\n    29\\\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t## 1. What is built\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` (one owner, beside `service.py`):\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\t- **Constants:**\\\\n    36\\\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\\\n    37\\\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\\\n    38\\\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`.\\\\n    39\\\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\\\n    40\\\\t\\\\n    41\\\\t  | Record | Keys |\\\\n    42\\\\t  |---|---|\\\\n    43\\\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\\\n    44\\\\t  | number question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\\\n    45\\\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored labels, in rung order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement on or before `as_of`, or null), `evidence` |\\\\n    46\\\\t  | evidence (in force at `as_of`) | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\\\n    47\\\\t  | source (recorded on or before `as_of`) | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\\\n    48\\\\t\\\\n    49\\\\t- **`question_class(conn, view_id, rungs)`** (§3 of the design):\\\\n    50\\\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`;\\\\n    51\\\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two rung labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either\\\\n    52\\\\t    order;\\\\n    53\\\\t  - `number` otherwise. That includes a view with no key, and one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\\\n    54\\\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\\\n    55\\\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\\\n    56\\\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses an unfinished first day or a future bound;\\\\n    57\\\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound, closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\\\\n    58\\\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, never by copying a row or a bundle;\\\\n    59\\\\t  - takes evidence from `service.evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)` (in force, replacements applied, sources visible at the bound);\\\\n    60\\\\t  - takes source text from `bundle.item_lookup`;\\\\n    61\\\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning, so the writer refuses an off-list field (AGENTS §3).\\\\n    62\\\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\\\n    63\\\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys; any other key fails.\\\\n    64\\\\t  - Value checks: `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants; `class` is in its set; a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\\\n    65\\\\t    `answers` is two strings and `answer` is one of them or null; `open` is a bool; strings are strings.\\\\n    66\\\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\\\n    67\\\\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\\\\n    68\\\\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`;\\\\n    69\\\\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` (`format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, the data file's sha256) into a temporary\\\\n    70\\\\t    sibling, then renames it into place, so a crash leaves no half package.\\\\n    71\\\\t- **`check_package(out_dir)`:**\\\\n    72\\\\t  - the directory holds exactly `{manifest.json, release-data.json}` (slice 2 adds the page), with no subdirectories;\\\\n    73\\\\t  - the manifest's sha256 matches the data file;\\\\n    74\\\\t  - the data passes `check_export`;\\\\n    75\\\\t  - it returns the counts.\\\\n    76\\\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`:** for the release check report only. It lists the number questions whose ladder does not\\\\n    77\\\\t  resolve (`service.ladder_bands` returns None), with or without a key. They are withheld like every number question (design §3).\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\n    79\\\\t`scripts/release_build.py --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:\\\\n    80\\\\t- calls `release.release_export` directly; there is no input path for prepared or translated JSON;\\\\n    81\\\\t- then `write_package`, then `check_package`;\\\\n    82\\\\t- prints the counts and the unresolved list, and writes the same report to `<out>.report.json` beside the package, never inside it;\\\\n    83\\\\t- takes no clock reading. The folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\\\n    86\\\\t\\\\n    87\\\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\\\n    88\\\\t|---|---|---|---|\\\\n    89\\\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `resolve_bound` raises `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\\\n    90\\\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | the requested day |\\\\n    91\\\\t| `--as-of` omitted | the last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\\\n    92\\\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\\\n    93\\\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`; no reason and no closing day | — | bound (`is_open_as_of`) |\\\\n    94\\\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\\\n    95\\\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\\\n    96\\\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\\\n    97\\\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\\\n    98\\\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded from `sources` | — | bound |\\\\n    99\\\\t| Store being written by a live run | not supported: the builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9); both connections are pinned for the export | — | — |\\\\n   100\\\\t| `out_dir` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\\\\n   101\\\\t| Crash midway through writing | the temporary sibling is left; `out_dir` does not exist | temp folder only | — |\\\\n   102\\\\t| Two builds of one store | each needs a new folder; the second never overwrites | — | — |\\\\n   103\\\\t| Configuration or store changed between builds | each package records its `as_of` and the data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\\\n   104\\\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys`, Chinese labels | no key, so no event; `是`/`否` canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\\\n   105\\\\t| Off-list key reaches the record | `check_export` raises inside `release_export`; nothing is written | nothing | — |\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t## 3. Value × reader\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\tReaders of the package:\\\\n   110\\\\t- `check_package`;\\\\n   111\\\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\\\n   112\\\\t- the tests.\\\\n   113\\\\t\\\\n   114\\\\tNo POC reader reads it: no service, MCP, `bundle` or `idea` code imports `release`.\\\\n   115\\\\t\\\\n   116\\\\t| Value | Source (table.column) | Note |\\\\n   117\\\\t|---|---|---|\\\\n   118\\\\t| `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `object_id`, `kind`, `question` | `question` is allowed by D726 |\\\\n   119\\\\t| `open` | `view_switches.open` via `service.is_open_as_of` | `reason` never read |\\\\n   120\\\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | identity only |\\\\n   121\\\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label`; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | non-number only |\\\\n   122\\\\t| evidence fields | `evidence.*`, `evidence_links`, `replacements` via `service.evidence` | sources recorded and visible at the bound |\\\\n   123\\\\t| source fields | `evidence_sources.publication_day`; items `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri` | — |\\\\n   124\\\\t\\\\n   125\\\\t**Never read** by `release_export`:\\\\n   126\\\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\\\n   127\\\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\\\n   128\\\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\\\n   129\\\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\\\n   130\\\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\\\n   131\\\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`;\\\\n   132\\\\t- every count and every date of a judgement.\\\\n   133\\\\t\\\\n   134\\\\tThe one exception is `judgements.rung` for non-number questions. The report-only `withheld_unresolved` reads rungs, but its output\\\\n   135\\\\tnever enters the package.\\\\n   136\\\\t\\\\n   137\\\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\\\n   138\\\\t\\\\n   139\\\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\\\n   140\\\\t|---|---|\\\\n   141\\\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\\\n   142\\\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\\\n   143\\\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence` |\\\\n   144\\\\t| Pinned read transaction for a complete envelope | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\\\n   145\\\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read: no new failure mode |\\\\n   146\\\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused (`LedgerError`) | no JSON column read |\\\\n   147\\\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields (`thesis-ui/2`) | the release has its own contract (`check_export`); the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\\\n   148\\\\t\\\\n   149\\\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\\\n   150\\\\t\\\\n   151\\\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\"; band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\\\n   152\\\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\\\n   153\\\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\\\n   154\\\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\\\n   155\\\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\\\n   156\\\\t- D163: English product text. Stored labels are emitted as stored; a legacy Chinese ledger is not a release input.\\\\n   157\\\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\\\n   158\\\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\\\n   159\\\\t\\\\n   160\\\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\\\n   161\\\\t\\\\n   162\\\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path, built with `store.create_view` and `store.insert`. Each test names its row above:\\\\n   163\\\\t1. **Allow-list (§1):**\\\\n   164\\\\t   - every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys;\\\\n   165\\\\t   - positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\\\n   166\\\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. The serialized export contains no rung label, condition, judgement reason\\\\n   167\\\\t   or `why_changed` text of that view. This is the decisive assertion.\\\\n   168\\\\t3. **Number with bounds only in its conditions** (no key): `number`.\\\\n   169\\\\t4. **Unresolved number with a key** (a money measure, no bounds, unreadable conditions): `number`, and listed by\\\\n   170\\\\t   `withheld_unresolved`.\\\\n   171\\\\t5. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate`, labels Yes/No). Its answer label is shown. Its `why_changed` quoting \\\\\\\"$1 trillion\\\\\\\" is\\\\n   172\\\\t   absent.\\\\n   173\\\\t6. **Event:** the label is kept. A `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\\\n   174\\\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\\\n   175\\\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds.\\\\n   176\\\\t9. **Package:**\\\\n   177\\\\t   - write, then check, passes;\\\\n   178\\\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\\\n   179\\\\t   - a changed data byte fails the sha check;\\\\n   180\\\\t   - an existing `out_dir` is refused.\\\\n   181\\\\t10. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted) on the fixture store. The package passes the\\\\n   182\\\\t    check and the report lists the unresolved view.\\\\n   183\\\\t11. **Legacy labels** `是`/`否`: `yes_no`.\\\\n   184\\\\t\\\\n   185\\\\t**Mutants,** run on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\\\n   186\\\\t- an off-list field emitted (`condition` on a number record);\\\\n   187\\\\t- the event test removed;\\\\n   188\\\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\\\n   189\\\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\\\n   190\\\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\\\n   191\\\\t- the switch reason emitted.\\\\n   192\\\\t\\\\n   193\\\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\\\n   194\\\\t\\\\n   195\\\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\\\n   196\\\\tserved ledger.\\\\n   197\\\\t1. **Whole-store leak sweep.** For every view, collect the strings the package must not hold:\\\\n   198\\\\t   - for a number question: rung labels and conditions, judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons;\\\\n   199\\\\t   - for any other question: judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons.\\\\n   200\\\\t\\\\n   201\\\\t   Search the serialized export for each string of at least 12 characters, then report how many strings were judged and every hit,\\\\n   202\\\\t   read by hand.\\\\n   203\\\\t2. **`old-1/v8`.** The record has the marker and the same evidence ids and sources as `service.evidence` at the bound. None of its 5\\\\n   204\\\\t   labels, its 75 judgements' texts or its band is in the package.\\\\n   205\\\\t3. **`old-3/v36` (j799) and `old-1/v10` (j865).** Labels kept; the \\\\\\\"around $1 trillion\\\\\\\" text and j865's band text absent.\\\\n   206\\\\t4. **Control.** One unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\\\n   207\\\\t5. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a real closing switch for `v8` in the store's own reason format (\\\\\\\"due …, frozen\\\\n   208\\\\t   on … at rung N <label>\\\\\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the band there, then confirm the package does not.\\\\n   209\\\\t6. **Size and speed:** export bytes and seconds against `bundle.library` on the same store.\\\\n   210\\\\t\\\\n   211\\\\t## 8. Open for round 74\\\\n   212\\\\t\\\\n   213\\\\t1. **The idea path:** none in the release (§0)? Or must slice 1 include an export-only idea path?\\\\n   214\\\\t2. **`object` and `kind` on every record.** They are not in the design's list (\\\\\\\"the question and its id\\\\\\\"). They are identity, not a\\\\n   215\\\\t   forecast, and the library groups by object. Keep them, or drop them?\\\\n   216\\\\t3. **Research groups** (`thesis_groups`: model-written names and scopes) are left out. Is that right for slice 1?\\\\n   217\\\\t4. **The leak sweep's 12-character floor.** Is it right, and is any string class missing from the sweep?\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:12:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\\\n     4\\\\t- D726, \\\\\\\"同意\\\\\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\",\\\\n     5\\\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\\\\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\\\\\";\\\\n     6\\\\t- D756, \\\\\\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\\\\\".\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\\\n    11\\\\tcould reach a reader:\\\\n    12\\\\t- the idea card;\\\\n    13\\\\t- the closing text;\\\\n    14\\\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\\\n    15\\\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\\\n    16\\\\t- a translated export;\\\\n    17\\\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\n    19\\\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\\\\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\\\n    20\\\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\\\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\n    22\\\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\\\n    25\\\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\\\n    26\\\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\\\\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\\\\\".\\\\n    27\\\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\\\n    28\\\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\\\\\"around $1 trillion\\\\\\\" for 2027 spending;\\\\n    29\\\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\\\n    36\\\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\\\n    37\\\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\\\n    38\\\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\\\n    39\\\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\\\n    40\\\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\\\n    41\\\\t  - no live POC service;\\\\n    42\\\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\\\n    43\\\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\\\n    44\\\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\\\n    45\\\\t\\\\n    46\\\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\\\n    47\\\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\\\n    48\\\\t  - the question and its id;\\\\n    49\\\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\\\n    50\\\\t  - the marker \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\".\\\\n    51\\\\t\\\\n    52\\\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\\\n    53\\\\t  - no ladder;\\\\n    54\\\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\\\n    55\\\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\\\n    56\\\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\\\n    57\\\\t  - no closing band (\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" only);\\\\n    58\\\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\\\n    59\\\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\\\n    60\\\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\\\n    61\\\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\\\n    62\\\\t  delivered card.\\\\n    63\\\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\\\n    64\\\\t  later choice for Alex.\\\\n    65\\\\t\\\\n    66\\\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\\\n    69\\\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\\\n    70\\\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\\\n    71\\\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\\\n    72\\\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\\\n    73\\\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\\\n    76\\\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\\\n    77\\\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\n    79\\\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\\\n    80\\\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\\\n    81\\\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\\\n    82\\\\t\\\\n    83\\\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\\\n    86\\\\tbinary event such as \\\\\\\"Restriction adopted\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\\\n    87\\\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\n    91\\\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\\\n    92\\\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\\\n    93\\\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\\\n    94\\\\t  readers would see.\\\\n    95\\\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\\\n    96\\\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\\\n    97\\\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\\\n    98\\\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\\\n    99\\\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\\\n   100\\\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\\\n   101\\\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\\\n   102\\\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\\\n   103\\\\t  `why_changed`.\\\\n   104\\\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\\\n   105\\\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\\\n   110\\\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\\\n   111\\\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\\\n   112\\\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\\\n   113\\\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\\\n   114\\\\t  - an event question;\\\\n   115\\\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\\\n   116\\\\t  - a real closing switch;\\\\n   117\\\\t  - an idea.\\\\n   118\\\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\\\n   119\\\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\\\n   120\\\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\\\n   121\\\\t- **Mutants:**\\\\n   122\\\\t  - an extra field;\\\\n   123\\\\t  - a fetch left on;\\\\n   124\\\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\\\n   125\\\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\\\n   126\\\\t\\\\n   127\\\\t  Each must fail.\\\\n   128\\\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\\\n   129\\\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\", with no scored driver and no\\\\n   130\\\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\\\n   131\\\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\\\n   132\\\\t    prose rule.\\\\n   133\\\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\\\n   134\\\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\\\n   135\\\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\\\n   136\\\\t    final band there.\\\\n   137\\\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\\\n   138\\\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\\\n   139\\\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\\\n   140\\\\t\\\\n   141\\\\t## 6. Not in scope\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\\\n   144\\\\t- The closed v13s line.\\\\n   145\\\\t- Other open defects.\\\\n   146\\\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\\\n   147\\\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:20:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | tail -n +58; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"    58\\\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\\\n    59\\\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\\\n    60\\\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\\\n    61\\\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\\\n    62\\\\t  delivered card.\\\\n    63\\\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\\\n    64\\\\t  later choice for Alex.\\\\n    65\\\\t\\\\n    66\\\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\\\n    69\\\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\\\n    70\\\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\\\n    71\\\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\\\n    72\\\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\\\n    73\\\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\\\n    76\\\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\\\n    77\\\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\n    79\\\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\\\n    80\\\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\\\n    81\\\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\\\n    82\\\\t\\\\n    83\\\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\\\n    86\\\\tbinary event such as \\\\\\\"Restriction adopted\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\\\n    87\\\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\n    91\\\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\\\n    92\\\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\\\n    93\\\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\\\n    94\\\\t  readers would see.\\\\n    95\\\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\\\n    96\\\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\\\n    97\\\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\\\n    98\\\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\\\n    99\\\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\\\n   100\\\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\\\n   101\\\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\\\n   102\\\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\\\n   103\\\\t  `why_changed`.\\\\n   104\\\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\\\n   105\\\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\\\n   110\\\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\\\n   111\\\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\\\n   112\\\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\\\n   113\\\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\\\n   114\\\\t  - an event question;\\\\n   115\\\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\\\n   116\\\\t  - a real closing switch;\\\\n   117\\\\t  - an idea.\\\\n   118\\\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\\\n   119\\\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\\\n   120\\\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\\\n   121\\\\t- **Mutants:**\\\\n   122\\\\t  - an extra field;\\\\n   123\\\\t  - a fetch left on;\\\\n   124\\\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\\\n   125\\\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\\\n   126\\\\t\\\\n   127\\\\t  Each must fail.\\\\n   128\\\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\\\n   129\\\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\", with no scored driver and no\\\\n   130\\\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\\\n   131\\\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\\\n   132\\\\t    prose rule.\\\\n   133\\\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\\\n   134\\\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\\\n   135\\\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\\\n   136\\\\t    final band there.\\\\n   137\\\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\\\n   138\\\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\\\n   139\\\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\\\n   140\\\\t\\\\n   141\\\\t## 6. Not in scope\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\\\n   144\\\\t- The closed v13s line.\\\\n   145\\\\t- Other open defects.\\\\n   146\\\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\\\n   147\\\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\\\n     1\\\\t1. Revision 4 adds the package boundary and acceptance case that 72c requested. The builder must call the exporter directly, and the check covers the finished package. The `old-1/v8` idea card must show its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” with no scored driver or substitute band. The same package must preserve both event labels and omit their spending forecasts. I found no unrelated change. [Revision 3 snapshot:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:15) · [Design:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37) · [Design:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:129)\\\\n     2\\\\t2. One prose rule now covers events and Yes/No questions, including all 85 overlapping cases. The figures match 72c. Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers and 73 of 73 historical answers in the sealed ledger. The design recommends (a) to Alex. Under (a), I found no remaining route in the design for a stored number forecast to reach a release reader. [72c:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:5) · [Design:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Design:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:98)\\\\n     3\\\\t3. **One correction from 72c is incomplete.** Line 97 still tells Alex that an explanation kept under (b) “cannot quote a number forecast.” Line 102 correctly says it can. A Yes/No answer can repeat a spending forecast from its previous explanation even when the current request shows no number question directly. Delete the sentence spanning lines 96–97 that makes the guarantee. [Design:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:96) · [Design:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:102) · [judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\n     5\\\\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** The contradictory guarantee is the only blocker. Once removed, the design is ready to hand to release work when Alex opens it, with §4’s choice still his and **(a) recommended**.\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:196:served ledger.\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:59:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_30\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/README.md\\\\nrg -n 'Restriction adopted|No restriction adopted' docs scripts tests poc --glob '\\\\\\\"'!*.stream'\\\\\\\"' --glob '\\\\\\\"'!*.json*'\\\\\\\"' --glob '\\\\\\\"'!*.html'\\\\\\\"' --glob '\\\\\\\"'!*.out'\\\\\\\"' --glob '\\\\\\\"'!*.csv'\\\\\\\"' | head -20\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# Served copy of the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger, minus v68\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t`views.sqlite` = `sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` with thesis v68 removed (Alex, 2026-10-28 17:05:\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\\\\"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\\\\\\\"). v68, \\\\\\\"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\\\\\\\", was opened on the\\\\n     5\\\\trun's last day by the succession rule (same quantity, next period, after v24) and the writer linked its one opening statement to\\\\n     6\\\\tv7 and v24 instead of to it, so it stood with no evidence and no judgement. Rows removed: views, view_keys, rungs, successions,\\\\n     7\\\\tview_switches, views_fts for v68 (no evidence_links or judgements existed). The sealed folder is untouched and remains the record;\\\\n     8\\\\tthe front end, the API and the page build read this copy.\\\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3509:- Alex, after the browser check showed v49's state as \\\\\\\"No No restriction adopted\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"修，然后 merge main\\\\\\\".\\\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510:- Mechanism: the state chip and the chart's spoken text join the score and the rung label. A two-rung ladder's score is Yes/No; when the ladder names its outcomes (06-views allows named outcomes for yes/no theme theses), the label repeats it. Census: 1 of 55 two-rung theses in the served ledger (v49: Restriction adopted / No restriction adopted) and 1 in the 2026-10-27 snapshot (Permission granted / Permission not granted).\\\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3512:- Result: the D336 UI test fails on the old composition (\\\\\\\"No No restriction adopted\\\\\\\"); 58 UI tests, lint, format and the 20 standing UI mutation checks pass. In headless Chrome, with the cache disabled, v49 shows \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" and v14 \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\".\\\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:302:  named.rungs[0].label = 'Restriction adopted';\\\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:303:  named.rungs[1].label = 'No restriction adopted';\\\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:308:  assert.equal(stateText(thesis, 2), 'No restriction adopted');\\\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:311:    '<span class=\\\\\\\"chip chip--state state--negative\\\\\\\"><b>No restriction adopted</b></span>',\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:80:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_41\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"1. **The single export closes the old routes if the release builder takes its data only from that exporter.** That covers the idea card, both places where its summary re-reads the ladder, the closing sentence, the live `/library` reload, translated JSON and composite trials. One detail still matters at handoff. A marker and version identify a format. They cannot establish who supplied the text in an allowed field. Have the builder call the exporter directly, and check the finished package as well as the page. The current builder accepts external JSON, embeds market data and trials separately, and writes beside the translated export. A page can make zero fetches while its package still contains the unrestricted file. [Design §2:35](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20) · [mock_build.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:54) · [mock_translate.py:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:129) · [idea.py:346](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:346)\\\\n\\\\n2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\\\n\\\\n3. **Recommend (a) for the first release. Option (b) is measurable, but §4 overstates what it proves.** I matched each Yes/No judgement to its archived request by call ID and request hash. Counting requests with no directly shown number-question state, (b) would keep **31/769**, **44/776** and **43/958** explanations across the three comparison runs. For a reader viewing the latest answer, it would keep explanations on **21/85 questions**. It would also keep **73/73** historical explanations in the sealed ledger. That is the benefit Alex would give up under (a). The limit is that a request also includes the question’s previous reasoning and can include another Yes/No question’s reasoning. Either can carry a forecast it saw earlier. Checking the current request for a directly shown number question cannot justify §4’s promise that the explanation “cannot quote a number forecast.” Both known disclosures are specifically in `why_changed`, including “around $1 trillion” in `old-3/v36`. [Design §4:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:84) · [archived requests:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:40) · [judgement-to-request link:308](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:308) · [reasoning copied into requests:202](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:202) · [stored cases:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27)\\\\n\\\\n4. **Before handoff, write one end-to-end acceptance case around what the reader gets.** Use `old-1/v8` as the only question in an idea. Its sources and “Forecast unavailable” must survive onto the card, with no scored driver and no invented replacement band. This matters because the current idea code expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate. In the same release package, verify that the two known event answers retain their labels and omit the spending forecasts under Alex’s chosen prose rule. Keep the design’s separate real closing-switch check. This review was read-only and cost $0. [idea_composite.py:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:214) · [idea_composite.py:231](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:231) · [design acceptance:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:115) · [Alex’s release decision:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833)\\\\n\\\\n**Verdict — not ready as written.** Keep the single exporter and §3. Make the package boundary enforceable, apply one prose rule across overlapping event and Yes/No questions, and put the measured trade-off to Alex with **(a)** recommended.\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:3:2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:86:binary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r73.stream:15:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\\\n     4\\\\t- D726, \\\\\\\"同意\\\\\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\",\\\\n     5\\\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\\\\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\\\\\";\\\\n     6\\\\t- D756, \\\\\\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\\\\\".\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\\\n    11\\\\tcould reach a reader:\\\\n    12\\\\t- the idea card;\\\\n    13\\\\t- the closing text;\\\\n    14\\\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\\\n    15\\\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\\\n    16\\\\t- a translated export;\\\\n    17\\\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\n    19\\\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\\\\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\\\n    20\\\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\\\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\n    22\\\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\\\n    25\\\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\\\n    26\\\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\\\\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\\\\\".\\\\n    27\\\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\\\n    28\\\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\\\\\"around $1 trillion\\\\\\\" for 2027 spending;\\\\n    29\\\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\\\n    36\\\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\\\n    37\\\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\\\n    38\\\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\\\n    39\\\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\\\n    40\\\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\\\n    41\\\\t  - no live POC service;\\\\n    42\\\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\\\n    43\\\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\\\n    44\\\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\\\n    45\\\\t\\\\n    46\\\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\\\n    47\\\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\\\n    48\\\\t  - the question and its id;\\\\n    49\\\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\\\n    50\\\\t  - the marker \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\".\\\\n    51\\\\t\\\\n    52\\\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\\\n    53\\\\t  - no ladder;\\\\n    54\\\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\\\n    55\\\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\\\n    56\\\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\\\n    57\\\\t  - no closing band (\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" only);\\\\n    58\\\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\\\n    59\\\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\\\n    60\\\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\\\n    61\\\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\\\n    62\\\\t  delivered card.\\\\n    63\\\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\\\n    64\\\\t  later choice for Alex.\\\\n    65\\\\t\\\\n    66\\\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\\\n    69\\\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\\\n    70\\\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\\\n    71\\\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\\\n    72\\\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\\\n    73\\\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\\\n    76\\\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\\\n    77\\\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\n    79\\\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\\\n    80\\\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\\\n    81\\\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\\\n    82\\\\t\\\\n    83\\\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\\\n    86\\\\tbinary event such as \\\\\\\"Restriction adopted\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\\\n    87\\\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\n    91\\\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\\\n    92\\\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\\\n    93\\\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\\\n    94\\\\t  readers would see.\\\\n    95\\\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\\\n    96\\\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\\\n    97\\\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\\\n    98\\\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\\\n    99\\\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\\\n   100\\\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\\\n   101\\\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\\\n   102\\\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\\\n   103\\\\t  `why_changed`.\\\\n   104\\\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\\\n   105\\\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\\\n   110\\\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\\\n   111\\\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\\\n   112\\\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\\\n   113\\\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\\\n   114\\\\t  - an event question;\\\\n   115\\\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\\\n   116\\\\t  - a real closing switch;\\\\n   117\\\\t  - an idea.\\\\n   118\\\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\\\n   119\\\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\\\n   120\\\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\\\n   121\\\\t- **Mutants:**\\\\n   122\\\\t  - an extra field;\\\\n   123\\\\t  - a fetch left on;\\\\n   124\\\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\\\n   125\\\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\\\n   126\\\\t\\\\n   127\\\\t  Each must fail.\\\\n   128\\\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\\\n   129\\\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\", with no scored driver and no\\\\n   130\\\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\\\n   131\\\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\\\n   132\\\\t    prose rule.\\\\n   133\\\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\\\n   134\\\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\\\n   135\\\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\\\n   136\\\\t    final band there.\\\\n   137\\\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\\\n   138\\\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\\\n   139\\\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\\\n   140\\\\t\\\\n   141\\\\t## 6. Not in scope\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\\\n   144\\\\t- The closed v13s line.\\\\n   145\\\\t- Other open defects.\\\\n   146\\\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\\\n   147\\\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:11:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t1. **The single export closes the old routes if the release builder takes its data only from that exporter.** That covers the idea card, both places where its summary re-reads the ladder, the closing sentence, the live `/library` reload, translated JSON and composite trials. One detail still matters at handoff. A marker and version identify a format. They cannot establish who supplied the text in an allowed field. Have the builder call the exporter directly, and check the finished package as well as the page. The current builder accepts external JSON, embeds market data and trials separately, and writes beside the translated export. A page can make zero fetches while its package still contains the unrestricted file. [Design §2:35](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20) · [mock_build.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:54) · [mock_translate.py:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:129) · [idea.py:346](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:346)\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\n     5\\\\t3. **Recommend (a) for the first release. Option (b) is measurable, but §4 overstates what it proves.** I matched each Yes/No judgement to its archived request by call ID and request hash. Counting requests with no directly shown number-question state, (b) would keep **31/769**, **44/776** and **43/958** explanations across the three comparison runs. For a reader viewing the latest answer, it would keep explanations on **21/85 questions**. It would also keep **73/73** historical explanations in the sealed ledger. That is the benefit Alex would give up under (a). The limit is that a request also includes the question’s previous reasoning and can include another Yes/No question’s reasoning. Either can carry a forecast it saw earlier. Checking the current request for a directly shown number question cannot justify §4’s promise that the explanation “cannot quote a number forecast.” Both known disclosures are specifically in `why_changed`, including “around $1 trillion” in `old-3/v36`. [Design §4:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:84) · [archived requests:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:40) · [judgement-to-request link:308](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:308) · [reasoning copied into requests:202](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:202) · [stored cases:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27)\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\n     7\\\\t4. **Before handoff, write one end-to-end acceptance case around what the reader gets.** Use `old-1/v8` as the only question in an idea. Its sources and “Forecast unavailable” must survive onto the card, with no scored driver and no invented replacement band. This matters because the current idea code expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate. In the same release package, verify that the two known event answers retain their labels and omit the spending forecasts under Alex’s chosen prose rule. Keep the design’s separate real closing-switch check. This review was read-only and cost $0. [idea_composite.py:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:214) · [idea_composite.py:231](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:231) · [design acceptance:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:115) · [Alex’s release decision:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833)\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\n     9\\\\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** Keep the single exporter and §3. Make the package boundary enforceable, apply one prose rule across overlapping event and Yes/No questions, and put the measured trade-off to Alex with **(a)** recommended.\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:13:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\\\n     4\\\\t- D726, \\\\\\\"同意\\\\\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\",\\\\n     5\\\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\\\\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\\\\\";\\\\n     6\\\\t- D756, \\\\\\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\\\\\".\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\\\n    11\\\\tcould reach a reader:\\\\n    12\\\\t- the idea card;\\\\n    13\\\\t- the closing text;\\\\n    14\\\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\\\n    15\\\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\\\n    16\\\\t- a translated export;\\\\n    17\\\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\n    19\\\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\\\\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\\\n    20\\\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\\\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\n    22\\\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\\\n    25\\\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\\\n    26\\\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\\\\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\\\\\".\\\\n    27\\\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\\\n    28\\\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\\\\\"around $1 trillion\\\\\\\" for 2027 spending;\\\\n    29\\\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\\\n    36\\\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\\\n    37\\\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\\\n    38\\\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\\\n    39\\\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\\\n    40\\\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\\\n    41\\\\t  - no live POC service;\\\\n    42\\\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\\\n    43\\\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\\\n    44\\\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\\\n    45\\\\t\\\\n    46\\\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\\\n    47\\\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\\\n    48\\\\t  - the question and its id;\\\\n    49\\\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\\\n    50\\\\t  - the marker \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\".\\\\n    51\\\\t\\\\n    52\\\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\\\n    53\\\\t  - no ladder;\\\\n    54\\\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\\\n    55\\\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\\\n    56\\\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\\\n    57\\\\t  - no closing band (\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" only);\\\\n    58\\\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\\\n    59\\\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\\\n    60\\\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\\\n    61\\\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\\\n    62\\\\t  delivered card.\\\\n    63\\\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\\\n    64\\\\t  later choice for Alex.\\\\n    65\\\\t\\\\n    66\\\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\\\n    69\\\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\\\n    70\\\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\\\n    71\\\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\\\n    72\\\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\\\n    73\\\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\\\n    76\\\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\\\n    77\\\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\n    79\\\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\\\n    80\\\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\\\n    81\\\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\\\n    82\\\\t\\\\n    83\\\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\\\n    86\\\\tbinary event such as \\\\\\\"Restriction adopted\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\\\n    87\\\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\n    91\\\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\\\n    92\\\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\\\n    93\\\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\\\n    94\\\\t  readers would see.\\\\n    95\\\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\\\n    96\\\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown). It keeps the reasoning where it\\\\n    97\\\\t  cannot quote a number forecast.\\\\n    98\\\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\\\n    99\\\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\\\n   100\\\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\\\n   101\\\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\\\n   102\\\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\\\n   103\\\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\\\n   104\\\\t  `why_changed`.\\\\n   105\\\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\\\n   106\\\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\\\n   107\\\\t\\\\n   108\\\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\\\n   109\\\\t\\\\n   110\\\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\\\n   111\\\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\\\n   112\\\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\\\n   113\\\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\\\n   114\\\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\\\n   115\\\\t  - an event question;\\\\n   116\\\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\\\n   117\\\\t  - a real closing switch;\\\\n   118\\\\t  - an idea.\\\\n   119\\\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\\\n   120\\\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\\\n   121\\\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\\\n   122\\\\t- **Mutants:**\\\\n   123\\\\t  - an extra field;\\\\n   124\\\\t  - a fetch left on;\\\\n   125\\\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\\\n   126\\\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\\\n   127\\\\t\\\\n   128\\\\t  Each must fail.\\\\n   129\\\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\\\n   130\\\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\", with no scored driver and no\\\\n   131\\\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\\\n   132\\\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\\\n   133\\\\t    prose rule.\\\\n   134\\\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\\\n   135\\\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\\\n   136\\\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\\\n   137\\\\t    final band there.\\\\n   138\\\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\\\n   139\\\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\\\n   140\\\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\\\n   141\\\\t\\\\n   142\\\\t## 6. Not in scope\\\\n   143\\\\t\\\\n   144\\\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\\\n   145\\\\t- The closed v13s line.\\\\n   146\\\\t- Other open defects.\\\\n   147\\\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\\\n   148\\\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:40:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,difflib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"); s=json.loads((p/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"codex-r72c.stream\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").read_text().splitlines()[14])[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"][\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]; a=[l.split(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",1)[1] for l in s.splitlines()]; b=(p/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").read_text().splitlines();print(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,n=0)))'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"--- \\\\n\\\\n+++ \\\\n\\\\n@@ -10 +10 @@\\\\n\\\\n-**Revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\\\n+**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\\\n@@ -36,0 +37,3 @@\\\\n\\\\n+- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\\\n+  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\\\n+  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\\\n@@ -82 +85,5 @@\\\\n\\\\n-## 4. Yes/No questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n+**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\\\n+binary event such as \\\\\\\"Restriction adopted\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"No restriction adopted\\\\\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\\\n+every question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\\\n+\\\\n+## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\\\n@@ -91,2 +98,9 @@\\\\n\\\\n-- **Claude's lean is (b).** It keeps value and is decided by structure. It needs a $0 census of how many Yes/No judgements it keeps\\\\n-  on the stored stores before release.\\\\n+- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\\\n+  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\\\n+  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\\\n+  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\\\n+- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\\\n+  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\\\n+  `why_changed`.\\\\n+- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\\\n+  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\\\n@@ -114,0 +129,5 @@\\\\n\\\\n+- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\\\n+  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\", with no scored driver and no\\\\n+    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\\\n+  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\\\n+    prose rule.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | head -n 248'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\\n     2\\tevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\\n     3\\tswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\\n     4\\tend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     5\\timport json\\n     6\\tfrom contextlib import contextmanager\\n     7\\tfrom datetime import date\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tfrom . import service\\n    10\\tfrom .views import store\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t@contextmanager\\n    14\\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\\n    15\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    16\\t    owned = []\\n    17\\t    try:\\n    18\\t        for conn in connections:\\n    19\\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\\n    20\\t                conn.execute('begin')\\n    21\\t                owned.append(conn)\\n    22\\t        yield\\n    23\\t    finally:\\n    24\\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\\n    25\\t            conn.rollback()\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\\n    30\\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    31\\t    cache = {}\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t    def item_of(input_id):\\n    34\\t        if input_id not in cache:\\n    35\\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\\n    36\\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\\n    37\\t        return cache[input_id]\\n    38\\t    return item_of\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\\n    42\\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's ladder as the new system's writer stored it (`clean_ladders`, written in the view's own call): the parsed\\n    47\\t    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\\n    48\\t    view. A row that is not readable JSON with a ladder, or two rows for one view, is refused.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49\\t    if not views_db.execute(\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where type='table' and name='clean_ladders'\\\").fetchone():\\n    50\\t        return 'no table'\\n    51\\t    rows = views_db.execute('select checked_answer from clean_ladders where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchall()\\n    52\\t    if not rows:\\n    53\\t        return 'no row'\\n    54\\t    if len(rows) > 1:\\n    55\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: {len(rows)} ladder rows for one view')\\n    56\\t    try:\\n    57\\t        ladder = json.loads(rows[0][0])['ladder']\\n    58\\t    except (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError) as error:\\n    59\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder ({error!r})')\\n    60\\t    if not isinstance(ladder, dict):\\n    61\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder')\\n    62\\t    return ladder\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\tdef not_judged(views_db, view_id, created_seq, as_of=None):\\n    66\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"D397: the parts of a topic its one judged question leaves out, with their reasons, from the view's ladder row. None for a\\n    67\\t    legacy ledger, for a view with no row, and before the view's creation at as_of; [] when the row lists none. A malformed row,\\n    68\\t    or two rows for one view, is refused. Called directly for a view not visible at the resolved bound, it refuses the view\\n    69\\t    (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3), so a question created after that day is never returned.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    70\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n    71\\t    if as_of is not None and not _visible(views_db, created_seq, as_of):\\n    72\\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n    73\\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\\n    74\\t    if ladder in ('no table', 'no row'):\\n    75\\t        return None\\n    76\\t    parts = ladder.get('not_judged')\\n    77\\t    if not isinstance(parts, list) or not all(isinstance(p, dict) and isinstance(p.get('part'), str) and isinstance(p.get('why'), str) for p in parts):\\n    78\\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its parts not judged are not a list of {{part, why}} texts')\\n    79\\t    return [{'part': p['part'], 'why': p['why']} for p in parts]\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\tdef answer_shape(views_db, view_id):\\n    83\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"(shape, favourable end) of the view's answer choices, as the page needs them to read the stored labels without inventing a\\n    84\\t    direction (page-contract/DESIGN.md): (None, None) for a legacy ledger; ('unrecorded', None) for a view with no row in a store\\n    85\\t    that has rows; ('event', None) or ('figure', 'higher' | 'lower' | 'n/a') from the row. Not suppressed before creation: it says\\n    86\\t    how to read the labels, which are shown as they are.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    87\\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\\n    88\\t    if ladder == 'no table':\\n    89\\t        return None, None\\n    90\\t    if ladder == 'no row':\\n    91\\t        return 'unrecorded', None\\n    92\\t    if ladder.get('event'):\\n    93\\t        return 'event', None\\n    94\\t    figure = ladder.get('figure')\\n    95\\t    if isinstance(figure, dict) and figure.get('favourable_end') in ('higher', 'lower', 'n/a'):\\n    96\\t        return 'figure', figure['favourable_end']\\n    97\\t    raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row is neither an event nor a figure with a favourable end')\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\tdef view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\\n   101\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One view's complete record as of the bound (resolved; an omitted bound on a store with no completed day reads every\\n   102\\t    record, as before). A view not visible at the bound is refused (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   103\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n   104\\t    v = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   105\\t    if v is None:\\n   106\\t        raise KeyError(view_id)\\n   107\\t    if as_of is not None and not service.view_exists(views_db, v, as_of):\\n   108\\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n   109\\t    columns = {r[1] for r in views_db.execute('pragma table_info(rungs)')}\\n   110\\t    bounds = ', lo, hi' if {'lo', 'hi'} <= columns else ''          # a ledger written before keys has no bounds; the adapter then reads the prose\\n   111\\t    rungs = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute(f'select position, label, condition{bounds} from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n   112\\t    switches = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,))\\n   113\\t                if _visible(views_db, r['after_seq'], as_of)]\\n   114\\t    for switch in switches:\\n   115\\t        switch['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, switch['after_seq'])\\n   116\\t    judgements = []\\n   117\\t    for j in views_db.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\\n   118\\t        if as_of is not None and j['publication_day'] > as_of:\\n   119\\t            continue\\n   120\\t        judgements.append({'id': str(j['judgement_id']), 'day': j['publication_day'], 'seq': j['seq'], 'rung': j['rung'], 'changed': bool(j['changed']),\\n   121\\t                           'why_changed': j['why_changed'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'cited': list(dict.fromkeys(json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json'] or '[]'))),   # each id once (UI contract uniqueItems); the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger holds one judgement citing an id twice\\n   122\\t                           'cited_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json'] or '[]'), 'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json'] or '[]'),\\n   123\\t                           'from_item': j['input_id']})\\n   124\\t    evidence = []\\n   125\\t    for e in views_db.execute('select e.*, l.seq as linked_seq from evidence_links l join evidence e on e.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by l.id', (view_id,)):\\n   126\\t        if not _visible(views_db, e['linked_seq'], as_of):\\n   127\\t            continue\\n   128\\t        sources = [dict(s) for s in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (e['evidence_id'],))\\n   129\\t                   if _visible(views_db, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   130\\t        replaced_by = views_db.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   131\\t        if replaced_by is not None and not _visible(views_db, replaced_by['seq'], as_of):\\n   132\\t            replaced_by = None\\n   133\\t        replaces = views_db.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   134\\t        if replaces and not _visible(views_db, replaces['seq'], as_of):\\n   135\\t            replaces = None\\n   136\\t        first = sources[0] if sources else {'input_id': e['created_from_input'], 'publication_day': '', 'seq': e['created_seq']}\\n   137\\t        item = item_of(first['input_id'])\\n   138\\t        evidence.append({'id': e['evidence_id'], 'one_line': e['one_line'], 'quote': e['quote'], 'tier': e['tier'], 'speaker': e['speaker'],\\n   139\\t                         'original_who': e['original_who'], 'original_day': e['original_day'], 'event_time': e['event_time'],\\n   140\\t                         'day': first['publication_day'] or item['publication_day'], 'seq': first['seq'], 'linked_seq': e['linked_seq'],\\n   141\\t                         'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, e['linked_seq']),\\n   142\\t                         'source': {'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'publisher_type': item['publisher_type'],\\n   143\\t                                    'category': item['category'], 'uri': item['source_uri']},\\n   144\\t                         'sources': [{'input_id': s['input_id'], 'day': s['publication_day'],\\n   145\\t                                      'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, s['seq']),\\n   146\\t                                      'source': item_of(s['input_id'])} for s in sources],\\n   147\\t                         'outlets': len(sources), 'replaced_by': {'new_evidence_id': replaced_by['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': replaced_by['said_day'],\\n   148\\t                                                               'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, replaced_by['seq'])} if replaced_by else None,\\n   149\\t                         'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces else None})\\n   150\\t    dependencies = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select dependency_id, depends_on, direction, wait_chain_view_id, wait_year, seq from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,))\\n   151\\t                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   152\\t    for dependency in dependencies:\\n   153\\t        dependency['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, dependency['seq'])\\n   154\\t        dependency['resolutions'] = [dict(target=r['resolved_to'], day=service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq']), seq=r['seq'])\\n   155\\t                                    for r in views_db.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id', (dependency['dependency_id'],))\\n   156\\t                                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   157\\t    dependants = sorted({r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)},\\n   158\\t                        key=lambda s: (len(s), s))\\n   159\\t    created = item_of(v['created_from_input'])\\n   160\\t    key = store.view_key(views_db, view_id)\\n   161\\t    identity = {name: key[name] for name in ('measure', 'scope', 'period_start', 'period_end', 'basis', 'unit', 'event_type')} if key else None\\n   162\\t    successions = [{'thesis_id': r['succeeds'] if r['view_id'] == view_id else r['view_id'],\\n   163\\t                    'relation': 'previous' if r['view_id'] == view_id else 'next',\\n   164\\t                    'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq'])}\\n   165\\t                   for r in views_db.execute('select * from successions where view_id=? or succeeds=? order by id', (view_id, view_id))\\n   166\\t                   if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\\n   167\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'object': v['object_id'], 'kind': v['kind'], 'looks_at': v['looks_at'], 'question': v['question'],\\n   168\\t            'due_day': v['due_day'], 'year': v['year'], 'identity': identity, 'successions': successions,\\n   169\\t            'created_seq': v['created_seq'], 'created_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, v['created_seq']),\\n   170\\t            'created_from': {'title': created['title'], 'publisher': created['publisher'], 'category': created['category']},\\n   171\\t            'rungs': rungs, 'open': not any(not s['open'] for s in switches), 'switches': switches,\\n   172\\t            'judgements': judgements, 'evidence': evidence, 'dependencies': dependencies, 'dependants': dependants,\\n   173\\t            'not_judged': not_judged(views_db, view_id, v['created_seq'], as_of),\\n   174\\t            **dict(zip(('answer_shape', 'favourable_end'), answer_shape(views_db, view_id)))}\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\tdef days(views_db, as_of=None):\\n   178\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The completed days the front end's time axis runs over, up to as_of.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   179\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\\n   180\\t    return [r[0] for r in views_db.execute('select day from days_completed order by day') if as_of is None or r[0] <= as_of]\\n   181\\t\\n   182\\t\\n   183\\tdef _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\\n   184\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Complete, dated UI inputs for caller-selected theses; no search, model call or ledger write. Its bound is already resolved\\n   185\\t    by its caller (`thesis_bundles`, `library`).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   186\\t    date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   187\\t    if not isinstance(view_ids, list) or not view_ids or any(not isinstance(id, str) or not id for id in view_ids):\\n   188\\t        raise ValueError('thesis_bundles needs a non-empty list of view ids')\\n   189\\t    lookup = item_lookup(items_db)\\n   190\\t    records = []\\n   191\\t    for view_id in dict.fromkeys(view_ids):\\n   192\\t        row = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   193\\t        if row is None or not service.view_exists(views_db, row, as_of):\\n   194\\t            raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\\n   195\\t        records.append(view_bundle(views_db, lookup, view_id, as_of))\\n   196\\t    return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': records,\\n   197\\t            'coverage': coverage, 'groups': research_groups(views_db, view_ids, as_of)}\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\tdef research_groups(conn, view_ids, as_of):\\n   201\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Stored groups, with dated memberships limited to the envelope's loaded theses.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   202\\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_groups)').fetchone():\\n   203\\t        return []\\n   204\\t    loaded = set(view_ids)\\n   205\\t    result = []\\n   206\\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from thesis_groups order by created_seq, rowid'):\\n   207\\t        if not service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of):\\n   208\\t            continue\\n   209\\t        members = [{'thesis_id': m['view_id'], 'day': service.day_of_seq(conn, m['seq']), 'basis': m['basis'] or ''}\\n   210\\t                   for m in conn.execute('select * from thesis_group_members where group_id=? order by id', (row['group_id'],))\\n   211\\t                   if m['view_id'] in loaded and service.visible(conn, m['seq'], as_of)]\\n   212\\t        if members:\\n   213\\t            result.append({'id': row['group_id'], 'name': row['name'], 'scope': row['scope'],\\n   214\\t                           'aliases': json.loads(row['aliases'] or '[]') if 'aliases' in row.keys() else [],\\n   215\\t                           'created_day': service.day_of_seq(conn, row['created_seq']), 'members': members})\\n   216\\t    return result\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\tdef thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\\n   220\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   221\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   222\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\\n   228\\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\\n   229\\t        if not as_of:\\n   230\\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\\n   231\\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\\n   232\\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\\n   233\\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\\n   234\\t        if not view_ids:\\n   235\\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\\n   236\\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '8,106p;158,172p;223,242p;348,379p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | head -n 55\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     8\\timport json\\n     9\\timport os\\n    10\\timport re\\n    11\\timport sqlite3\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\tTABLES = {\\n    14\\t    'views': 'view_id text primary key, object_id text, object_kind text, kind text, looks_at text, question text, due_day text, year text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text, created_at text',\\n    15\\t    'rungs': 'view_id text, position integer, label text, condition text, lo real, hi real',\\n    16\\t    'view_keys': 'view_id text primary key, measure text, scope text, scope_key text, period_start text, period_end text, basis text, unit text, event_type text, seq integer, scope_source text, key_version integer',\\n    17\\t    'view_switches': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, open integer, reason text, by_whom text, after_seq integer',\\n    18\\t    'judgements': 'judgement_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, rung integer, reasons text, cited_evidence_json text, cited_views_json text, pushes_json text, changed integer, why_changed text, config_checksum text, call_id integer, request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text, reference text, implied_outcome text',\\n    19\\t    'evidence': 'evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\\n    20\\t    'evidence_sources': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, input_id text, category text, publication_day text, location text, seq integer',\\n    21\\t    'evidence_links': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, view_id text, seq integer',\\n    22\\t    'replacements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',   # history: written before D202, read as before\\n    23\\t    'revisions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',      # D202: the new piece revises the old; both stay in force\\n    24\\t    'same_claims': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer',                    # D204: the matcher read the new piece as the same claim as the old; both stored, both in force\\n    25\\t    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer, kind text default \\\\'\\\\'',   # kind: '' (a seed's or the generative matcher's row, read as before) or 'reads' (a chosen reading link, D694)\\n    26\\t    'dependency_resolutions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer',\\n    27\\t    'successions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer',\\n    28\\t    'handovers': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text',\\n    29\\t    'match_records': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text',\\n    30\\t    'processing_steps': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text',\\n    31\\t    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\\n    32\\t    'late_statements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer',\\n    33\\t    'days_completed': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text',\\n    34\\t    # D694: how the links of an article were chosen (views/links.py), append-only per attempt: proposed, then committed or failed\\n    35\\t    'link_selections': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, attempt_id text, seq integer, input_id text, config_checksum text, status text, record_json text',\\n    36\\t    # D149 research groups: an ongoing business subject several distinct theses belong to; membership is decided by extraction and written with the thesis\\n    37\\t    'thesis_groups': 'group_id text primary key, name text, scope text, aliases text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\\n    38\\t    'thesis_group_members': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, basis text',\\n    39\\t    # D166 (2026-11-01): the names a later declaration gives a stored group, appended once each; a group's aliases are its creation's plus these\\n    40\\t    'thesis_group_aliases': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, alias text, seq integer, input_id text',\\n    41\\t}\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\tINDEXES = [\\n    44\\t    'create index if not exists views_object on views(object_id)',\\n    45\\t    'create index if not exists judgements_view on judgements(view_id, judgement_id)',\\n    46\\t    # 06-views step 7: a view is judged once per round (one item = one sequence number)\\n    47\\t    'create unique index if not exists judgements_once_per_round on judgements(view_id, seq)',\\n    48\\t    'create index if not exists links_view on evidence_links(view_id)',\\n    49\\t    'create index if not exists links_evidence on evidence_links(evidence_id)',\\n    50\\t    'create index if not exists sources_evidence on evidence_sources(evidence_id)',\\n    51\\t    'create index if not exists steps_input on processing_steps(input_id, id)',\\n    52\\t    'create index if not exists switches_view on view_switches(view_id, id)',\\n    53\\t    'create index if not exists deps_view on dependencies(view_id)',\\n    54\\t]\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tdef open_db(path):\\n    58\\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\\n    59\\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\\n    60\\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\\n    61\\t    for name, columns in TABLES.items():\\n    62\\t        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({columns})')\\n    63\\t        conn.execute(f\\\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\\\")\\n    64\\t        conn.execute(f\\\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\\\")\\n    65\\t    for statement in INDEXES:\\n    66\\t        conn.execute(statement)\\n    67\\t    ensure_writable_columns(conn)\\n    68\\t    conn.execute(\\\"create virtual table if not exists views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\\\")\\n    69\\t    conn.execute(\\\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\\\")\\n    70\\t    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\\n    71\\t    conn.commit()\\n    72\\t    return conn\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tdef insert(conn, table, **fields):\\n    76\\t    columns = list(fields)\\n    77\\t    cursor = conn.execute(f'insert into {table} ({\\\",\\\".join(columns)}) values ({\\\",\\\".join(\\\"?\\\" * len(columns))})', [fields[c] for c in columns])\\n    78\\t    return cursor.lastrowid\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t# ---------- views ----------\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tdef create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\\n    84\\t    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\\n    85\\t           question=question, due_day=due_day, year=year, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id, created_at=created_at)\\n    86\\t    for position, rung in enumerate(rungs, start=1):\\n    87\\t        insert(conn, 'rungs', view_id=view_id, position=position, label=rung['label'], condition=rung['condition'], lo=rung.get('lo'), hi=rung.get('hi'))\\n    88\\t    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\\n    89\\t    conn.execute('insert into views_fts (view_id, text) values (?, ?)', (view_id, f'{object_id} {looks_at} {question}'))\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\tdef view(conn, view_id):\\n    93\\t    row = conn.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n    94\\t    return dict(row) if row else None\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\tdef rungs_of(conn, view_id):\\n    98\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The rungs with their bounds when the ledger has them (keyed views); a ledger written before keys has no lo/hi columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    99\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\\n   100\\t    has_bounds = any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rows) or view_key(conn, view_id) is not None\\n   101\\t    return [dict(position=r['position'], label=r['label'], condition=r['condition'],\\n   102\\t                 **({'lo': r.get('lo'), 'hi': r.get('hi')} if has_bounds else {})) for r in rows]\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\tdef add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\\n   106\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The view's key (keyed-views-plan.md 2.1), written once with the view.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\tdef view_key(conn, view_id):\\n   160\\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(view_keys)').fetchone():\\n   161\\t        return None\\n   162\\t    row = conn.execute('select * from view_keys where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   163\\t    if not row:\\n   164\\t        return None\\n   165\\t    key = dict(row)\\n   166\\t    if not key.get('scope_source'):\\n   167\\t        key['scope_source'] = 'none' if not key['scope'] else 'model'\\n   168\\t    return key\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\tdef open_views_with_key(conn, object_id, measure, scope_key, period_start, period_end, basis='n/a', unit='n/a', event_type=None):\\n   172\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Open views of the object with the same measure, scope and unit whose period overlaps: the ones a candidate must\\n   223\\tdef open_read_only(path):\\n   224\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The views database for a reader (the agent layer, reports): no schema creation, no writes. Opened by its own path: a symlink\\n   225\\t    resolved, a store with another hard link refused (`live_lock.LockRefused`; live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 7), since\\n   226\\t    SQLite finds a WAL store's side files by the opened path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    from hivemind import live_lock\\n   228\\t    real, _ = live_lock.own_path(path)\\n   229\\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{real}?mode=ro', uri=True, timeout=READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\\n   230\\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\\n   231\\t    return conn\\n   232\\t\\n   233\\t\\n   234\\tdef current_state(conn, view_id):\\n   235\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The latest judgement: rung, reasons, changed, seq and day, and its reference and implied outcome (D260) where the ledger has them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   236\\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\\n   237\\t    stance = ''.join(f', {field}' for field in ('reference', 'implied_outcome') if field in columns)\\n   238\\t    row = conn.execute(f'select judgement_id, rung, reasons, changed, seq, publication_day{stance} from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\\n   239\\t    return dict(row) if row else None\\n   240\\t\\n   241\\t\\n   242\\tdef dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\\n   348\\t    except sqlite3.OperationalError:\\n   349\\t        return []\\n   350\\t    return [r['view_id'] for r in rows]\\n   351\\t\\n   352\\t\\n   353\\t# ---------- evidence ----------\\n   354\\t\\n   355\\tdef add_evidence(conn, *, evidence_id, quote, one_line, speaker, original_who, original_day, tier, event_time, seq, input_id):\\n   356\\t    insert(conn, 'evidence', evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=quote, one_line=one_line, speaker=speaker, original_who=original_who,\\n   357\\t           original_day=original_day, tier=tier, event_time=event_time, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id)\\n   358\\t\\n   359\\t\\n   360\\tdef add_source(conn, evidence_id, input_id, category, publication_day, location, seq):\\n   361\\t    insert(conn, 'evidence_sources', evidence_id=evidence_id, input_id=input_id, category=category, publication_day=publication_day, location=location, seq=seq)\\n   362\\t\\n   363\\t\\n   364\\tdef link(conn, evidence_id, view_id, seq):\\n   365\\t    exists = conn.execute('select 1 from evidence_links where evidence_id=? and view_id=?', (evidence_id, view_id)).fetchone()\\n   366\\t    if not exists:\\n   367\\t        insert(conn, 'evidence_links', evidence_id=evidence_id, view_id=view_id, seq=seq)\\n   368\\t        return True\\n   369\\t    return False\\n   370\\t\\n   371\\t\\n   372\\tdef replace(conn, old_id, new_id, said_day, seq):\\n   373\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Retires old_id (history before D202; kept for the readers and tests of stored ledgers, no longer called by the writer).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   374\\t    insert(conn, 'replacements', old_evidence_id=old_id, new_evidence_id=new_id, said_day=said_day, seq=seq)\\n   375\\t\\n   376\\t\\n   377\\tdef revise(conn, old_id, new_id, said_day, seq):\\n   378\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"D202: new_id is the matcher's later version of old_id; both stay in force, the judge sees the path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   379\\t    insert(conn, 'revisions', old_evidence_id=old_id, new_evidence_id=new_id, said_day=said_day, seq=seq)\\n     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"The canonical English values of every closed field the pipeline reads (D163, docs/research/2026-10-25-english/plan.md,\\n     2\\t\\\"Canonical vocabulary\\\"), and the exact legacy-to-canonical conversion of the values the Chinese prompt versions wrote.\\n     3\\t\\n     4\\tA value is converted only where an answer or a stored record is read for comparison; prose is never touched, rows are\\n     5\\tnever rewritten, and an unknown value passes through unchanged so that the schema or the code check that owns the\\n     6\\tfield refuses it as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tKINDS = ['asset', 'theme']\\n     9\\tTIERS = ['fact', 'party_statement', 'third_party_view', 'rumour']\\n    10\\tCANDIDATE_OUTCOMES = ['merge', 'succession', 'new', 'skip']\\n    11\\tEVIDENCE_OUTCOMES = ['repeat', 'replace', 'new']\\n    12\\tPUSHES = ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']\\n    13\\tDIRECTIONS = ['first_is_bullish', 'last_is_bullish', 'same', 'opposite']\\n    14\\tASSET_LABELS = ['Strongly bullish', 'Bullish', 'Neutral', 'Bearish', 'Strongly bearish']\\n    15\\tYES_NO = ['Yes', 'No']\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\tLEGACY = {\\n    18\\t    'kind': {'对象观点': 'asset', '主题观点': 'theme'},\\n    19\\t    'tier': {'发生的事': 'fact', '当事人说的': 'party_statement', '第三方看法': 'third_party_view', '传闻': 'rumour'},\\n    20\\t    'candidate_outcome': {'归入已有的': 'merge', '接续': 'succession', '新观点': 'new', '不开': 'skip'},\\n    21\\t    'evidence_outcome': {'重复': 'repeat', '替代': 'replace', '新证据': 'new'},\\n    22\\t    'push': {'推向第一格': 'toward_first', '推向最后一格': 'toward_last', '不推': 'none'},\\n    23\\t    'direction': {'对方第一格是看多': 'first_is_bullish', '对方最后一格是看多': 'last_is_bullish', '同向': 'same', '反向': 'opposite'},\\n    24\\t    'label': {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'},\\n    25\\t}\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tdef canonical(field, value):\\n    29\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The canonical value of a closed field: a legacy value converted, a canonical one kept, anything else unchanged.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    30\\t    if not isinstance(value, str):\\n    31\\t        return value\\n    32\\t    return LEGACY[field].get(value.strip(), value)\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\tdef legacy(field, value):\\n    36\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The Chinese spelling of a canonical value, for a request built for a Chinese prompt version.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    37\\t    for old, new in LEGACY[field].items():\\n    38\\t        if new == value:\\n    39\\t            return old\\n    40\\t    return value\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\tdef extraction_answer(data):\\n    44\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"An extraction answer with canonical kind, tier and standard rung labels; other fields untouched.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    45\\t    out = dict(data)\\n    46\\t    out['candidates'] = [dict(c, kind=canonical('kind', c.get('kind')),\\n    47\\t                              rungs=[dict(r, label=canonical('label', r.get('label'))) for r in c.get('rungs', [])]) for c in data.get('candidates', [])]\\n    48\\t    out['evidence'] = [dict(e, tier=canonical('tier', e.get('tier'))) for e in data.get('evidence', [])]\\n    49\\t    return out\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\tdef candidate(c):\\n    53\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A handover candidate (fresh or saved) with canonical kind and labels.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    54\\t    return dict(c, kind=canonical('kind', c.get('kind')), rungs=[dict(r, label=canonical('label', r.get('label'))) for r in c.get('rungs', [])])\\n    55\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:38:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '58,145p;224,256p'; rg -A20 -n 'def ladder_bands' src/hivemind/service.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    58\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\\n    61\\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\\n    62\\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\\n    63\\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    64\\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\\n    65\\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\\n    66\\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\\n    67\\t    if not bound:\\n    68\\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\\n    69\\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\\n    70\\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\\n    71\\t    return bound\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\\n    75\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\\n    76\\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\\n    77\\t    start is included; a client polling \\\"what changed since the day I last saw\\\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\\n    78\\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\\n    80\\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\\n    81\\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\\n    82\\t    return end\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\\n    89\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\\n    90\\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\\n    91\\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    92\\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\\n    93\\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\\n    94\\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\\n    95\\t        return entry[2]\\n    96\\t    cache = {}\\n    97\\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\\n    98\\t        cache[seq] = day\\n    99\\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\\n   100\\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\\n   101\\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\\n   102\\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\\n   103\\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\\n   104\\t    return cache\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\\n   108\\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\\n   112\\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\\n   113\\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t# ---------- views\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\\n   119\\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   123\\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\\n   124\\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\\n   125\\t            return bool(row['open'])\\n   126\\t    return True\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\\n   130\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   131\\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\\n   132\\t    if not rows:\\n   133\\t        return None\\n   134\\t    last = rows[-1]\\n   135\\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\\n   136\\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\\n   137\\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\\n   138\\t            previous = row['rung']\\n   139\\t            break\\n   140\\t        since = row['publication_day']\\n   141\\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\\n   142\\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t\\n   145\\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\\n   224\\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\\n   225\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\\n   226\\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   227\\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\\n   228\\t    if not piece:\\n   229\\t        return None\\n   230\\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\\n   231\\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\\n   232\\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\\n   233\\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\\n   234\\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\\n   235\\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\t\\n   238\\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\\n   239\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   240\\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\\n   241\\t    out = []\\n   242\\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\\n   243\\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\\n   244\\t            continue\\n   245\\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\\n   246\\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\\n   247\\t            continue\\n   248\\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\\n   249\\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\\n   250\\t            continue\\n   251\\t        out.append(piece)\\n   252\\t    return out\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t\\n   255\\t# ---------- history\\n   256\\t\\n499:def ladder_bands(rungs):\\n500-    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every rung's band, or None with the reason when the ladder is not one unbroken partition by amount. Rungs that\\n501-    carry numeric bounds are read from them; the prose parser serves the views written before keys.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n502-    numeric = numeric_bands(rungs)\\n503-    if numeric is not None:\\n504-        ordered = sorted(numeric.items(), key=lambda pb: pb[1][0])\\n505-        for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n506-            if a[2] != b[0]:\\n507-                return None, f'numeric bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n508-        return numeric, None\\n509-    bands = [(r['position'], band(r['condition'])) for r in rungs]\\n510-    unreadable = [p for p, b in bands if b is None]\\n511-    if unreadable:\\n512-        return None, f'conditions not read as amounts: positions {unreadable}'\\n513-    ordered = sorted(bands, key=lambda pb: (pb[1][0], pb[1][2]))\\n514-    for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\\n515-        if a[2] != b[0] or a[3] == b[1]:          # adjacent bands share the boundary amount and exactly one of them owns it\\n516-            return None, f'bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\\n517-    lowest, highest = ordered[0][1], ordered[-1][1]\\n518-    if not (lowest[0] == -INF or (lowest[0] == 0 and lowest[1])) or highest[2] != INF:     # an amount that cannot be negative may start at 0\\n519-        return None, 'the ladder does not cover the line up to +inf'\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:40:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10991,11007p;11823,11890p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md | head -n 70\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\" 10991\\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n 10992\\t\\n 10993\\t- **The questions** (after D725):\\n 10994\\t  - \\\"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\\\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\\n 10995\\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\\n 10996\\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\\n 10997\\t  - \\\"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\\\" Options: 同意\\n 10998\\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\\n 10999\\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \\\"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\\\"; \\\"同意 (推荐)\\\".\\n 11000\\t- **Decided (Alex):**\\n 11001\\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\\n 11002\\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\\n 11003\\t    ceiling.\\n 11004\\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\": the band, the\\n 11005\\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\\n 11006\\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\\n 11007\\t\\n 11823\\t## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n 11824\\t\\n 11825\\t- **The question** (after D755): \\\"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\\\"\\n 11826\\t  - Options:\\n 11827\\t    - \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\": the council's consensus;\\n 11828\\t    - \\\"换更强的模型再小测一次\\\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\\n 11829\\t    - \\\"先停，我想谈谈\\\".\\n 11830\\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\".\\n 11831\\t- **Decided (Alex):**\\n 11832\\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\\n 11833\\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", the band, the\\n 11834\\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\\n 11835\\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\\n 11836\\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" appear.\\n 11837\\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\\n 11838\\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\\n 11839\\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\\n 11840\\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\\n 11841\\t\\n 11842\\t## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n 11843\\t\\n 11844\\t- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \\\"Forecast\\n 11845\\t  unavailable\\\" (D756). D726 says it \\\"is built with the release work, which is not started\\\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\\n 11846\\t  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\\n 11847\\t- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\\n 11848\\t  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\\n 11849\\t  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\\n 11850\\t- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\\n 11851\\t  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\\n 11852\\t  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\";\\n 11853\\t  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\\n 11854\\t  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\\n 11855\\t    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\\n 11856\\t  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\\n 11857\\t  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\\n 11858\\t    approach with one structural rule.\\n 11859\\t- **Open for Alex:**\\n 11860\\t  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\\n 11861\\t  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\\n 11862\\t     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\\n 11863\\t     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\\n 11864\\t       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\\n 11865\\t- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\\n 11866\\t\\n 11867\\t## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n 11868\\t\\n 11869\\t- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \\\"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\\n 11870\\t  Production 方向去走了\\\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \\\"同意\\\"; D756 \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\"). D757 left two\\n 11871\\t  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\\n 11872\\t- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\\n 11873\\t  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\\n 11874\\t     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\\n 11875\\t     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \\\"not started\\\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\\n 11876\\t  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\\n 11877\\t     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\\n 11878\\t     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\\n 11879\\t  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\\n 11880\\t     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\\n 11881\\t  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\\n 11882\\t     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\\n 11883\\t- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\\n     1\\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t## What to review\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n     8\\trelease. The governing documents:\\n     9\\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\\n    10\\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\\n    11\\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\tCode that the design reuses:\\n    14\\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\\n    15\\t  `ladder_bands`;\\n    16\\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\\n    17\\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\\n    18\\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\\n    19\\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\\n    20\\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## Questions\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\\n    25\\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\\n    26\\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\\n    27\\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t   Name any path with a stored example.\\n    30\\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\\n    31\\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\\n    32\\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\\n    33\\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\\n    34\\t   forecast restated in different words?\\n    35\\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\\n    36\\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\\n    37\\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\\n    38\\t   - groups left out;\\n    39\\t   - the sweep floor.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t   Decide each.\\n    42\\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\\n    45\\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:42:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba README.md | sed -n '87,105p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | head -n 110; nl -ba src/hivemind/baseline.py | sed -n '163,225p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/idea.py | sed -n '115,146p;215,279p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    87\\tUse Python 3.12 or later for the backend and Node.js 22 or later with npm for frontend builds. The HTTP service uses the Python standard library. The optional MCP service needs `mcp==1.26.0`. Frontend development dependencies are locked in `poc/ui/package-lock.json`.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\tThe default backend reads these local files:\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t| Purpose | Path |\\n    92\\t|---|---|\\n    93\\t| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\\n    94\\t| Source items | `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` (cleaned pages, D351, with the whole pages as fetched in column `text_page`; also kept apart in `items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.page.sqlite`) |\\n    95\\t| Replay configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370): v108 extraction, matching and judging settings without seeded starting questions or separate report import |\\n    96\\t| Idea configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two discovery calls and a final adoption/weighting call |\\n    97\\t| Derived service index and Idea archive | `poc/data/service-english/` by default; overridable per run |\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t`poc/data/` is excluded from Git. A fresh clone includes the standalone demo, not these databases. Use the [data manifest](docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md) to locate preserved runs, or supply your own files with the documented CLI options. Keep provider credentials in the owner-only local file `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository.\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t### Switching the served data\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\tThe page build, the two services and Compose each carry the same two defaults: the thesis ledger (`views.sqlite`) and the items database the ledger's input ids come from. Swap both together; a ledger whose items are missing shows evidence without titles or sources. Serve a copy of a ledger a run may still write (`snapshot.sh` in a run folder makes one with SQLite's backup API), never the file the run writes. The places that name the defaults, all changed in one edit:\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t| Place | What to change |\\n     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"06-views.md step 6: write one item's round into the views database. Themes before objects; a repeat adds a source;\\n     2\\ta `replace` decision is recorded as a revision (D202: the new piece revises the old, both stay in force) and is ordered by the day it\\n     3\\twas said (a later-arriving older statement is logged, not linked); a revised piece still linked elsewhere links the new piece there too; new views come with rungs, dependencies and\\n     4\\tsuccessions; a waiting dependency is resolved when the chain's year is created; the set of views whose reading\\n     5\\tchanged is returned for the re-judging round.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     6\\timport dataclasses\\n     7\\timport json\\n     8\\timport re\\n     9\\timport time\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\tfrom . import identity, store\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t@dataclasses.dataclass\\n    15\\tclass Written:\\n    16\\t    changed_views: set\\n    17\\t    new_views: dict            # candidate id -> view_id\\n    18\\t    evidence_ids: dict         # handover evidence id -> evidence_id\\n    19\\t    notes: list\\n    20\\t    links: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)      # D694: the reading links committed, with their final labels\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\tdef _next_id(conn, table, column, prefix):\\n    24\\t    row = conn.execute(f'select {column} from {table} order by rowid desc limit 1').fetchone()\\n    25\\t    last = int(row[0][len(prefix):]) if row and row[0].startswith(prefix) and row[0][len(prefix):].isdigit() else 0\\n    26\\t    return f'{prefix}{last + 1}'\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tdef _store_piece(conn, e, seq, item):\\n    30\\t    evidence_id = _next_id(conn, 'evidence', 'evidence_id', 'e')\\n    31\\t    store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=e['quote'], one_line=e['one_line'], speaker=e['speaker'],\\n    32\\t                       original_who=e['original_who'], original_day=e['original_day'] or '', tier=e['tier'],   # D203: unknown stays unknown\\n    33\\t                       event_time=e['event_time'], seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'])\\n    34\\t    store.add_source(conn, evidence_id, item['input_id'], item['category'], item['publication_day'], e.get('location', ''), seq)\\n    35\\t    return evidence_id\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\tdef _create_view(conn, c, object_id, object_kind, seq, item, universe):\\n    39\\t    view_id = _next_id(conn, 'views', 'view_id', 'v')\\n    40\\t    # the year is stored in its one canonical spelling so that a waiting dependency's year joins it (D163 plan, period text)\\n    41\\t    year = universe.canonical_year(object_id, c['year']) if hasattr(universe, 'canonical_year') else c['year']\\n    42\\t    store.create_view(conn, view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=c['kind'], looks_at=c['looks_at'],\\n    43\\t                      question=c['question'], due_day=c['due_day'], year=year, rungs=c['rungs'], seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'],\\n    44\\t                      created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\\n    45\\t    if c.get('measure'):          # keyed candidates (extraction schema v4 and later) carry their key into the ledger\\n    46\\t        store.add_key(conn, view_id, c, seq)\\n    47\\t    return view_id\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\tdef resolve_waiting(conn, new_view_id, seq, changed):\\n    51\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A new view on a chain satisfies dependencies waiting for its year on that chain.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    52\\t    v = store.view(conn, new_view_id)\\n    53\\t    chain = {new_view_id}\\n    54\\t    frontier = [new_view_id]\\n    55\\t    while frontier:\\n    56\\t        current = frontier.pop()\\n    57\\t        for row in conn.execute('select succeeds from successions where view_id=?', (current,)):\\n    58\\t            if row['succeeds'] not in chain:\\n    59\\t                chain.add(row['succeeds'])\\n    60\\t                frontier.append(row['succeeds'])\\n    61\\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where wait_year=? and wait_chain_view_id is not null', (v['year'],)):\\n    62\\t        if dep['wait_chain_view_id'] in chain:\\n    63\\t            already = conn.execute('select 1 from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=?', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\\n    64\\t            if not already and not store.would_cycle(conn, dep['view_id'], new_view_id):\\n    65\\t                store.insert(conn, 'dependency_resolutions', dependency_id=dep['dependency_id'], resolved_to=new_view_id, reason='created', seq=seq)\\n    66\\t                changed.add(dep['view_id'])\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\tdef object_id_of(universe, candidate):\\n    70\\t    return universe.resolve(candidate['object']) or candidate['object']\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\tdef oriented_like(c, previous, notes):\\n    74\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"06-views: a successor's ladder keeps the predecessor's direction. A numeric ladder written the other way round (rung 1 the\\n    75\\t    lowest band where the predecessor's rung 1 is the highest) is the same ladder; it is stored reversed, rungs with their\\n    76\\t    labels and bounds, so positions mean the same along the chain. Undecidable pairs are stored as written.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    77\\t    from .matching import ladder_direction\\n    78\\t    before, after = (ladder_direction(previous) if previous else None), ladder_direction(c['rungs'])\\n    79\\t    if before is not None and after is not None and before != after:\\n    80\\t        notes.append(f'candidate {c[\\\"id\\\"]}: successor ladder reversed to the predecessor\\\\'s direction')\\n    81\\t        return dict(c, rungs=list(reversed(c['rungs'])))\\n    82\\t    return c\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\tTIER_RANK = {'fact': 3, 'party_statement': 3, 'third_party_view': 2, 'rumour': 1}\\n    86\\tISO_DAY = re.compile(r'^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$')\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\tdef revision_refused(incoming, old, new_day):\\n    90\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"06-views, the Replace row, read since D202 as a revision: a later account of the same matter by a party entitled to give one (a\\n    91\\t    speaker revises its own guidance or forecast, an official confirms or denies a report, the original source revises). Returns the\\n    92\\t    reason the revision is refused, or '' when it may be recorded: the incoming piece needs a stated day, a tier at least the stored\\n    93\\t    piece's (a view never revises a fact or a party's statement), and, when it is a third-party view or a rumour, the same party as the\\n    94\\t    stored piece. Nothing is retired either way; a refused revision is stored as one more piece.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    95\\t    from .. import vocabulary\\n    96\\t    if not old:\\n    97\\t        return ''\\n    98\\t    if not ISO_DAY.match(new_day or ''):\\n    99\\t        return 'no stated day'\\n   100\\t    new_tier, old_tier = vocabulary.canonical('tier', incoming.get('tier')), vocabulary.canonical('tier', old.get('tier'))\\n   101\\t    if TIER_RANK.get(new_tier, 0) < TIER_RANK.get(old_tier, 0):\\n   102\\t        return f'{new_tier} cannot revise {old_tier}'\\n   103\\t    if new_tier in ('third_party_view', 'rumour') \\\\\\n   104\\t            and (incoming.get('original_who') or '').strip().casefold() != (old.get('original_who') or '').strip().casefold():\\n   105\\t        return f'another party\\\\'s {old_tier.replace(\\\"_\\\", \\\" \\\")}'       # an official confirms or denies; the original source revises\\n   106\\t    return ''\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\tclass WriteConflict(ValueError):\\n   110\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The checked plan no longer fits the writable ledger; no partial write is retained.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   163\\t    progressed = conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 limit 1').fetchone() or \\\\\\n   164\\t        conn.execute('select 1 from days_completed limit 1').fetchone()\\n   165\\t    if progressed:\\n   166\\t        raise BaselineRefused('coverage start has passed in this ledger: the coverage-start reading runs only on a ledger that has processed nothing yet')\\n   167\\t    return 'run'\\n   168\\t\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\tdef run(conn, items_db, archive, cfg, *, ticker, coverage_start, transport=None, log=print):\\n   171\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reads, checks and writes the starting figures; returns the step's record (or None when the configuration has no baseline setting or the step\\n   172\\t    ran before). All model calls first (archived, so a rerun after a failure reuses them), then every record, link and the step row in one commit.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   173\\t    setting = getattr(cfg, 'baseline', None)\\n   174\\t    if setting is None:\\n   175\\t        return None\\n   176\\t    system, task = prompt(setting.prompt_version)\\n   177\\t    if guard(conn, ticker, coverage_start) == 'skip':\\n   178\\t        log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: done before, skipped')\\n   179\\t        return None\\n   180\\t    items = report_items(items_db, ticker, coverage_start)\\n   181\\t    seq = store.next_sequence(conn)\\n   182\\t    at = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\\n   183\\t    if not items:\\n   184\\t        record = {'changed': [], 'report': [], 'kept': 0, 'refused': [], 'empty': [], 'note': f'no earnings report of {ticker} before {coverage_start}'}\\n   185\\t        store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, 'none'), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record), coverage_start, at)\\n   186\\t        conn.commit()\\n   187\\t        return record\\n   188\\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, {'publication_day': items[0]['publication_day'], 'category': 'T1', 'object_identifiers': [{'value': ticker}]}, [ticker])\\n   189\\t    readings = []\\n   190\\t    for view in sorted(shown, key=lambda v: int(v['view_id'][1:]) if v['view_id'][1:].isdigit() else 0):\\n   191\\t        lines = placement.question_lines([view])\\n   192\\t        for item in items:\\n   193\\t            answer = model.call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user_message(lines, item, task), SCHEMA, SCHEMA_NAME, STEP, transport=transport)\\n   194\\t            readings.append((view['view_id'], item, check_figures(answer.data.get('figures', []), item['text_page'])))\\n   195\\t    records, changed, refused, empty, kept = {}, [], [], [], 0\\n   196\\t    for view_id, item, figures in readings:\\n   197\\t        if not figures:\\n   198\\t            empty.append([view_id, item['input_id']])\\n   199\\t        for f in figures:\\n   200\\t            if not f['kept']:\\n   201\\t                refused.append({'view_id': view_id, 'input_id': item['input_id'], 'quote': f['quote'][:300], 'value': f['value'],\\n   202\\t                                'reason': 'quote not in the report' if not f['in_report'] else ('no label' if not f['labelled'] else 'value not printed in the quote')})\\n   203\\t                continue\\n   204\\t            key = (item['input_id'], comparable(f['quote']))\\n   205\\t            if key not in records:\\n   206\\t                evidence_id = _next_id(conn, 'evidence', 'evidence_id', 'e')\\n   207\\t                store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=f['quote'], one_line=one_line_of(f), speaker=item['publisher'],\\n   208\\t                                   original_who=item['publisher'], original_day=item['publication_day'], tier='fact', event_time='', seq=seq,\\n   209\\t                                   input_id=item['input_id'])\\n   210\\t                store.add_source(conn, evidence_id, item['input_id'], 'T1', item['publication_day'], '', seq)\\n   211\\t                records[key] = evidence_id\\n   212\\t            if store.link(conn, records[key], view_id, seq) and view_id not in changed:\\n   213\\t                changed.append(view_id)\\n   214\\t            kept += 1\\n   215\\t    record = {'changed': changed, 'report': [item['input_id'] for item in items], 'kept': kept, 'records': len(records), 'refused': refused, 'empty': empty}\\n   216\\t    store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, items[0]['publication_day']), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False), coverage_start, at)\\n   217\\t    conn.commit()\\n   218\\t    log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: {len(items)} report items, {len(readings)} readings, {len(records)} records linked to {changed}, '\\n   219\\t        f'{len(refused)} figures refused')\\n   220\\t    return record\\n   115\\t    missing = sorted(o for o in (aliases or {}) if o not in counts)\\n   116\\t    return (f'Objects with open views as of {as_of} (object, kind, number of views): {covered}.'\\n   117\\t            + (f' Objects in the universe with no view yet: {\\\", \\\".join(missing)}.' if missing else ''))\\n   118\\t\\n   119\\t\\n   120\\tdef judged(ledger, view_id, as_of, detailed=False):\\n   121\\t    state = service.state_as_of(ledger, view_id, as_of)\\n   122\\t    if not state:\\n   123\\t        return None\\n   124\\t    rung = next((g for g in store.rungs_of(ledger, view_id) if g['position'] == state['position']), {})\\n   125\\t    result = {'position': state['position'], 'label': rung.get('label', '')}\\n   126\\t    if detailed:\\n   127\\t        result.update(condition=rung.get('condition', ''), day=state['judgement_day'], reasons=state['reasons'])\\n   128\\t    return result\\n   129\\t\\n   130\\t\\n   131\\tdef brief(ledger, results, as_of, detailed=False):\\n   132\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Candidate state at the requested date; analyst context is explicit and versioned by the caller.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   133\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(ledger, as_of)\\n   134\\t    records = []\\n   135\\t    for result in results:\\n   136\\t        record = {'view_id': result['view_id'], 'object': result['object'], 'looks_at': result['looks_at'],\\n   137\\t                  'judged': judged(ledger, result['view_id'], as_of, detailed)}\\n   138\\t        if detailed:\\n   139\\t            record['question'] = result['question']\\n   140\\t        records.append(record)\\n   141\\t    return records\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\tdef related_views(ledger, view_ids, as_of, exclude=()):\\n   145\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The given views' neighbours in the ledger's dependency graph, as of the day: what each depends on (upstream)\\n   146\\t    and what depends on it (downstream), with the judged position; `exclude` are views already on the card.\\n   215\\t    return out[:limit]\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\tdef read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\\n   219\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The idea card: idea, what the idea's own search found, the reading (typed parts, the candidates each got, the\\n   220\\t    views each maps to, the summary, the claim), the related views from the dependency graph, the evaluation, every\\n   221\\t    view's bundle, the days, the trace of searches, and all call costs. No recorded view → no model call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   222\\t    text = (text or '').strip()\\n   223\\t    if not text:\\n   224\\t        raise ValueError('an idea needs text')\\n   225\\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(ledger, as_of)\\n   226\\t    report = on_progress or (lambda stage: None)\\n   227\\t    report('search')\\n   228\\t    found = search.search(ledger, index, text, k, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed)\\n   229\\t    card = {'idea': {'text': text, 'as_of': as_of}, 'search': {'mode': found['mode'], 'candidates': [r['view_id'] for r in found['results'] or []]},\\n   230\\t            'reading': None, 'evaluation': None, 'related': [], 'views': [], 'days': bundle.days(ledger, as_of),\\n   231\\t            'no_recorded_view': found['results'] is None, 'cost': dict(NO_COST)}\\n   232\\t    if found['results'] is None:\\n   233\\t        return card\\n   234\\t    setting = cfg.idea\\n   235\\t    if setting is None:\\n   236\\t        raise config.ConfigError(f'config {cfg.version} has no idea setting')\\n   237\\t    decompose_prompt, map_prompt = prompts(setting)\\n   238\\t    started = time.time()\\n   239\\t    cost = dict(NO_COST)\\n   240\\t    cost['cached'] = True\\n   241\\t\\n   242\\t    def spend(answer):\\n   243\\t        cost['usd'] += answer.cost_usd\\n   244\\t        cost['input_tokens'] += answer.input_tokens\\n   245\\t        cost['output_tokens'] += answer.output_tokens\\n   246\\t        cost['turns'] += 1\\n   247\\t        cost['cached'] = cost['cached'] and answer.cached\\n   248\\t\\n   249\\t    # call 1: the parts\\n   250\\t    report('decompose')\\n   251\\t    user = f'Idea: {text}\\\\nDay: {as_of} (the library as judged on this day)\\\\n\\\\n{object_list(ledger, as_of, aliases)}'\\n   252\\t    made, slips = call_english(archive, cfg, setting, decompose_prompt, user, DECOMPOSE, 'idea_decompose', transport,\\n   253\\t                               lambda d: [f for p in d['parts'] for f in (p['looks_for'], p['period'])])\\n   254\\t    for answer in made:\\n   255\\t        spend(answer)\\n   256\\t    first = made[-1]\\n   257\\t    parts = [dict(p) for p in first.data['parts'][:MAX_PARTS]]\\n   258\\t    # the service: one search per part, the candidates each part got\\n   259\\t    report('retrieve')\\n   260\\t    detailed = setting.prompt_version == 'idea-v12'\\n   261\\t    idea_rows = brief(ledger, found['results'][:IDEA_ROWS], as_of, detailed)\\n   262\\t    trace, candidates, ranks = [], [], []\\n   263\\t    queries = [((part.get('query') or '').strip() or canonical_query(part, aliases), canonical_query(part, aliases)) for part in parts]\\n   264\\t    if semantic and found['mode'] == 'semantic':\\n   265\\t        search.warm_queries(index, [q for pair in queries for q in pair], embed)      # one embeddings round trip for every part instead of two per part\\n   266\\t    # a part's candidates: the service's canonical query and the model's own, interleaved (tried 2026-10-25 and dropped:\\n   267\\t    # the object's views ranked by the idea text alone lost the model's finds, gold direct right 17 → 15 of 19)\\n   268\\t    for i, (part, (query, own)) in enumerate(zip(parts, queries)):\\n   269\\t        hit = search.search(ledger, index, query, PER_PART, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed)\\n   270\\t        steady = search.search(ledger, index, own, PER_PART, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed) if own.lower() != query.lower() else hit\\n   271\\t        rows = brief(ledger, merged(steady['results'] or [], hit['results'] or [], PER_PART), as_of, detailed)\\n   272\\t        candidates.append(rows)\\n   273\\t        ranks.append({r['view_id']: n for n, r in enumerate(hit['results'] or [])})      # the part's own search order, the tie-break among the model's direct views\\n   274\\t        trace.append({'tool': 'search', 'part': i, 'query': query, 'canonical': own, 'returned': [r['view_id'] for r in rows]})\\n   275\\t    # call 2: the mapping\\n   276\\t    report('map')\\n   277\\t    map_schema, payload = CONTRACTS.get(setting.prompt_version, (MAP, full_payload))\\n   278\\t    user = payload(text, as_of, parts, candidates, idea_rows)\\n   279\\t    made, more = call_english(archive, cfg, setting, map_prompt, user, map_schema, 'idea_map', transport,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:50:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\")\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\"\\ndef conn(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\")]\\nname,p,ip=inputs[0]; c=conn(p); i=conn(ip)\\nfor row in i.execute(\\\\\\\"select input_id, publisher, title, substr(text,1,300) from items where input_id like '\\\\\\\\''extra:%'\\\\\\\\'' or input_id like '\\\\\\\\''truenorth:%'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\"):\\n print(tuple(row))\\nfor e in c.execute(\\\\\\\"select e.*,group_concat(view_id) as v from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) where created_from_input like '\\\\\\\\''truenorth:%'\\\\\\\\'' group by e.evidence_id limit 6\\\\\\\"):\\n print(e['\\\\\\\\''v'\\\\\\\\''],e['\\\\\\\\''one_line'\\\\\\\\''],e['\\\\\\\\''quote'\\\\\\\\''])\\nfor e in c.execute(\\\\\\\"select e.*, group_concat(view_id) as v from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) where evidence_id in ('\\\\\\\\''e2295'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''e5309'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''e5384'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''e5385'\\\\\\\\'') group by e.evidence_id\\\\\\\"):\\n print(e['\\\\\\\\''v'\\\\\\\\''],e['\\\\\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\\\\\''],e['\\\\\\\\''one_line'\\\\\\\\''],e['\\\\\\\\''quote'\\\\\\\\''],dict(i.execute(\\\\\\\"select input_id,title,source_uri from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\",(e['\\\\\\\\''created_from_input'\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()))\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# NVDA Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Sarah, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's Fourth Quarter Earnings Call. [Operator Instructions]. Toshiya Hari, you may begin your conference.\\\\n**Toshiya Hari:*\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-05-20', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\"# NVDA Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Sarah, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's First Quarter Earnings Call. All lines have been placed on mute to prevent any background noise. After the speakers'\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\"# NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Tiffany, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's second quarter earnings call. [Operator Instructions]. Toshiya Hari, you may begin your conference.\\\\n**Toshiya Hari\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:AMD:2026-08-04', 'Advanced Micro Devices', 'AMD Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# AMD Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Greetings, and welcome to the AMD Second Quarter 2026 Conference Call. [Operator Instructions] And please note that this conference is being recorded. I will now turn the conference over to Matt Ramsey, VP, Financial Strategy and IR. Thank you, Matt. You m')\\n('truenorth:transcript:AMZN:2026-07-30', 'Amazon', 'AMZN Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# AMZN Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Thank you for standing by. Good day, everyone, and welcome to the Amazon.com Quarter Two 2026 financial results teleconference. At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode. After the presentation, we will conduct a question-and-answer session')\\n('truenorth:transcript:ASML:2026-10-14', 'ASML Holding', 'ASML Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# ASML Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good day, and thank you for standing by. Welcome to the ASML 26 Third Quarter Financial Results Conference Call on 10/14/2026, After the speakers' introduction, there will be a question-and-answer session. To ask a question during the session, you will ne\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:AVGO:2026-09-02', 'Broadcom', 'AVGO Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# AVGO Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Welcome to Broadcom Inc.'s Third Quarter Fiscal Year 2026 Financial Results Conference Call. At this time, for opening remarks and introductions, I would like to turn the call over to Ji Yoo, Head of Investor Relations of Broadcom Inc. Please go ahead.\\\\n**\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:CRWV:2026-08-11', 'CoreWeave', 'CRWV Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# CRWV Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, everyone. Thank you for joining us, and welcome to CoreWeave's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Call. [Operator Instructions] I will now hand the conference over to CoreWeave. Please go ahead.\\\\n**Unknown Executive:** Thank you. Good afternoon, and welco\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:DELL:2026-09-01', 'Dell Technologies', 'DELL Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\"# DELL Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon, and welcome to the Fiscal Year 2027 Second Quarter Financial Results Conference Call for Dell Technologies Inc. I'd like to inform all participants this call is being recorded at the request of Dell Technologies. This broadcast is the copy\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:META:2026-07-29', 'Meta Platforms', 'META Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# META Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, and welcome to Meta's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Conference Call. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to Meta's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Conference Call. And this call will be recorded. Thank you very much. Chad Heaton, Meta's Vice\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:META:2026-10-21', 'Meta Platforms', 'META Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# META Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Krista, and I will be your conference operator. Today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to Meta's Third Quarter 26 Earnings Conference Call. All lines have been placed on mute to prevent any background noise. After\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:MSFT:2026-07-29', 'Microsoft', 'MSFT Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# MSFT Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Greetings, and welcome to the Microsoft Fiscal Year 2026 Fourth Quarter Earnings Conference Call. As a reminder, this conference is being recorded. It is now my pleasure to introduce Jonathan Neilson, Vice President of Investor Relations. Please go ahead.')\\n('truenorth:transcript:MU:2026-09-30', 'Micron Technology', 'MU Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# MU Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, everyone. Thank you for joining us, and welcome to Micron's Fourth Quarter Post-Earnings Analyst Call. [Operator Instructions] I will now hand the conference over to Satya Kumar, Corporate Vice President, Investor Relations and Treasury. Satya, pleas\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:ORCL:2026-09-10', 'Oracle', 'ORCL Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call', '# ORCL Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Good day, everyone, and welcome to the Oracle Corporation First quarter fiscal year 27 earnings call. Just a reminder that this call is being recorded. If you have a question today, please press 1 on your telephone keypad. Please limit yourself to 1 quest')\\n('truenorth:transcript:SMCI:2026-08-11', 'Super Micro Computer', 'SMCI Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# SMCI Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Operator:** Thank you for standing by. My name is Jen, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to the Super Micro Computer, Inc. Q4 FY '26 Business Update Call. With us today are Charles Liang, Founder, President a\\\")\\n('truenorth:transcript:TSM:2026-10-15', 'Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing', 'TSM Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\"# TSM Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\n**Jeff Su:** Good afternoon, everyone, and welcome to TSMC's third quarter 2026 earnings conference call. This is Jeff Su, TSMC's Director of Investor Relations and your host for today. TSMC is hosting our earnings conference call via live audio webcast through the comp\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa144-e165-7c82-9e62-eda545606513', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia Reportedly Moves to Backstop $250 Billion in OpenAI Data Center Financing, Michael Burry Says, 'Around and Around We Go'\\\", \\\"Nvidia Reportedly Moves to Backstop $250 Billion in OpenAI Data Center Financing, Michael Burry Says, 'Around and Around We Go'\\\\nNvidia is reportedly in talks to provide a $250 billion financing guarantee for OpenAI's data center project in Ohio, with Michael Burry and Ed Zitron raising concerns abou\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa1ad-b65a-70f3-8475-22532b009667', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Deepens South Korea AI Push With $1 Billion NAVER Investment', 'Nvidia Deepens South Korea AI Push With $1 Billion NAVER Investment\\\\nNVIDIA plans to invest $1 billion in NAVER by purchasing newly issued shares, deepening its AI push in South Korea with a focus on expanding AI datacenter infrastructure using Vera Rubin and Blackwell systems.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa5b7-4053-7212-a591-5ca748ead6bb', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Funds AI Frenzy: Timeline of its Circular Financing Deals ... So Far', 'Nvidia Funds AI Frenzy: Timeline of its Circular Financing Deals ... So Far\\\\nNvidia is in talks to finance a $250 billion data center for OpenAI, with potential total project costs exceeding $500 billion. This follows a pattern of Nvidia providing financing that recipients use to purchase Nvidia chip')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa833-9f24-7c73-853c-6b0a122a3f9a', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Employee Detained in Taiwan as Prosecutors Allege AI Chip Smuggling to China: Report', 'Nvidia Employee Detained in Taiwan as Prosecutors Allege AI Chip Smuggling to China: Report\\\\nTaiwanese prosecutors detained an Nvidia employee for allegedly falsifying documents to smuggle advanced AI chips to China via Super Micro servers. The case is part of a broader global crackdown involving U.S')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa914-c6dc-73a3-820a-7ad50cb9124f', 'benzinga.com', \\\"NVDA Down 6% in Two Days: What's Happening to Nvidia's Default Insurance Costs?\\\", \\\"NVDA Down 6% in Two Days: What's Happening to Nvidia's Default Insurance Costs?\\\\nNvidia's credit default swaps surged 14 basis points to a record high amid reports the company is in early talks to guarantee up to $250 billion in financing for OpenAI's data center project, raising concerns about balan\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa924-cc13-75d2-b8ba-2f591f30d0b4', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Corning's AI-Fueled Expectations Crush the Stock\\\", \\\"Corning's AI-Fueled Expectations Crush the Stock\\\\nCorning (GLW) reported Q2 earnings that beat estimates (EPS $0.78 vs $0.76, revenue $4.74B vs $4.61B) with strong optical growth (+32%) and AI deals with NVDA and AMZN. However, Q3 guidance was in line with expectations, leading to a ~20% share price \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa995-2c61-7c81-8d59-10fad4dba818', 'benzinga.com', 'Coherent, Lumentum, Ciena Stocks Fall After Corning Earnings Trigger Sector Selloff', 'Coherent, Lumentum, Ciena Stocks Fall After Corning Earnings Trigger Sector Selloff\\\\nCorning reported Q2 earnings beat (EPS $0.78 vs $0.76 est, revenue $4.74B vs $4.61B est) and in-line Q3 guidance, which triggered a sector selloff in optical/connectivity peers Coherent, Lumentum, and Ciena.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fcc91-2844-75f3-8908-cb6005710f67', 'benzinga.com', \\\"'Nvidia, Dell Back AI Cloud Startup Volta at $2.4 Billion Value' - Bloomberg\\\", \\\"'Nvidia, Dell Back AI Cloud Startup Volta at $2.4 Billion Value' - Bloomberg\\\\nNvidia and Dell have invested in AI cloud startup Volta at a $2.4 billion valuation, according to Bloomberg.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fce63-1014-7d81-a427-f420fc66466c', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Is Partnering With NVIDIA To Design The Starmind AI1 Satellite Compute Payload; Each Of The Starmind Satellites Will Include NVIDIA Rubin GPUs And Vera CPUs For Datacenter Class Space Compute', 'SpaceX Is Partnering With NVIDIA To Design The Starmind AI1 Satellite Compute Payload; Each Of The Starmind Satellites Will Include NVIDIA Rubin GPUs And Vera CPUs For Datacenter Class Space Compute\\\\nSpaceX and NVIDIA are partnering to design the Starmind AI1 satellite compute payload, with each sate')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fd0ad-ed87-72e2-84a6-7715fbe442bb', 'benzinga.com', 'Musk Praises Vera Rubin Platform on SpaceX Earnings Call, Nvidia Stock Climbs', \\\"Musk Praises Vera Rubin Platform on SpaceX Earnings Call, Nvidia Stock Climbs\\\\nElon Musk announced on SpaceX's earnings call that SpaceX will build exclusively on Nvidia, causing Nvidia shares to rise in extended trading.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fd1d9-555c-7d70-8a5e-0aae3fc3c088', 'benzinga.com', \\\"QUICK SPARK: SpaceX Goes All-In on Nvidia. Jim Cramer Thinks That's All Investors Need to Know.\\\", \\\"QUICK SPARK: SpaceX Goes All-In on Nvidia. Jim Cramer Thinks That's All Investors Need to Know.\\\\nElon Musk announced that SpaceX will use Nvidia GPUs exclusively, and JPMorgan expects SpaceX to receive a significant share of Nvidia's 2027 shipments, deepening their partnership.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fdc5e-9cb8-7a10-9005-45aa6a1c904a', 'benzinga.com', \\\"AMD Buys AI Chip Startup Taalas—Here's Why It Matters To NVDA Investors\\\", \\\"AMD Buys AI Chip Startup Taalas—Here's Why It Matters To NVDA Investors\\\\nAMD announced the acquisition of AI chip startup Taalas, which specializes in model-specific silicon for faster and cheaper inference. This deal intensifies competition with Nvidia in the AI inference market.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fdda6-6242-7230-94e0-3924ef57daba', 'benzinga.com', 'The AI Chip Trade Is Getting Bigger — and More Leveraged. Meet REX’s New 3X Bets', \\\"The AI Chip Trade Is Getting Bigger — and More Leveraged. Meet REX’s New 3X Bets\\\\nREX has launched new 3X leveraged semiconductor ETNs (SMHU and SMHD) to capitalize on AI-driven demand and volatility in the semiconductor sector. The article highlights record inflows into semiconductor ETFs, SMH's 60%\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fe6fe-191d-7ec3-b0ef-693423bd9cdf', 'benzinga.com', 'US-China AI War: Inside the Battle for Global Tech Dominance', \\\"US-China AI War: Inside the Battle for Global Tech Dominance\\\\nThe article covers the escalating US-China AI competition, highlighted by China's Moonshot AI releasing Kimi K3, which caused a 1.4% Nasdaq drop on July 17. The White House accused Moonshot of stealing US technology via distillation of Ant\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019feb0e-2d2e-73c1-90aa-7bd4f056e57f', 'benzinga.com', 'Taiwan Semiconductor’s Blockbuster Run Rolls On: July Revenue Surges 45%', 'Taiwan Semiconductor’s Blockbuster Run Rolls On: July Revenue Surges 45%\\\\nTaiwan Semiconductor reported July revenue of NT$467.58 billion, up 44.7% YoY and 5.6% MoM, with YTD revenue up 37% to NT$2.872 trillion. The company also raised its 2026 capex outlook to $60-64 billion and expects full-year sa')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fec2c-bac6-7fb0-9a7c-f8d0fe40a6b8', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Built the AI Brain, Now TSMC Wants to Give It Eyes', 'Nvidia Built the AI Brain, Now TSMC Wants to Give It Eyes\\\\nTSMC and Sony are planning a $6.3 billion joint venture for image sensors, positioning TSMC for growth in AI-driven robotics and autonomous vehicles. Production is expected to begin in 2029.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019feeea-b3ca-7b32-a8ca-2dc921d04f8c', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Says 'First Time' That Chips Have Become An Investable Asset Class as BlackRock, Blackstone and Others Join $500 Billion AI Push\\\", \\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Says 'First Time' That Chips Have Become An Investable Asset Class as BlackRock, Blackstone and Others Join $500 Billion AI Push\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang announced a new initiative with six Wall Street firms to raise $500 billion for AI infrastructure, positioning chips as an \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff091-ef1d-7bc3-a58f-44fb941939ef', 'benzinga.com', \\\"NVIDIA's Jensen Huang Says AI Isn’t Just Tech Anymore — It’s Infrastructure, and Wall Street Is Financing It\\\", \\\"NVIDIA's Jensen Huang Says AI Isn’t Just Tech Anymore — It’s Infrastructure, and Wall Street Is Financing It\\\\nNVIDIA is partnering with Wall Street firms including Goldman Sachs and BlackRock to unlock over $500 billion for AI infrastructure and GPU financing, positioning AI chips as long-lived, reve\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff3c2-b5c8-71a1-b9af-ca482478f643', 'benzinga.com', \\\"CoreWeave Stock Surges Nearly 16% After Earnings, Analyst Says Old Nvidia GPUs Can 'Still Generate Revenue Nearly a Decade Later'\\\", \\\"CoreWeave Stock Surges Nearly 16% After Earnings, Analyst Says Old Nvidia GPUs Can 'Still Generate Revenue Nearly a Decade Later'\\\\nCoreWeave reported Q2 revenue of $2.58B, beating estimates, with a narrower adjusted loss. The company highlighted a $104B backlog and provided Q3 guidance. Analysts comm\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff45c-6357-7620-a9b3-52bbdf427f74', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Jim Cramer Asks if Wall Street's 'Long Knives' for Nvidia Should Stay Sheathed as CoreWeave Powers Neocloud Optimism\\\", \\\"Jim Cramer Asks if Wall Street's 'Long Knives' for Nvidia Should Stay Sheathed as CoreWeave Powers Neocloud Optimism\\\\nCoreWeave reported Q2 earnings that beat expectations, with revenue of $2.58B vs $2.56B expected and a narrower adjusted loss of $1.03 vs $1.22 expected. The company raised full-year \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff593-4909-79e2-be2e-d62881553377', 'benzinga.com', \\\"FLY Stock Climbs Over 4% During Wednesday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\", \\\"FLY Stock Climbs Over 4% During Wednesday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\nFirefly Aerospace reported record Q2 revenue of $117.7 million, up 659% YoY, beating estimates, with adjusted loss of $0.42 per share better than expected. Growth driven by NASA, national security contracts, and Nvidia collaborat\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff6e8-5134-7f71-92d0-893bccacf954', 'benzinga.com', 'Lumentum Posts Solid Q4, Set To Hit $1.25B Revenue Target 3 Months Early', 'Lumentum Posts Solid Q4, Set To Hit $1.25B Revenue Target 3 Months Early\\\\nLumentum reported strong Q4 results with revenue surpassing $1 billion, up 190% YoY, and guided Q1 revenue to $1.25 billion, beating expectations and hitting its mid-term target a quarter early. Shares rose 14.89% to $942.75.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff6f8-3e38-7b11-bf8c-912b4b230c55', 'benzinga.com', 'Stock Market Today: Nasdaq 100 Rises on Strong AI Earnings, Benign Inflation', 'Stock Market Today: Nasdaq 100 Rises on Strong AI Earnings, Benign Inflation\\\\nAI infrastructure earnings lifted tech stocks and the Nasdaq 100, while a consensus-matched CPI print cooled yields and trimmed September Fed hike odds.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffb2c-4c8d-7de2-8521-9db4eef52e1d', 'benzinga.com', 'AMD’s 2027 Server Revenue Outlook Is Already 20% Bigger Than the Entire 2025 Market', 'AMD’s 2027 Server Revenue Outlook Is Already 20% Bigger Than the Entire 2025 Market\\\\nAMD outlined aggressive AI and server growth plans at its Technology Leadership Forum 2026, targeting over 80% server revenue growth in H2 2026 and at least 70% in 2027, backed by Helios customer commitments and clou')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffb7b-df23-7c93-856b-d0170706ac85', 'benzinga.com', 'IREN Jumps 10% as Microsoft Accepts First AI Data Center Under $9.7 Billion Deal', \\\"IREN Jumps 10% as Microsoft Accepts First AI Data Center Under $9.7 Billion Deal\\\\nIREN's stock jumped 10% after Microsoft accepted the first AI data center under a $9.7 billion deal, marking a key milestone in IREN's pivot from Bitcoin mining to AI infrastructure. The acceptance triggers monthly invo\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffbbe-d6ca-7be2-8c8f-9e7e4d922970', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Why Nvidia May Stand in the Way of Wall Street's Plans to Turn AI Compute Into a Commodity\\\", \\\"Why Nvidia May Stand in the Way of Wall Street's Plans to Turn AI Compute Into a Commodity\\\\nCME Group plans to launch futures contracts on Nvidia H100 and B200 compute, aiming to create a standardized commodity market for AI compute. However, Nvidia's dominance over supply and pricing may hinder the \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffbc5-319c-7d50-a059-bf7048fd499b', 'benzinga.com', 'IREN Hands Microsoft Its First AI Cloud Deployment', 'IREN Hands Microsoft Its First AI Cloud Deployment\\\\nIREN stock rose 6.92% after delivering Horizon 1, the first of four planned 50MW AI cloud deployments for Microsoft under a $9.7B five-year contract, and securing NVIDIA Exemplar Cloud status.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc1e-87c4-7453-87dd-1e713140ad2b', 'benzinga.com', 'AMD Prepares Record $5B Bond Sale to Fuel Massive AI Expansion', 'AMD Prepares Record $5B Bond Sale to Fuel Massive AI Expansion\\\\nAMD is preparing a record $5 billion bond sale across four tranches with maturities from three to ten years, to fund AI infrastructure expansion and refinance debt. The company has not finalized the offering size, which may change based ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc4d-37df-7b81-a1d2-1c72dc8c1936', 'benzinga.com', 'Nebius Says AI Compute Prices Jumped 15%, Signaling Strong Pricing Power', 'Nebius Says AI Compute Prices Jumped 15%, Signaling Strong Pricing Power\\\\nNebius Group reported that its first AI capacity auction cleared at a price 15% above its previous highest, indicating strong customer willingness to pay for scarce AI computing power. The auction, which involved access to Nvid')\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc6d-49db-73b0-9cfa-4689323d0ef9', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Dell Rallies 2% After Lenovo's AI Server Pipeline Hits $54 Billion, Fueling Nvidia Demand Optimism\\\", \\\"Dell Rallies 2% After Lenovo's AI Server Pipeline Hits $54 Billion, Fueling Nvidia Demand Optimism\\\\nLenovo reported record quarterly results with AI server pipeline surging 157% to $54 billion, reinforcing strong AI infrastructure demand. Dell shares rose 2.5% following the news, with Super Micro's b\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fff6a-bea9-70d0-b03b-666f5ebe7635', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia's Next-Gen Feynman AI Platform Is Ramping Up, Forcing TSMC to Race Ahead: Report\\\", \\\"Nvidia's Next-Gen Feynman AI Platform Is Ramping Up, Forcing TSMC to Race Ahead: Report\\\\nNvidia is reportedly accelerating development of its next-gen Feynman AI platform, pushing TSMC to ramp 2nm and advanced packaging capacity. The report highlights TSMC's expansion of SoIC and CoWoS capacity, with\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00033-bc19-70e2-b821-58d32fcbc3ef', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Says ‘Free AI’ Is Great For Chips — Jensen Huang’s Open-Source Bet Could Fuel GPU Demand', 'NVIDIA Says ‘Free AI’ Is Great For Chips — Jensen Huang’s Open-Source Bet Could Fuel GPU Demand\\\\nNVIDIA released Nemotron 3.5 Lightning, an open-source AI model, and introduced NeMo Switchyard software. CEO Jensen Huang advocates for open-source AI, linking it to increased hardware demand. The compan')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0014d-05a7-7222-b775-a09b01383fe1', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, Cathie Wood Strike Gold With Databricks' $190 Billion Valuation\\\", \\\"Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, Cathie Wood Strike Gold With Databricks' $190 Billion Valuation\\\\nDatabricks raised $5 billion in a new funding round led by Coatue, valuing the company at $190 billion, up from $43 billion in September 2023. Early investors including Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, and Cathie Wood's Ark I\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00da7-9c2f-7d51-b8fe-2cfe4e291576', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Harvard Reveals $2.2 Billion SpaceX Stake, Its Largest Public Equity Holding: University's Bet on Elon Musk-led Company Outshines Amazon and Nvidia\\\", \\\"Harvard Reveals $2.2 Billion SpaceX Stake, Its Largest Public Equity Holding: University's Bet on Elon Musk-led Company Outshines Amazon and Nvidia\\\\nHarvard Management Co. disclosed a $2.2 billion stake in SpaceX, its largest public equity holding, via a 13F filing. The stake, held as of June 30, rep\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00f11-b57d-7a80-b17d-df8968149e55', 'benzinga.com', 'Harvard Did Not Sell Its Bitcoin ETF Holdings in Q2, Discloses No New Ethereum ETF Stake', \\\"Harvard Did Not Sell Its Bitcoin ETF Holdings in Q2, Discloses No New Ethereum ETF Stake\\\\nHarvard University's 13F filing shows it held its Bitcoin ETF position steady in Q2, with 3.04 million shares of IBIT worth $101.35 million, while not adding any Ethereum ETF stake after liquidating it in Q1. Th\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00f37-8c51-7103-8efd-9138a4064dcc', 'benzinga.com', \\\"HIVE Stock Jumps After AI Cloud Deal - Here's Why\\\", \\\"HIVE Stock Jumps After AI Cloud Deal - Here's Why\\\\nHIVE Digital Technologies announced a five-year GPU cloud services agreement worth approximately $350 million with an investment-grade enterprise customer, expected to add roughly $70 million in annualized revenue. Shares rose about 8% in premarket t\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01023-a283-7851-8628-e75e38978be8', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA’s Ohio AI Megadeal: OpenAI, 8 GW of Compute and a $1.5 Billion SB Energy Bet', 'NVIDIA’s Ohio AI Megadeal: OpenAI, 8 GW of Compute and a $1.5 Billion SB Energy Bet\\\\nNVIDIA and SB Energy partner to build an 8 GW AI campus in Ohio for OpenAI, with NVIDIA investing $1.5B in SB Energy. NVIDIA is also reworking its financing structure to reduce its initial guarantee from $250B to les')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0107f-1189-7443-b708-93eaa30d391f', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Stock Is Everywhere: Google, Nvidia, AMD, Harvard Disclose Stakes', \\\"SpaceX Stock Is Everywhere: Google, Nvidia, AMD, Harvard Disclose Stakes\\\\nSpaceX's Nasdaq debut has made it one of the most widely disclosed names in Q2 13F filings, with major tech companies, hedge funds, and institutions revealing large positions. Alphabet disclosed a ~$94B stake, Nvidia ~$21B, AMD\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a010be-cc2c-7893-8cb4-60423f75a42a', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia-OpenAI Deal Isn't 'Circular Financing,' Says Jensen Huang, Sees $600B Compute Opportunity\\\", \\\"Nvidia-OpenAI Deal Isn't 'Circular Financing,' Says Jensen Huang, Sees $600B Compute Opportunity\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang refutes the 'circular financing' characterization of Nvidia's $1.5 billion investment in SB Energy for OpenAI's Ohio AI campus, framing it as securing infrastructure supply. He hi\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01128-ef8e-78f1-a21a-c6f1083651fc', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Stock Jumps After Multibillion-Dollar Stakes Revealed', \\\"SpaceX Stock Jumps After Multibillion-Dollar Stakes Revealed\\\\nSpaceX shares rose 4.17% to $145.84 after 13F filings revealed major institutional holdings, including Google's $94 billion stake, Nvidia's $21 billion stake, and AMD's first-ever $565.5 million position. Additional disclosures included Ha\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0146f-3bb8-7ab0-b435-a044470e2162', 'benzinga.com', 'Trump-Backed World Liberty Partners With Platform Offering Chinese AI Models Flagged by US: Report', 'Trump-Backed World Liberty Partners With Platform Offering Chinese AI Models Flagged by US: Report\\\\nWorld Liberty Financial, a Trump-backed crypto venture, has partnered with Hong Kong-based WorldClaw, which offers access to Chinese AI models including those from Alibaba and Baidu. The deal raises et')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01504-3aca-7e51-825a-668b8d4c0f00', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia: The Customer List Behind Fabrinet's AI Boom\\\", \\\"Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia: The Customer List Behind Fabrinet's AI Boom\\\\nFabrinet reported fiscal Q4 earnings, revealing that Cisco, Nvidia, Nokia, and Amazon each account for more than 10% of annual revenue, highlighting the company's diversified role in AI infrastructure. Management expressed \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0158a-423f-7292-afab-e5ffd66fc11d', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Meta Slide as Bond Yields Surge: Why Tech Stocks Are Getting Hit', 'Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Meta Slide as Bond Yields Surge: Why Tech Stocks Are Getting Hit\\\\nTech and AI stocks fell sharply as the 30-year Treasury yield hit its highest level since 2007, with the 10-year around 4.73%. The selloff was concentrated in high-growth tech names, with AMD down 5%, Broadcom an')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0158c-7740-71d1-9fbe-48cc70e8cb27', 'benzinga.com', 'Citadel Advisors and Millennium Boosted Fabrinet Stakes in Q2 as AI Demand Accelerated', 'Citadel Advisors and Millennium Boosted Fabrinet Stakes in Q2 as AI Demand Accelerated\\\\nCitadel and Millennium significantly increased their Fabrinet (FN) stakes in Q2 2026, as disclosed in 13F filings. Fabrinet reported record results with a diversified customer base (Cisco 20%, Nvidia 16%, Nokia 11')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a015a5-b9ad-7a43-8e70-33e3a0708c37', 'benzinga.com', 'Fabrinet Shares Tumble As Nvidia Datacom Weakness Overshadows Telecom Strength', 'Fabrinet Shares Tumble As Nvidia Datacom Weakness Overshadows Telecom Strength\\\\nFabrinet reported strong Q4 FY2026 results with revenue and EPS beating estimates, but shares fell 20% due to declining Nvidia datacom sales and concerns about competition. Analysts reaffirmed Buy ratings with high price ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01811-3d71-7632-97f2-de168b8b61ab', 'benzinga.com', 'Elon Musk Warns Nvidia-Backed $105 Billion Ohio Data Center for OpenAI Will Take ‘Much Longer’ to Come Online Than Expected', \\\"Elon Musk Warns Nvidia-Backed $105 Billion Ohio Data Center for OpenAI Will Take ‘Much Longer’ to Come Online Than Expected\\\\nElon Musk publicly doubted the timeline for Nvidia's up to $105 billion Ohio data center project for OpenAI, citing potential delays. The project involves Nvidia's SEC-filed co\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a018b9-104c-7151-b4b9-b0b3e469e202', 'benzinga.com', 'Cerebras Stock Takes a Hit as New AI Server Targets Nvidia With Giant Chips and Faster Chatbot Queries', 'Cerebras Stock Takes a Hit as New AI Server Targets Nvidia With Giant Chips and Faster Chatbot Queries\\\\nCerebras unveiled its CS-4 AI server to challenge Nvidia, but its stock fell 12.69% after revenue missed estimates. Core revenue grew 103% YoY, and guidance for Q3 was provided.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01942-08c8-7cb2-a8e0-e51c89430141', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s H200 Chips Are Flowing Into China Again: ByteDance, Tencent Get Around 10,000 Each, Report Says', \\\"Nvidia’s H200 Chips Are Flowing Into China Again: ByteDance, Tencent Get Around 10,000 Each, Report Says\\\\nChina has approved limited shipments of Nvidia's H200 AI chips to ByteDance and Tencent, with each receiving around 10,000 processors, signaling a cautious easing of restrictions. The approvals f\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01985-2c6d-7472-baed-885c49e6cfea', 'benzinga.com', 'SKHY Stock Rips 6% in Premarket on $29 Billion Buyback Plan', 'SKHY Stock Rips 6% in Premarket on $29 Billion Buyback Plan\\\\nSK Hynix announced a $29 billion (40 trillion won) treasury share buyback and cancellation plan, along with a commitment to return over 50% of cumulative free cash flow from 2025-2027 to shareholders. The stock rose 5.56% in premarket tradi')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01991-56de-70a2-93d2-88c96e4a3be6', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Supplier SK Hynix Rolls Out $29 Billion Buyback After AI Spending Fears Hammer Stock', 'NVIDIA Supplier SK Hynix Rolls Out $29 Billion Buyback After AI Spending Fears Hammer Stock\\\\nSK hynix stock rebounded 5% in premarket trading after announcing a $29 billion (40 trillion won) stock buyback plan and raising its shareholder return target to over 50% of free cash flow. The move follows a')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a019c8-0e5b-7df2-9fc6-8c4bdda6ea6a', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Jim Cramer Slams Data Center Reliance on Leveraged Retail-Driven SK Hynix, Samsung Stocks: 'Decided By Them, Not Us'\\\", \\\"Jim Cramer Slams Data Center Reliance on Leveraged Retail-Driven SK Hynix, Samsung Stocks: 'Decided By Them, Not Us'\\\\nSK Hynix announced a $29 billion (40 trillion won) share buyback and cancellation plan to support its stock amid AI demand concerns. Jim Cramer criticized the data center supply chain\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01a36-a4f7-7aa1-95d2-06b570e0b49b', 'benzinga.com', 'NVDA Rival Cerebras Unveils New AI System It Says Is Up to 30X Faster Than Nvidia GPUs', 'NVDA Rival Cerebras Unveils New AI System It Says Is Up to 30X Faster Than Nvidia GPUs\\\\nCerebras unveiled its new CS-4 AI inference system, claiming up to 30x faster inference than Nvidia GPUs, with speeds exceeding 4,400 tokens per second per user on GPT-OSS-120B. The first systems are expected onli')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01a75-17f5-7653-91cd-6bf3ab93c8c5', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Rival Marvell Surges After Google Strikes AI Chip Deal, Gets Option to Buy $12.2B Stake', 'Broadcom Rival Marvell Surges After Google Strikes AI Chip Deal, Gets Option to Buy $12.2B Stake\\\\nMarvell announced a sweeping custom AI chip agreement with Google, including a warrant for Google to buy nearly 59 million Marvell shares at $206.58 each, potentially worth $12.2 billion. The deal could ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01b00-8458-7af3-bf3b-4a72fc171264', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Investors Should Position For Humanoid Robot Boom—Here's A Picks-And-Shovels Play; First mRNA Cancer Vaccine Succeeds\\\", \\\"Investors Should Position For Humanoid Robot Boom—Here's A Picks-And-Shovels Play; First mRNA Cancer Vaccine Succeeds\\\\nThe article covers multiple market-moving events: Moderna and Merck's Phase 3 mRNA cancer vaccine success, US Treasury doubling buyback support for long bonds, SK Hynix's $28B buybac\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01bde-a23b-7e12-a2ae-20724c9385e9', 'benzinga.com', 'Samsung Tumbled Nearly 8% in Seoul Even as AI Demand Drives Chip Prices Up To 15%', \\\"Samsung Tumbled Nearly 8% in Seoul Even as AI Demand Drives Chip Prices Up To 15%\\\\nSamsung raised prices for advanced chipmaking services by up to 15% for new orders, driven by AI demand and full production lines. The move highlights pricing power in the semiconductor foundry market, even as Samsung'\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01f76-7671-74b1-b8ec-790d3f11f6d6', 'benzinga.com', 'CoreWeave Lands Multibillion-Dollar Hudson River Deal as Wall Street Races for Nvidia Chips', \\\"CoreWeave Lands Multibillion-Dollar Hudson River Deal as Wall Street Races for Nvidia Chips\\\\nCoreWeave has secured a multibillion-dollar, multiyear AI cloud deal with Hudson River Trading, providing access to Nvidia's Vera Rubin and B200 systems. This follows a $6 billion commitment from Jane Street \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01f84-eb78-7003-bf96-a3619f1d91b8', 'benzinga.com', \\\"A 10-Year Treasury Bond Now Pays More Than 118 Of America's Biggest Companies\\\", \\\"A 10-Year Treasury Bond Now Pays More Than 118 Of America's Biggest Companies\\\\nThe 10-year Treasury yield now exceeds the dividend yield of 118 S&P 500 mega-cap stocks, with only 3.85% of the index yielding more than the bond, the lowest since May 2007. This reflects rising long-term yields and low d\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a02009-f6f4-7421-a2b7-7cb042b79b24', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is SK Hynix Stock Surging on Thursday?', 'Why Is SK Hynix Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\nSK Hynix announced a 40 trillion won ($29 billion) share buyback and cancellation plan, plus expanded free cash flow return commitments, driving its stock up 4.25%.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023b9-2355-7e72-b586-582f54acafaf', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Steps up NVIDIA Challenge With Potential $100 Billion AI Financing Deal', 'Broadcom Steps up NVIDIA Challenge With Potential $100 Billion AI Financing Deal\\\\nBroadcom is exploring a massive up to $100 billion AI financing package with Apollo and Blackstone to fund custom AI chips for customers like Anthropic. The deal is in discussion stages, with talks ongoing and potential')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023de-e7e3-7de0-9166-b2db9f613441', 'benzinga.com', 'Waymo Unveils First Custom Robotaxi Chip With More Than 1,000 TOPS of AI Processing Power', \\\"Waymo Unveils First Custom Robotaxi Chip With More Than 1,000 TOPS of AI Processing Power\\\\nWaymo, Alphabet's autonomous driving unit, unveiled its first custom-designed robotaxi chip, a 5-nanometer ASIC with over 1,000 TOPS of AI processing power for real-time sensor data processing in its new Ojai v\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023eb-f2a1-7441-af46-75d8745b0856', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Looks to Strengthen AI Empire With Potential Rebellions Deal', \\\"NVIDIA Looks to Strengthen AI Empire With Potential Rebellions Deal\\\\nNVIDIA is in preliminary talks with South Korean AI chip startup Rebellions about a potential technical partnership, investment, or acquisition. The discussions are exploratory and may not result in a transaction. NVIDIA's stock ros\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a024c4-e685-77d0-bf65-9dd563950310', 'benzinga.com', 'Modine Stock Jumps After Report Names Google, Amazon as Data Center Cooling Customers', \\\"Modine Stock Jumps After Report Names Google, Amazon as Data Center Cooling Customers\\\\nModine shares rose after Hunterbrook Media reported that Google is the unnamed customer behind Modine's $4 billion cooling agreement, with additional pipeline from Amazon and others. The report also suggests Modine\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a031b6-72ce-7be2-8be9-79c2b5462e44', 'benzinga.com', 'Remember Hugging Face? The AI Hub Hit by an OpenAI Security Breach Is Reportedly Exploring a $13 Billion Sale', 'Remember Hugging Face? The AI Hub Hit by an OpenAI Security Breach Is Reportedly Exploring a $13 Billion Sale\\\\nHugging Face, an open-source AI platform, is reportedly exploring a potential sale that could value the company at $13 billion or more, nearly tripling its 2023 valuation of $4.5 billion. Th')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03201-1a85-7951-a679-fe5b82ffaa91', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Is Coming for OpenAI and DeepSeek With $6 Billion Poolside Deal to Build a Powerful Open-Weight AI Model: Report', \\\"Nvidia Is Coming for OpenAI and DeepSeek With $6 Billion Poolside Deal to Build a Powerful Open-Weight AI Model: Report\\\\nNvidia is acquiring Poolside's AI technology for $6 billion and investing $1 billion at a $12 billion pre-money valuation, with over 100 employees joining Nvidia to work on open-we\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a033ea-1b5c-7473-872f-43321e036056', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Dan Ives Says Nvidia's 15% AI Server Price Hike Is Bullish for Tech. Could Micron Be the Real Winner?\\\", \\\"Dan Ives Says Nvidia's 15% AI Server Price Hike Is Bullish for Tech. Could Micron Be the Real Winner?\\\\nNvidia has reportedly informed major customers of a more than 15% price increase for AI servers shipping in early 2027, driven by surging memory costs. Analyst Dan Ives views this as bullish for AI \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a034ac-c1ff-7d02-8611-b20b7f13f4f3', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceXAI Taps NVIDIA To Build Faster AI Agents', \\\"SpaceXAI Taps NVIDIA To Build Faster AI Agents\\\\nSpaceXAI, the AI division of SpaceX, announced a partnership with NVIDIA to deploy NVIDIA's Vera CPUs for agentic AI applications and expand Grok's infrastructure. The collaboration also includes plans to use NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform for orbital com\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a034c7-84d7-70f2-a481-cdffe4a12335', 'benzinga.com', 'Memory Stocks Slide as Trump Threatens 50% Tariffs on Canadian Autos, Steel in 2027: Stock Market Today', 'Memory Stocks Slide as Trump Threatens 50% Tariffs on Canadian Autos, Steel in 2027: Stock Market Today\\\\nUS equities mixed as Trump escalates trade war with Canada via 50% auto tariffs, memory stocks slide on Samsung disappointment, and Bitcoin rallies past $79k.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03501-58ad-7083-8bd7-84dd5c70a3a1', 'benzinga.com', \\\"EXCLUSIVE: How AI's $220 Billion Bond Boom Competes With the Treasury\\\", \\\"EXCLUSIVE: How AI's $220 Billion Bond Boom Competes With the Treasury\\\\nAI companies have issued $220B in debt this year, intensifying competition with Treasury supply and contributing to higher long-term yields. Treasury Secretary Bessent expanded buybacks, but analysts see limited impact. Commentary\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03541-98e7-73b3-8645-f8d14d349a52', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Magnificent 7 Built The AI Boom, 'Munificent Seven' Wants to Power It\\\", \\\"Magnificent 7 Built The AI Boom, 'Munificent Seven' Wants to Power It\\\\nHarbor Capital Advisors launched the Munificent Seven ETF (BBLS), an actively managed fund targeting seven major energy companies positioned to benefit from surging electricity demand driven by AI infrastructure growth. The fund b\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a036fc-ca3f-78e3-b3f3-1298008ebac0', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Trump Snapped Up SpaceX Shares 11 Days After $1.77 Trillion IPO: Here's What Else He Purchased\\\", \\\"Trump Snapped Up SpaceX Shares 11 Days After $1.77 Trillion IPO: Here's What Else He Purchased\\\\nPresident Trump disclosed buying up to $50,000 in SpaceX shares shortly after its record IPO, along with other stock trades, raising conflict-of-interest questions as his administration advances space poli\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03728-79db-7f72-bf5b-77c3603e7156', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Elizabeth Warren Says if Jensen Huang Has Time for $1 Million Mar-a-Lago Dinner, He Can 'Find Time to Testify' and Explain Nvidia Tech in Russian Drones\\\", \\\"Elizabeth Warren Says if Jensen Huang Has Time for $1 Million Mar-a-Lago Dinner, He Can 'Find Time to Testify' and Explain Nvidia Tech in Russian Drones\\\\nSenator Elizabeth Warren is pressuring Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang to testify before Congress after reports that Nvidia's Jetson Orin computers were fo\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03834-2bf3-7020-bc02-47ee8cb9acc9', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Manager Named ‘Key Figure’ in Alleged B300 GPU Smuggling to China, 8 Others Indicted in Taiwan Probe', 'Nvidia Manager Named ‘Key Figure’ in Alleged B300 GPU Smuggling to China, 8 Others Indicted in Taiwan Probe\\\\nTaiwanese prosecutors indicted nine individuals, including employees of Nvidia and Super Micro, for allegedly exporting prohibited B300 AI GPUs to China. 74 servers were successfully shipped v')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03a59-3dba-7cf2-bd65-23fdfaca9e2d', 'benzinga.com', 'Leveraged Single-Stock ETF Closures Went From 3 To 63 In A Year As Money Piles Into Nvidia Bets', 'Leveraged Single-Stock ETF Closures Went From 3 To 63 In A Year As Money Piles Into Nvidia Bets\\\\nThe leveraged ETF market is undergoing a shakeout in 2026, with record launches but widespread closures and asset concentration in top products like NVDL, SOXL, and SOXS. The article highlights the trend ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03c58-cf2c-75d0-93ca-9e5268d2acd9', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Jim Cramer Sees 'No Real Competitors' to Nvidia, Even as Sam Altman Says OpenAI 'Made a Chip and It Is Fast'\\\", \\\"Jim Cramer Sees 'No Real Competitors' to Nvidia, Even as Sam Altman Says OpenAI 'Made a Chip and It Is Fast'\\\\nOpenAI announced its first custom inference chip, Jalapeño, developed with Broadcom, claiming significant efficiency and latency improvements over Nvidia's GB200 and GB300 chips. The chip is \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03d04-0776-7890-a753-f3d09710ac24', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, Zoom Communications and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Wednesday', 'Nvidia, Zoom Communications and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Wednesday\\\\nStock futures mixed; Intuit and Zoom reported earnings with guidance misses, while Nvidia, Williams-Sonoma, and Smucker are set to report.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03d06-0e58-7a91-8aba-33273ad7929c', 'benzinga.com', 'Dow Gains for Third Session as Treasury Yields Fall: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear Index Remains in ‘Greed’ Zone', 'Dow Gains for Third Session as Treasury Yields Fall: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear Index Remains in ‘Greed’ Zone\\\\nU.S. stocks rose for a third session as Treasury yields fell, with the Dow gaining 160 points. The Fear & Greed Index improved to 58.6 (Greed zone). Economic data showed Case-Shiller ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03efa-9153-7cb0-80f4-b4451228c5a4', 'benzinga.com', 'Microsoft, Amazon, Google Court Kimi K3 Maker Despite Bessent Blacklist Threat', \\\"Microsoft, Amazon, Google Court Kimi K3 Maker Despite Bessent Blacklist Threat\\\\nMicrosoft, Amazon, and Google are in early talks with China's Moonshot AI for revenue-sharing deals on its Kimi K3 model, despite potential U.S. sanctions. The talks are preliminary and may not result in agreements.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03fd1-ae9d-7e13-9776-7330b4bfa9a1', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Q2 Highlights: Double Beat, Huang Says ‘AI Infrastructure Buildout is at Full Steam’', 'Nvidia Q2 Highlights: Double Beat, Huang Says ‘AI Infrastructure Buildout is at Full Steam’\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 FY2025 revenue of $96.22B (beat $92.18B estimate), EPS of $2.22 (beat $2.10), and issued Q3 guidance of $105.84B-$110.16B (above $104.20B estimate). Stock fell 1.8% after hours despite the ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04036-7a46-7443-81c2-92f2fb963c83', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia's Real Story Isn't the Beat — It's What Kress Said About 2028\\\", \\\"Nvidia's Real Story Isn't the Beat — It's What Kress Said About 2028\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 FY2025 results with revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, beating estimates. Q3 guidance of $108B also exceeded expectations. CFO Colette Kress projected 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, we\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a040ed-a9c7-79d3-9fd9-fd846051ce4e', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta and Abercrombie & Fitch: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\", \\\"Nvidia, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta and Abercrombie & Fitch: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\nMajor U.S. indices ended lower, but several stocks moved sharply after earnings. NVIDIA, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta, and Abercrombie & Fitch all reported quarterly results and guidance\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a040fd-f4a6-7712-bd68-81e25fa37749', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia Pops 4.7% After Hours as Earnings Blowout Lifts Dow Futures 180 Points: Jensen Huang Says, 'Compute is Revenue'\\\", \\\"Nvidia Pops 4.7% After Hours as Earnings Blowout Lifts Dow Futures 180 Points: Jensen Huang Says, 'Compute is Revenue'\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) beating estimates, and issued strong Q3 guidance. This drove a 4.7% after-hours stock surge and lifted Dow \\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04176-8c05-7572-b378-1cc02f718e32', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia Revenue Set to Increase 18X in 4 Years; Analyst Says 'Never in History' Has a Company Grown This Fast\\\", \\\"Nvidia Revenue Set to Increase 18X in 4 Years; Analyst Says 'Never in History' Has a Company Grown This Fast\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.22 billion (beat $92.11B estimate) and guided Q3 revenue to $108 billion, well above the $103.52B estimate. CEO Jensen Huang said 'compute is revenue' and de\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041a1-ba9c-7ba3-abd3-72bf56eaaac9', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Jim Cramer Says Nvidia Is 'Not Going to Stop Here' as Ross Gerber Sees NVDA Stock Hitting $450 as Analysts Dissect Q2 Earnings\\\", \\\"Jim Cramer Says Nvidia Is 'Not Going to Stop Here' as Ross Gerber Sees NVDA Stock Hitting $450 as Analysts Dissect Q2 Earnings\\\\nNvidia reported strong fiscal Q2 results with revenue of $96.2 billion (up 106% YoY) and net income up 126%, beating expectations. The company guided Q3 revenue to $105.84-$\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041ae-3a31-78c3-8301-58cd7c880d4c', 'benzinga.com', 'Dow Falls Over 100 Points Following PCE Inflation Data: Investor Sentiment Weakens, Fear & Greed Index Moves to ‘Neutral’ Zone', 'Dow Falls Over 100 Points Following PCE Inflation Data: Investor Sentiment Weakens, Fear & Greed Index Moves to ‘Neutral’ Zone\\\\nU.S. stocks fell on Wednesday following the release of PCE inflation data, which showed a slight miss versus expectations. The Dow dropped over 100 points, while the S&P 500')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041ea-18f9-79c2-8972-66fc116d16eb', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Agrees to Acquire Hugging Face For $12.9 Billion In One of Its Largest Acquisitions So Far As It Expands Control Of Open-Source AI Models: Report', 'Nvidia Agrees to Acquire Hugging Face For $12.9 Billion In One of Its Largest Acquisitions So Far As It Expands Control Of Open-Source AI Models: Report\\\\nNvidia has reportedly agreed to acquire Hugging Face, an open-source AI model repository, for $12.9 billion, according to The Information. This wou')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04202-1778-7571-a282-0434fb0e167a', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Not Taking OpenAI's 'Jalapeño' Chip Personally: 'Lots of Projects Get Started. Lots of Projects Get Canceled'\\\", \\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Not Taking OpenAI's 'Jalapeño' Chip Personally: 'Lots of Projects Get Started. Lots of Projects Get Canceled'\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang downplayed OpenAI's new Jalapeño AI inference chip, expressing confidence in Nvidia's technology and market position. The article also reports\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0420a-5ff5-73d3-8c15-c45c1a20269a', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia's Earnings Smash Estimates, but Crypto Bettors Aren't Buying a $250 Close by Month-End\\\", \\\"Nvidia's Earnings Smash Estimates, but Crypto Bettors Aren't Buying a $250 Close by Month-End\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.2B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, beating estimates. Despite this, Polymarket bettors give only 8% chance of NVDA closing above $250 by month-end, do\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04269-050c-75d0-9fcc-fe5964c7e63c', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia, Micron, Intel Climb in Thursday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\", \\\"Nvidia, Micron, Intel Climb in Thursday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 results with revenue of $96.22 billion (up 106% YoY) and issued robust guidance, projecting 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028 and Q3 guidance of $108 billion. CEO Jensen Huang cited strong AI demand and s\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04272-5523-78f2-b1a5-fa7892eae486', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Elon Musk's SPCX Now Accounts for 5% of Nvidia Revenue, Gene Munster Says: 'The Script Has Flipped'\\\", \\\"Elon Musk's SPCX Now Accounts for 5% of Nvidia Revenue, Gene Munster Says: 'The Script Has Flipped'\\\\nGene Munster estimates SpaceX now accounts for 5% of Nvidia's revenue, up from 3%, implying ~$4.8B in sales. Nvidia's Q2 revenue beat estimates at $96.22B, with data-center sales doubling. The company\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042a2-6b99-7830-98a6-eb851becdfec', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Jokes His Dinner Plans Can Double a Stock—His Track Record Says He’s Not Wrong', \\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Jokes His Dinner Plans Can Double a Stock—His Track Record Says He’s Not Wrong\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and Q3 guidance, beating estimates, while CEO Jensen Huang's comments on supply chain and quantum computing affected various tech stocks.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042a8-eb86-73a0-aae2-811f66931d0c', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Is Still the AI Bellwether—And Rivals Aren’t Close', 'NVIDIA Is Still the AI Bellwether—And Rivals Aren’t Close\\\\nNVIDIA reported Q2 revenue of $96.22B (beat $92.18B) and EPS of $2.22 (beat $2.10), with Q3 guidance of $105.84B-$110.16B. Stock rose 7.41% premarket. Analysts debate whether hypergrowth is slowing.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042d4-023b-77c0-96be-148af63414d4', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Jensen Huang Has a Message for NVDA Bears Betting on Open Models: 'Both Closed and Open Models Are Going to Succeed'\\\", \\\"Jensen Huang Has a Message for NVDA Bears Betting on Open Models: 'Both Closed and Open Models Are Going to Succeed'\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.22B, up 106% YoY, beating estimates, and issued Q3 guidance above $105B. CEO Jensen Huang commented on open vs closed AI models, stating both drive d\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0430d-c7d1-7e43-aa8f-0d77cb515e05', 'benzinga.com', \\\"NVDA Downplays 'Circular Financing' Concerns Days After Michael Burry Called it a Wall Street Stunt: 'We See it Differently'\\\", \\\"NVDA Downplays 'Circular Financing' Concerns Days After Michael Burry Called it a Wall Street Stunt: 'We See it Differently'\\\\nNvidia's management, including CEO Jensen Huang and CFO Colette Kress, defended the company's $500B AI infrastructure financing strategy against 'circular financing' criticism\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04321-f700-7952-9719-2714dfd8bc8e', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Surges 6% Premarket—These ETFs Are Amplifying the AI Trade', 'Nvidia Surges 6% Premarket—These ETFs Are Amplifying the AI Trade\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.2B (beat ~$92.3B estimate) and adjusted EPS of $2.22, beating forecasts. The company guided Q3 revenue to $105.8B-$110.1B. NVDA surged ~6-7% premarket, driving leveraged ETFs (NVDL, NVDU, NVDX, NVDB) ')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0433d-2134-7fa0-947c-96b174946f02', 'benzinga.com', 'Jim Cramer Has a Message for Nvidia Investors After the Earnings Blowout: ‘Don’t Let the Bears Deceive You’ Into Selling NVDA', 'Jim Cramer Has a Message for Nvidia Investors After the Earnings Blowout: ‘Don’t Let the Bears Deceive You’ Into Selling NVDA\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.22 billion (106% YoY), beating estimates, and data center revenue of $89.0 billion. CEO Jensen Huang declared AI deman')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0433e-ec5f-7fa1-babe-b79249d6211a', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA’s Biggest AI Bottleneck Isn’t Demand—It’s Memory', \\\"NVIDIA’s Biggest AI Bottleneck Isn’t Demand—It’s Memory\\\\nNVIDIA's earnings and growth outlook signal strong AI-driven memory demand and tight supply, boosting Micron and SK Hynix shares. Former NVIDIA executive Jeff Herbst expects elevated memory prices to persist due to capacity constraints and long\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04348-9566-76d2-8fd6-524a164bac08', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Nebius Group Stock Soaring Thursday?', 'Why Is Nebius Group Stock Soaring Thursday?\\\\nNebius (NBIS) stock surged 6.25% premarket after NVIDIA named it as the first customer for its upcoming Groq 3 LPX hardware, with volume shipments expected later this quarter. NVIDIA also reported strong Q2 earnings, beating estimates.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0436a-a84c-7102-ad4a-dd3d4603fad6', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s AI Boom Hits Its First Margin Wall: Memory Prices', \\\"Nvidia’s AI Boom Hits Its First Margin Wall: Memory Prices\\\\nNvidia's gross margins are expected to decline from 75% in Q2 to 71%-72% in Q4 due to soaring memory prices, marking the first major margin drop of the AI cycle. The company expects margins to recover in fiscal 2028 as it raises prices.\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04387-4280-7540-be99-8249f4bf5650', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Arm Stock Surging on Thursday?', \\\"Why Is Arm Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\nArm Holdings stock surged on Thursday following Nvidia's blowout Q2 earnings and strong AI infrastructure guidance, which sparked a broad semiconductor rally. Nvidia reported revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, both beating estimates, with data ce\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04387-b329-7ab3-a674-5c36786ec78e', 'benzinga.com', 'Nasdaq Surges 200 Points; Nvidia Posts Upbeat Q2 Results', 'Nasdaq Surges 200 Points; Nvidia Posts Upbeat Q2 Results\\\\nUS stocks traded mixed with Nasdaq up 200 points. Nvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and guidance. Economic data showed jobless claims below estimates. Several small-cap movers highlighted.')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0438c-1ece-7dd2-ace8-029431bfb8ae', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Bill Gates Wants to Hit the Brakes. Nvidia Is Financing AI's Next Sprint.\\\", \\\"Bill Gates Wants to Hit the Brakes. Nvidia Is Financing AI's Next Sprint.\\\\nNvidia's earnings call revealed extended payment terms for investment-grade customers and a broader AI financing strategy, while Bill Gates expressed support for slowing AI development. The article highlights Nvidia's shift fr\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a043ba-c7b7-7d53-93a1-f3514e628fa8', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Intel Stock Surging on Thursday?', \\\"Why Is Intel Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\nIntel stock surged on Thursday, driven by a semiconductor sector rally following Nvidia's strong Q2 earnings and reports of potential broad U.S. chip tariffs. Nvidia beat revenue and EPS estimates, while the Trump administration is considering new tariffs on s\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a043c3-cb28-7fe1-adc6-22436804bd31', 'benzinga.com', 'QUICK SPARK: Nvidia Stock Adds $370 Billion Market Value, A Whole Coca-Cola', 'QUICK SPARK: Nvidia Stock Adds $370 Billion Market Value, A Whole Coca-Cola\\\\nNvidia reported stronger-than-expected Q2 results, with revenue of $96.2 billion (up 106% YoY) and data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion. The company guided to ~70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the ~44% con')\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0442a-82a0-7a93-a210-0c1ac2e1811b', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia's Unusual Move Answers AI Trade’s Key Question; $40 Trillion US Debt Bomb Ticks; Key Fed Speech Awaited\\\", \\\"Nvidia's Unusual Move Answers AI Trade’s Key Question; $40 Trillion US Debt Bomb Ticks; Key Fed Speech Awaited\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and revenue, and provided forward guidance including Q3 revenue and FY28 growth, which is unusual for the company. The article also discusses the US debt,\\\")\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0446d-03f0-7c51-8156-1f3f635d4033', 'benzinga.com', \\\"Nvidia Stock 'Valuation Remains Conservative': Early 2028 Guidance Has Analysts Increasing Price Targets\\\", \\\"Nvidia Stock 'Valuation Remains Conservative': Early 2028 Guidance Has Analysts Increasing Price Targets\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 results that beat estimates and provided early fiscal 2028 revenue guidance of ~70% growth, which is well above