chingen  wheel    117 Nov 23 09:46 bunr9mxm5.output\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  wheel    116 Nov 23 09:42 b7cv8heu0.output\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  wheel    116 Nov 23 03:32 brylfmusa.output\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  wheel    419 Nov 23 03:28 bwtonlkf0.output\n40:def own_path(store_path):\n41-    \"\"\"(the store's real path, (device, inode)); a store with another hard link is refused.\"\"\"\n42-    real = os.path.realpath(store_path)\n43-    status = os.stat(real)\n44-    if status.st_nlink > 1:\n45-        raise LockRefused(f'{real} has {status.st_nlink} hard links: a store is opened only by its own path')\n46-    return real, (status.st_dev, status.st_ino)\n47-\n48-\n49-class Held:\n50-    \"\"\"A held lock: the store's real path and identity, the lock file's path, descriptor and inode.\"\"\"\n51-\n52-    def __init__(self, real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor):\n53-        self.real_path, self.identity, self.lock_path, self.descriptor = real_path, identity, lock_path, descriptor\n54-        self.lock_inode = os.fstat(descriptor).st_ino\n55-\n56-\n     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 1: built and checked at $0 (2026-11-23)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result.** Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md` revision 10, which was ready per council 74j after ten review rounds. It passes the\n     4\tdesign's tests, its mutants and the $0 release check on four stored stores. Nothing is committed, published or deployed. The POC is\n     5\tunchanged; no POC code imports the release module.\n     6\t\n     7\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n     8\t- Check: `release_check.py` (this folder). Output: `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/` (`results.json`, one package per store, the\n     9\t  dated leak packages and the closing copy).\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. No regressions, and one equivalent mutant\n    12\t\n    13\t- **Full suite:** 412 passed, the 23 new release tests included. `tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` is part of it.\n    14\t- **Mutants:** 21 of the design's 22 mutants fail the release tests on scratch copies (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`, no `__pycache__`);\n    15\t  the unmutated control passes.\n    16\t- **The 22nd, the canonical-day check removed, is equivalent on this repository's Python 3.10.10:** its `date.fromisoformat` already\n    17\t  refuses `20260825`, so no input can tell the two apart.\n    18\t- **Under Python 3.13, which accepts `20260825`,** the check is decisive. On a temporary copy of `old-1` with one later completed day:\n    19\t  - the real code refuses `20260825`;\n    20\t  - the mutant exports `v8` with 1,284 pieces of evidence, the latest source dated 2026-09-20, into a package dated 2026-08-25, where\n    21\t    the right package holds 621.\n    22\t\n    23\t## 2. The $0 release check (design §7)\n    24\t\n    25\t| Store | Bound | Number / event / Yes-No | Evidence | Fields compared | Data bytes (library) | Seconds (library) |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
