{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\breplacements\\\\b' src/hivemind/views/store.py src/hivemind/views/writing.py | head -35; rg -n 'replace' docs/prd/06-views.md | head -16; rg -n 'def add_(evidence|source)|def create_view' -A9 src/hivemind/views/store.py; /usr/bin/python3 -V; ls -d /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/* /opt/homebrew/Cellar/python* 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/views/store.py:2:replacements, dependencies, successions, match records, processing steps and the review pool; a trigram\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:22:    'replacements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',   # history: written before D202, read as before\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:374:    insert(conn, 'replacements', old_evidence_id=old_id, new_evidence_id=new_id, said_day=said_day, seq=seq)\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:410:    return bool(conn.execute('select 1 from replacements where old_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone())\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:414:    row = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id from replacements where new_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\n12:A thesis records an investment question and its evidence. A date, ladder and other research details are conditional on the information available; missing details can be researched later. Evidence moves its state when it can be judged. Search then compare candidates with existing theses to merge, continue, create or skip; compare evidence within its thesis to repeat, replace or add. Extra source references alone do not trigger rejudgement. Extraction determines group associations; the writer preserves them after resolving final thesis IDs under the [grouping contract](#research-groups-associate-during-extraction).\n133:- Rejudge an open thesis when its inputs change: new evidence, replacement, a new link to existing evidence, a dependency declaring a changed conclusion, or (for an asset thesis) a theme thesis declaring one. Additional source references alone do not count. Binding an awaited A or moving to its successor also changes B's inputs. Closed theses do not update. A memo-derived thesis is first judged when evidence first links to it; before that, it and its dependants see “not yet judged”.\n152:| Decision | Existing identity or part, succession, new thesis or skip | Repeat, replace or new evidence |\n168:  ↓ 4 Match (Model): The matcher does not read the original item. Jev answers, with a score, each candidate's relation to every thesis on its list (shown with its subject, question, focus, ladder, due date and open/closed state) and each piece of evidence's relation to every stored piece on its list under each linked thesis; code turns the answers into the destinations below and owns identity on typed keys (D155, D169, D197). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own subject and measure, the collision judge, one generative call, answers the analyst's question for those theses under D248's test, and its verdict replaces Jev's (D190, D258). Jev is not asked for dependencies. Evidence linked to candidates waits for their destinations, then searches all linked existing theses together and is compared once more. Evidence linked only to new theses is new evidence.\n170:  ↓ 6 Write to the library (Code): Resolve extraction's group associations to final theses and save them in this step. Each subject has its own writing queue; write theme theses before asset theses. Save new theses with their dependency edges. Store every incoming piece once, as its own record with all its links (D204): a repeat also records the pair as the same claim; a replacement is linked wherever the piece it revises is linked and the pair is recorded as a revision, ordered by when each statement was made, both in force (D202); an older statement arriving later is stored and linked as one more piece, with no revision recorded. The writer retires nothing. If compared data changes before writing, repeat matching only for the affected part.\n245:  ↓ 1 Jev and the collision judge (Model): Jev answers under Config's matching setting (D169); for a candidate whose list holds a thesis of its own subject and measure, the collision judge, a generative model under Config's collision setting, answers for those theses and its verdict replaces Jev's (D190, D258)\n263:| Decision | Each candidate's destination and reason; new-thesis dependencies and directions; evidence repeat/replacement/new decisions; validation results and refusal reasons |\n318:- One queue writes each thesis: the theme's queue for theme theses; the company, cryptocurrency or commodity queue for asset theses. Within an item, write themes before assets. Rejudgement order follows dependencies under the round rule. Other queues send requests, such as dependency changes or replacement links, to the owning queue with the item's sequence number.\n347:- Classify every evidence comparison as repeat, replace or new. A repeat is stored as its own piece with the pair recorded as the same claim (D204); a replace is stored beside the old piece as a revision, both in force (D202); every new link to an open thesis queues it for the day's round.\n396:- Associate by business process, across companies and industries, not merely by company. A customer deployment explicitly using Rubin can join Rubin; NVIDIA PC chips cannot join just because they share a company. OpenAI deployment cannot join an SK-specific group merely because both involve Rubin. A group does not replace a research-universe theme.\n400:- Groups do not copy evidence. Read sources through members' real evidence links, filtered by the requested sequence and excluding evidence a legacy replacement record had retired by then (no new one is written, D202). No link means no evidence. A new member or an existing thesis change flag updates its groups. A repeated quote is stored as its own piece with the pair recorded (D204) and updates a group only through its thesis's change flag. Evidence-only articles update existing memberships without inventing theses or groups.\n83:def create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\n84-    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\n85-           question=question, due_day=due_day, year=year, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id, created_at=created_at)\n86-    for position, rung in enumerate(rungs, start=1):\n87-        insert(conn, 'rungs', view_id=view_id, position=position, label=rung['label'], condition=rung['condition'], lo=rung.get('lo'), hi=rung.get('hi'))\n88-    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\n89-    conn.execute('insert into views_fts (view_id, text) values (?, ?)', (view_id, f'{object_id} {looks_at} {question}'))\n90-\n91-\n92-def view(conn, view_id):\n--\n355:def add_evidence(conn, *, evidence_id, quote, one_line, speaker, original_who, original_day, tier, event_time, seq, input_id):\n356-    insert(conn, 'evidence', evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=quote, one_line=one_line, speaker=speaker, original_who=original_who,\n357-           original_day=original_day, tier=tier, event_time=event_time, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id)\n358-\n359-\n360:def add_source(conn, evidence_id, input_id, category, publication_day, location, seq):\n361-    insert(conn, 'evidence_sources', evidence_id=evidence_id, input_id=input_id, category=category, publication_day=publication_day, location=location, seq=seq)\n362-\n363-\n364-def link(conn, evidence_id, view_id, seq):\n365-    exists = conn.execute('select 1 from evidence_links where evidence_id=? and view_id=?', (evidence_id, view_id)).fetchone()\n366-    if not exists:\n367-        insert(conn, 'evidence_links', evidence_id=evidence_id, view_id=view_id, seq=seq)\n368-        return True\n369-    return False\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-oid6mtpN' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 10:43:25.311 xcodebuild[35332:76326561]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 10:43:25.495 xcodebuild[35332:76326560] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-xCzpwAVG' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 10:43:25.889 xcodebuild[35341:76326627]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 10:43:26.009 xcodebuild[35341:76326625] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nPython 3.9.6\nzsh:1: no matches found: /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/*\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
