{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '216,258p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '351,376p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74j.md | head -25; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '438,461p'\"","aggregated_output":"   216\t    return result\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\tdef thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\n   220\t    \"\"\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\"\"\"\n   221\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   222\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n   226\t    \"\"\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\"\"\"\n   227\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   228\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n   229\t        if not as_of:\n   230\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\n   231\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   232\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\n   233\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\n   234\t        if not view_ids:\n   235\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\n   236\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\t# ---------- evidence ----------\n   354\t\n   355\tdef add_evidence(conn, *, evidence_id, quote, one_line, speaker, original_who, original_day, tier, event_time, seq, input_id):\n   356\t    insert(conn, 'evidence', evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=quote, one_line=one_line, speaker=speaker, original_who=original_who,\n   357\t           original_day=original_day, tier=tier, event_time=event_time, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id)\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\tdef add_source(conn, evidence_id, input_id, category, publication_day, location, seq):\n   361\t    insert(conn, 'evidence_sources', evidence_id=evidence_id, input_id=input_id, category=category, publication_day=publication_day, location=location, seq=seq)\n   362\t\n   363\t\n   364\tdef link(conn, evidence_id, view_id, seq):\n   365\t    exists = conn.execute('select 1 from evidence_links where evidence_id=? and view_id=?', (evidence_id, view_id)).fetchone()\n   366\t    if not exists:\n   367\t        insert(conn, 'evidence_links', evidence_id=evidence_id, view_id=view_id, seq=seq)\n   368\t        return True\n   369\t    return False\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\tdef replace(conn, old_id, new_id, said_day, seq):\n   373\t    \"\"\"Retires old_id (history before D202; kept for the readers and tests of stored ledgers, no longer called by the writer).\"\"\"\n   374\t    insert(conn, 'replacements', old_evidence_id=old_id, new_evidence_id=new_id, said_day=said_day, seq=seq)\n   375\t\n   376\t\n     1\t**Ready to build slice 1.** The 74i finding is closed. I found no other serious blocker in revision 10.\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **`check` now has a defined outcome for the missing case.** If the package passes but creating the temporary report file raises `PermissionError`, `check` prints the pass and the write error, then exits 2. Test 21 requires all three. The same exit rule covers any failure before the report link succeeds. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:68) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:214) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:385](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:385)\n     4\t2. **The package checks are specific enough to implement.** I verified the stored example used for acceptance. Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate and the system’s own “About $390 billion” forecast are both present in `old-1`. The design requires the first to survive export and requires the checker to reject the second if it is substituted into Morningstar’s summary. The builder must run that check before publishing the package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:154](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:154) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:437](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:437)   438\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n   439\t   - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\n   440\t   - the genuine analyst \"$390 billion\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\n   441\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n   442\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n   443\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\n   444\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n   445\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\n   446\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \"around $1 trillion\" text and j865's band text are absent.\n   447\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\n   448\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n   449\t   rung N <label>\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\n   450\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\n   451\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\n   452\t   - rung labels and conditions;\n   453\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\n   454\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\n   455\t   - switch reasons.\n   456\t\n   457\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   458\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   459\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   460\t\n   461\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
