'\\\\'');print('\\\\''before'\\\\'',d['\\\\''questions'\\\\''][0])\nstore.insert(v,'\\\\''view_keys'\\\\'',view_id='\\\\''v1'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''event'\\\\'',seq=2)\nd=release.release_export(v,i,'\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\'');print('\\\\''after'\\\\'',d['\\\\''questions'\\\\''][0],'\\\\''check='\\\\'',release.check_origins(v,i,d,'\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\''))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src /Users/lchingen/.pyenv/versions/3.10.10/bin/python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,collections,hashlib,sys,runpy\nfrom hivemind import release\nrc=runpy.run_path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py'\\\\'')\nbase=Path('\\\\''poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23'\\\\'')\nres=json.loads((base/'\\\\''results.json'\\\\'').read_bytes())\ndef ro(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef walk(v):\n if isinstance(v,dict):\n  for x in v.values(): yield from walk(x)\n elif isinstance(v,list):\n  for x in v: yield from walk(x)\n elif isinstance(v,str): yield v\nfrom hivemind.views import store\nv=store.open_db('\\\\'':memory:'\\\\'')\ni=sqlite3.connect('\\\\'':memory:'\\\\''); i.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\nfor n,day in enumerate(['\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-08-25'\\\\''],1):\n store.insert(v,'\\\\''processing_steps'\\\\'',input_id=str(n),sequence_no=n,step='\\\\''handed_over'\\\\'',result='\\\\''ok'\\\\'',publication_day=day)\n store.insert(v,'\\\\''days_completed'\\\\'',day=day,seq=n)\nstore.create_view(v,view_id='\\\\''v1'\\\\'',object_id='\\\\''NVDA'\\\\'',object_kind='\\\\''company'\\\\'',kind='\\\\''asset'\\\\'',looks_at='\\\\''Revenue'\\\\'',question='\\\\''What is revenue?'\\\\'',due_day='\\\\''2026-12-31'\\\\'',year='\\\\''2026'\\\\'',rungs=[{'\\\\''label'\\\\'':'\\\\''Above the estimate'\\\\'','\\\\''condition'\\\\'':'\\\\''Above'\\\\''},{'\\\\''label'\\\\'':'\\\\''Below the estimate'\\\\'','\\\\''condition'\\\\'':'\\\\''Below'\\\\''}],seq=1,input_id='\\\\''1'\\\\'',created_at='\\\\''2026-08-24T00:00:00'\\\\'')\nstore.insert(v,'\\\\''judgements'\\\\'',view_id='\\\\''v1'\\\\'',publication_day='\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\'',seq=1,rung=1)\nd=release.release_export(v,i,'\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\'');print('\\\\''before'\\\\'',d['\\\\''questions'\\\\''][0])\nstore.insert(v,'\\\\''view_keys'\\\\'',view_id='\\\\''v1'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''event'\\\\'',seq=2)\nd=release.release_export(v,i,'\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\'');print('\\\\''after'\\\\'',d['\\\\''questions'\\\\''][0],'\\\\''check='\\\\'',release.check_origins(v,i,d,'\\\\''2026-08-24'\\\\''))'\"","aggregated_output":"before {'id': 'v1', 'question': 'What is revenue?', 'open': True, 'class': 'number', 'forecast': 'Forecast unavailable', 'evidence': []}\nafter {'id': 'v1', 'question': 'What is revenue?', 'open': True, 'class': 'event', 'answers': ['Above the estimate', 'Below the estimate'], 'answer': 'Above the estimate', 'evidence': []} check= 10\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: slice 1 is not accepted.** All four saved packages passed my read-only comparison with their stores. I also reproduced both refusals of the substituted $390 billion forecast. The release still accepts a value revision 10 forbids, and I reproduced a historical case where the exporter and checker agree on an answer that should have been withheld. [Saved acceptance results:10079](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10079)\n\n### 1. Design and leaks\n\n| Finding | Evidence and consequence |\n|---|---|\n| **A later classification can expose an earlier forecast.** | In memory, an August 24 question initially exported “Forecast unavailable.” After adding an event key dated August 25, the **same August 24 export** showed “Above the estimate,” and the origin check passed. Both paths use a key lookup that ignores its sequence. The normal writer creates the key with the question, and I found zero sequence mismatches in the four stores. The exposure applies to a snapshot that breaks that convention. [Key lookup:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:81) · [Origin check:289](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:289) · [Writer:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:42) |\n| **Ten required text fields accept `null`.** | Revision 10 requires strings for all six evidence text fields and all four source fields. On an in-memory copy of `old-1`, a visible evidence record with a null summary passed both export and origin checking. This is a package-contract failure. I found no such null in the four saved packages. [Design:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [Type check:170](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:170) · [Affected fields:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:210) |\n| **`check` can verify different bytes from the ones it hashes or reports.** | It checks file type by pathname, reads the data for its hash, then reopens it for parsing. The command opens it a third time for the report. If an existing package changes during verification, the hash, origin comparison, and reported date can describe different contents. The four stored packages were stable. [Package reads:400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:400) · [Report read:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:86) |\n| **Both commands can open a different database from the path named in the report.** | The release passes paths to an opener that inserts the literal filename into a SQLite URI without escaping it. I verified that SQLite decodes `%2D` in a directory name to `-`. If both literal paths exist, the filesystem check can inspect one database while export and origin checking read the other. The four recorded input paths do not have this ambiguity. [Command:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:51) · [Filesystem check:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40) · [SQLite open:229](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:229) |\n\nThere are also command and diagnostic departures with no observed forecast exposure. On a report-write failure, `check` prints only counts, so the user loses the date, unresolved list, size, and timings that revision 10 says it prints. Timings use the adjustable wall clock. An export-side missing-item error omits the evidence ID, and a changed summary is reported by list position instead of evidence ID. The direct visibility test and the separate required item lookup implement the specified selection and missing-item refusal on a stable snapshot. [Command contract:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:213) · [Printed result:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:98) · [Timer:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:48) · [Item error:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:116) · [Observed summary error:10104](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10104)\n\n### 2. Tests and mutants\n\nThe recorded full-suite run did pass 412 tests. I reviewed all 23 release tests. Several assertions can pass after the behavior they claim to protect has been removed. [Suite output:6](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bt1qa93h2.output:6)\n\n- **The staging-ownership test supplies the behavior it claims to prove.** Its instrumentation inserts `staged = None` itself. The mutant removes the exact text the instrumentation needs to find, so setup can fail before the marker is created. This leaves the claimed marker-survival proof vacuous against its designated mutant. [Test:548](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:548) · [Edit precondition:468](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:468) · [Mutant:38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:38)\n- **The missing-item test damages two things.** It removes the source and the entire `e2` record. A checker that silently skips a missing source still expects `e2` with an empty source list, so it refuses this package for an independent reason. The mutant fails the expected-message assertion, but the design explicitly requires a pair the faulty checker *accepts*. [Test:345](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:345) · [Checker:245](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:245) · [Design:365](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:365)\n- **Three other protections lack a decisive assertion.** Test 1 calls `check_export` again after export, so it cannot detect removal of the writer’s self-check. Test 2 omits the selected label “Bullish” and the label “Bearish” from its forbidden list. Test 9 changes a stored summary and accepts any refusal, so origin checking still makes it pass if hash verification is removed. [Test 1:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) · [Test 2:191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:191) · [Test 9:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:280)\n- **“21 of 22 caught” counts failing processes.** The scratch copies exclude bytecode and use their own source path. The runner nevertheless continues after a failed control and counts every nonzero pytest exit, including setup errors. Its “sets” mutant only deduplicates questions while preserving order. The date exception is supported independently: on Python 3.13 I reproduced 621 pieces for August 25 and 1,284 through September 20 with the compact-date mutant. [Mutant edits:25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:25) · [Environment and counting:44](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:44) · [Date result:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:16)\n\n### 3. The $0 result\n\nI reproduced the reported class, evidence, source, and field-comparison counts for all four default packages. The byte and time ratios follow from the saved numbers. The closing switch also worked: `v8` was closed and its full closing reason was absent. Three claims exceed what the check established. [Store results:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:3) · [Closing result:10140](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10140)\n\n- **“Bullish” appears in six `v8` fields in the closing package.** Five are source titles and one is the genuine `e1865` quote. The script tested whole-field equality. The report claimed absence from every field. These six occurrences are permitted source wording. [Comparison:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:226) · [Claim:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60) · [Six field locations:140](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:140)\n- **The diagnostic search was incomplete.** Across the four packages it skipped 28,170 decoded data strings plus all 16 manifest strings. It also skipped event conditions and the stored switch reason `created`, which occurs in 81 actual package fields. Revision 10 calls for reading every hit. The report records a sample of 14 out of 1,245 reported matches. [Field selection:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:49) · [Stored-string selection:76](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:76) · [Requirement:451](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:451) · [Sample:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:81)\n- **The dated check never tests j865’s selected-band phrase.** It searches for the full explanation and for j799’s “around $1 trillion.” A shortened copy containing only j865’s “rung 4” would escape that check. I searched the saved August 28 data separately and found zero occurrences of “rung 4.” The script also records failed acceptance comparisons and exceeded budgets as values in JSON without making them fail the command. [Required dated check:445](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:445) · [Actual comparison:190](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:190) · [Budget handling:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:143) · [Command completion:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:227)\n\nThe four saved packages support the narrower conclusion that their forecasts were withheld and their permitted content matched the named stores. The historical classification case, accepted nulls, and verification gaps prevent accepting slice 1 as specified."}}
